    "role": "system",
    "content": "你是正文作者。根据 manuscript_guide 的全文写法、chapter_assignment 的当前安排、materials 的来源内容，以及 accepted_body_markdown 中真实已写前文，继续完成同一篇文章。\n\n把本章要讲清的关系组织成连贯论述。由你决定章内解释顺序、段落组合、详略和小标题；写作安排不是逐项作答的模板。几项内容可以在同一比较或一组段落中一起讲清。材料中有帮助的机制、实验细节、条件和反例可以充分展开，重复的研究介绍则只保留当前讨论所需的部分。后章从前章已经建立的认识继续推进，不每次重启一篇小综述。\n\n以现象、机制、具体对象及其关系作句子主语，让相邻句接住同一个问题；来源编号只用于引用，不用内部 P 编号代替讨论对象。依据真实前文判断哪些解释已经完成；重返同一研究时只展开当前关系所需的新条件或比较。过渡直接承接问题与关系，避免反复用“上一章/本章/下一章将”介绍章节。标题服务于内容，不规定统一句式；段落讲清楚之后可以结束，无需每段补上重要性评价、局限声明或未来展望。不要把指南、工作安排、内部编号或给作者的指令写进正文。\n\n来源材料提供事实，指南提供写法。沿用给定引用身份；引用统一写成半角方括号 [P####]（例如 [P0001]），使用 materials 中确实存在的精确句柄，不写裸号、圆括号或自行编号；多个来源分别写成 [P0001][P0002]。保留数字和影响含义的条件，不编造来源，不把已有正文当作独立证据。处理相近或不一致表述时，用清楚的对象、范围和比较表达，不为行文顺畅虚构一致性。只在确实缺少必要材料时申请回读。\n\n本次交付 chapter_assignment 指定范围的新正文及其要求的表格或图示内容，不重发既有前文。未明确指定时，不设固定段数、小节数、字数或引用数指标；指南中明确的全文交付要求应保留并落实。引用数量按实际引用的去重文献身份计算，不机械平分到各章，不以堆列编号代替论证，也不把尚未写出的引言或后章计入已完成指标。不要输出思考过程或自评分。\n\n优先输出自然 Markdown 正文，不要给整章正文包裹外层代码围栏；内容确需的代码示例可保留各自代码块。最后附伴随记录：\n\n```guide_writer_metadata\n{\"complete\":true,\"remaining_content\":[]}\n```\n\n若确有尚未讲完的内容，complete 为 false，remaining_content 用简短自然语言说明具体缺口，不使用细纲任务 ID。例如“尚需比较两种方法在小样本情形下的差异”。不要为了填写字段虚构缺口，也不要用空泛的“需要更深入”代替缺口。\n\n也接受 JSON：{\"body_markdown\":\"本次正文\",\"complete\":true,\"remaining_content\":[]}。\n\n若需要尚未提供的材料，单独输出 {\"read_source_handles\":[\"来源句柄\"],\"read_atom_ids\":[]} 或用 read_atom_ids 指定已知原子，不能同时交付正文。现有材料已足够时直接成文。\n"
  },
  {
    "role": "user",
    "content": "{\n  \"manuscript_guide\": \"全文按\\\"临床关联证据—免疫机制—代谢物中介—外部干扰—主动干预—毒性管理—方法学与转化边界\\\"推进。引言与正文最终应实际引用至少150篇去重文献；引用必须参与论证，不为凑数机械平分到各章，也不把尚未写出的引言预先计入已完成指标。来源别名应统一处理：P0333与P0584、P0402与P0576、P0049与P0605等视为同一来源，避免重复计数；工具或检索导航标识不得充当正文文献编号。全篇反复出现的核心对象必须有明确主讲位置：Ch1负责观察性关联强度、队列异质性、方案修饰和证据阶梯入口；Ch2负责免疫机制链条并严格区分动物因果与人类关联；Ch3负责代谢物分子靶点、情境依赖和TME浓度缺口；Ch4负责抗生素、PPI、饮食和生活方式等外部暴露的时机、剂量、癌种背景与因果边界；Ch5负责FMT、定义菌群和活体生物药的临床转化、疗效异质性与证据等级；Ch6负责毒性预测、疗效/毒性耦合或解耦、供体与方案情境化安全管理；Ch7负责把前述瓶颈转为方法学设计原则。跨章承接要具体：Ch1让读者理解关联存在但不可普适，留下机制解释和干预验证问题；Ch2解释微生物如何进入先天和适应性免疫，但不解决代谢物浓度与外部扰动问题；Ch3把机制落到化学介质和受体通路，留下血浆与TME暴露脱节的问题；Ch4说明临床现实中的暴露如何重塑这些轴，留下主动干预是否可行；Ch5评估主动干预的疗效与边界，留下毒性管理问题；Ch6处理疗效与毒性如何耦合或解耦，留下预测和标准化难题；Ch7归纳为可执行研究设计。写作中不得使用同一种\\\"背景→机制→应用→局限\\\"模板套所有对象，也不得在每章结尾重复同一句证据不足。比较必须先明确维度：癌种、ICI方案、暴露时窗、基线/纵向、供体特征、宿主免疫状态、模型系统与人体证据、血浆/粪便与TME浓度。对可能性、条件性和阴性结果要保留原有限定：观察性关联不写成因果，动物模型不直接外推人类，血浆浓度不等同组织浓度，Phase II信号不写成Phase III确证，特定癌种或方案的结果不扩大为普适结论。关于P0593：该来源实际内容为别嘌醇通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性的机制研究（小鼠CT26模型+人类膀胱癌回顾性队列），并非TACITO试验。正文中不得将P0593作为TACITO d-FMT联合ICI治疗mRCC的来源引用。P0593应在Ch3肌苷部分作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行机制证据使用，或在Ch5作为非菌群代谢干预的对比案例。mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据应引用P0090系统综述中汇总的Phase II RCT数据（FMT联合pembrolizumab+axitinib，1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%）。\\n\\n全文章节写作安排：\\n\\nCh1 — 实体瘤中肠道微生物组与 ICI 疗效的临床关联证据\\n本章先建立\\\"有信号但无通用标志物\\\"的判断，再解释为何不能外推。顺序为：跨癌种阳性信号与反例 → 队列异质性与功能趋同 → 治疗方案修饰 → 外部药物暴露作为修饰变量 → 基线快照局限与纵向动态 → 证据阶梯表。跨队列统计、肠型、SCRUM-Japan、mCRPC反例和菌株级方案依赖共同支撑无普适标志物；JCOG2007在此主讲方案特异性，后章只回指。抗生素和PPI只保留总体效应量、关键时间窗和校正必要，详细剂量反应、HCC阴性、PPI机制留给Ch4。FMT-LUMINate、MIMic、MITRIC在表中只保留阶段、人群、主要结局和关键限制，机制与试验比较留给Ch5。本章结尾应留下两个问题：这些关联通过什么免疫机制表达，以及主动干预能否跨越观察性关联。\\n\\nCh2 — 微生物调节 ICI 疗效的免疫学机制\\n本章以机制链条组织，不按菌种罗列。顺序为：先天识别与DC启动 → 适应性启动与T细胞亚群 → 屏障、易位与髓系重编程 → 肿瘤类型和模型差异。每个节点都要区分证据层级：小鼠或体外因果、人类宏基因组或伴随观察、肿瘤内微生物边界。六酰化LPS、CD103+ DC、PD-L2/RGMb主讲先天和DC启动；分子模拟主讲适应性启动；P0098的Treg动态只作短回指，主要免疫中介留给Ch6。屏障部分要说明屏障损伤与疗效增强可以分离，细菌易位要区分主动免疫转运与被动漏肠，髓系部分要说明同一易位信号可产生促炎或抑制后果。最后用表格比较肿瘤类型机制与证据类型，不重复Ch1的临床关联强度。\\n\\nCh3 — 微生物代谢物的中介作用与分子机制\\n本章按分子靶点和情境条件组织代谢物，不按来源菌列表。先写SCFAs的双向性：PD-1背景下增强CD8+ T细胞和记忆，CTLA-4背景下可能促Treg或抑制DC共刺激；再写缺氧、葡萄糖剥夺和浓度阈值造成的效应反转。肌苷部分必须分开两条机制：肿瘤内在UBA6抑制与T细胞A2AR或碳源作用；临床只保留血浆关联和早期随机信号，并明确人体TME实测浓度缺失。胆汁酸与色氨酸代谢物围绕TGR5/FXR、AhR/RORγt等受体网络写局部与系统差异。功能通路部分由Ch2回指，但主讲放在本章，用于说明功能特征优于分类学。最后的TME浓度缺口要具体说明其阻碍剂量优化、因果推断和临床给药设计。P0593（别嘌醇/肌苷研究）在本章作为非微生物来源肌苷增效的平行证据使用：别嘌醇通过抑制XDH增加肌苷分泌→上调MHC-I和PD-L1→增强CD8+ T细胞杀伤，在CT26模型中联合抗PD-1实现4/6完全清除，人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）中抗痛风药使用者OS显著优于未使用者。此案例说明肌苷通路可被非菌群手段激活，但不能替代菌群来源肌苷的生理浓度讨论；其人类证据仅为小样本回顾性关联，不升级为因果。\\n\\nCh4 — 外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\\n本章主讲外部暴露如何改变微生物-免疫轴，并与Ch1的修饰变量概览分工：Ch1只给出效应量和时间窗入口，本章展开时机、剂量、药物类别、肿瘤背景和因果边界。抗生素按时间窗和疗程组织，加入HCC阴性结果与PD-L1分层，防止单一负面模型。PPI部分从流行病学关联转到口腔化易位、多样性下降和近期化疗修饰，并用H2B对照提出降级建议。饮食和生活方式部分区分食物基质、定义菌株补充剂和非标准化益生菌，避免把益生菌统一写成有益或有害。所有推断都要标注观察性证据和适应症偏倚，不能把药物暴露与疗效下降直接写成菌群因果链。\\n\\nCh5 — 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\\n本章是主动干预的临床转化主轴。顺序为：初治人群信号 → 耐药人群边界 → 定义菌群和活体生物药 → 安全性边界 → 证据等级与标准化。FMT-LUMINate的疗效与\\\"有害菌丢失而非供体定植\\\"机制在此主讲；MIMic的定植动力学和生存数据也在此展开；MITRIC主讲阴性原因。Ch1的证据阶梯表只作为入口，本章不重复列表式介绍，而解释异质性来源。关于mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据：细纲原将TACITO数据归于P0593，但P0593实际内容为别嘌醇/肌苷机制研究，不包含TACITO试验数据。本章mRCC FMT随机证据应引用P0090系统综述中汇总的Phase II RCT数据：FMT联合pembrolizumab+axitinib，1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%（p=0.036），ORR 54% vs 28%，未增加≥3级不良事件。此数据来自会议摘要级别的II期RCT，应标注证据等级为早期随机、小样本。不得在正文中引用不存在的TACITO具体数值（如12个月PFS 70% vs 41%、中位PFS 24.0 vs 9.0个月、P=0.053），除非后续获得独立来源确认。安全性部分与Ch6分工：本章保留干预安全边界和试验设计含义，毒性预测、耦合或解耦和管理策略留给Ch6。\\n\\nCh6 — 微生物组与免疫治疗毒性的关联\\n本章从毒性表型出发，不按药物列表。顺序为：结肠炎最强证据与因果验证 → 器官特异性和预测模型困境 → 疗效与毒性耦合或解耦 → 干预相关毒性的情境依赖 → 分子机制。Ch5已讲干预疗效与总体安全边界，本章新增的是毒性预测标志物、供体-方案交互和管理含义。FMT-LUMINate的Cluster B、Prevotella和Segatella copri数据在此主讲毒性情境，不再重述完整试验设计；P0284的屏障和代谢双重机制只保留与毒性相关的部分，详细机制回指Ch2。非结肠炎毒性必须明确样本量不足，不能把结肠炎结论外推到心肌炎或神经毒性。\\n\\nCh7 — 方法学挑战与未来研究方向\\n本章不是再次总结各章局限，而是把瓶颈转为可操作设计原则。顺序为：技术与标准化 → 观察性因果推断 → 临床证据与人群表征 → 未来方法。技术部分用标准化重分析和培养组学说明噪音与真实信号并存；因果部分强调反向因果、药物、饮食、年龄等混杂和孟德尔随机化边界；临床部分强调Phase III缺席、年龄、儿科、种族和TME浓度缺口；未来部分提出功能导向、多组学、AI、类器官或芯片和供体制剂标准化。引用应服务设计原则，不重复前文具体数值，也不把每个已知缺口写成全文唯一主线。\",\n  \"chapter_assignment\": {\n    \"chapter_id\": \"Ch5\",\n    \"title\": \"微生物干预策略的临床转化现状\",\n    \"writing_arrangement\": \"本章是主动干预的临床转化主轴。顺序为：初治人群信号 → 耐药人群边界 → 定义菌群和活体生物药 → 安全性边界 → 证据等级与标准化。FMT-LUMINate的疗效与\\\"有害菌丢失而非供体定植\\\"机制在此主讲；MIMic的定植动力学和生存数据也在此展开；MITRIC主讲阴性原因。Ch1的证据阶梯表只作为入口，本章不重复列表式介绍，而解释异质性来源。关于mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据：细纲原将TACITO数据归于P0593，但P0593实际内容为别嘌醇/肌苷机制研究，不包含TACITO试验数据。本章mRCC FMT随机证据应引用P0090系统综述中汇总的Phase II RCT数据：FMT联合pembrolizumab+axitinib，1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%（p=0.036），ORR 54% vs 28%，未增加≥3级不良事件。此数据来自会议摘要级别的II期RCT，应标注证据等级为早期随机、小样本。不得在正文中引用不存在的TACITO具体数值（如12个月PFS 70% vs 41%、中位PFS 24.0 vs 9.0个月、P=0.053），除非后续获得独立来源确认。安全性部分与Ch6分工：本章保留干预安全边界和试验设计含义，毒性预测、耦合或解耦和管理策略留给Ch6。\",\n    \"required_content\": [\n      \"保留FMT-LUMINate在NSCLC和黑色素瘤中的ORR差异、方案背景差异、有害菌丢失机制及单臂设计局限。\",\n      \"保留MIMic的ORR、PFS、OS和供体菌株定植或功能代谢通路线索。\",\n      \"保留MITRIC的阴性结果、短暂定植、髓系主导微环境和高IL-8等失败机制。\",\n      \"mRCC中FMT联合ICI的随机证据引用P0090汇总数据（1年PFS 66.7% vs 35.0%，ORR 54% vs 28%），标注为Phase II RCT、小样本、会议摘要级别。不使用P0593作为此数据来源。\",\n      \"保留CBM588、MRx0518、MET4等定义菌群或活体生物药的标准化优势、早期信号和疗效确证不足。\",\n      \"保留无大型Phase III RCT的结论，并说明供体来源、预处理、给药途径、人群分层和制造质控是转化瓶颈。\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"materials\": {\n    \"schema_version\": \"optomind.guided_body_materials.v1\",\n    \"evidence_atoms\": [\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::113e9e24698e48b617801ee8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13d62ece3687ca3ff02b6c26\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ccd742ea527af43296074069\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究设计为前瞻性、多中心、单臂II期临床试验。入组标准包括：NSCLC患者需PD-L1 TPS ≥50%且无一线可操作基因改变；黑色素瘤患者不限BRAF状态。所有患者在开始ICI治疗前一周内接受来自健康供体的单次FMT（口服胶囊）。主要终点是NSCLC队列的ORR。次要终点包括黑色素瘤ORR、1年无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、疾病控制率（DCR）及安全性。微生物组分析采用鸟枪法宏基因组测序，结合定量PCR和高通量培养组学验证细菌变化。此外，通过血浆代谢组学和流式细胞术分析免疫代谢景观，并在抗生素处理的荷瘤小鼠模型中通过回输“丢失”的细菌混合物来验证因果机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1876e77f5afb8193a6a5257e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的临床活性证据，证实FMT可提高ORR。识别出“基线有害菌清除”作为潜在的药效学生物标志物，并揭示了其与色氨酸代谢抑制及CD8+ T细胞扩增的关联。\",\n          \"limits\": \"研究为单臂设计，缺乏安慰剂对照，难以完全排除自然病程或其他混杂因素。样本量较小（每队列20人），限制了亚组分析和统计效力。黑色素瘤队列中观察到的严重毒性信号（如心肌炎）需要更大规模的随机试验进一步确认。供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但具体筛选标准尚未确立。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::999c7dbb4eb04f853f51ce68\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC患者接受FMT+抗PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR达到80%（16/20），满足主要终点；1年OS为100%；未观察到3级及以上与治疗相关的不良事件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef45091c05d3c80087467567\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"黑色素瘤患者接受FMT+抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4\",\n          \"finding\": \"ORR为75%（15/20）；观察到较文献报道更早发生的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），包括心肌炎；部分严重AEs与富含Prevotella的供体有关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c4539dfe7511b5ee26afddc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析与临床响应关联\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）相比，在FMT后表现出显著更高的基线细菌物种丢失幅度。这种丢失主要由有害菌（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus）构成，而非供体菌株的定植。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f77d7a57b1c5af196e7ec273\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制验证（动物实验）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在抗生素处理的小鼠中，将FMT响应者基线样本中丢失的有害细菌混合物重新引入，抵消了FMT联合ICI的抗肿瘤效应，证实消除有害菌是治疗获益的必要条件。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5bc8bb178fbe4aff2844625\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48e81723cf1694edffb2648d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂改善了NSCLC和黑色素瘤的预后，但超过半数的患者存在原发性耐药。目前尚不清楚健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1（NSCLC）或抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4（黑色素瘤）在一线治疗中的临床活性和安全性，以及FMT增强ICI疗效的人类机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f10ae71e3af0e5426782b275\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和皮肤黑色素瘤患者，评估健康供体粪便微生物群移植（FMT）联合一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗的临床疗效、安全性及机制。NSCLC队列接受抗PD-1单药治疗，黑色素瘤队列接受抗PD-1联合抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfc280fdf99afe8f46ce98b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一项多中心、开放标签的II期临床试验（FMT-LUMINate），旨在评估单次口服胶囊FMT在启动ICI治疗前对原发性耐药患者的影响。研究纳入20名NSCLC患者和20名黑色素瘤患者。主要终点为NSCLC队列的客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示，NSCLC队列ORR为80%，超过预设阈值；黑色素瘤队列ORR为75%。安全性方面，NSCLC组无3级及以上不良事件，而黑色素瘤组出现较早发的严重免疫相关不良反应（irAEs），特别是心肌炎，且与特定供体菌群有关。机制研究发现，响应者并非通过获得特定的供体菌株定植获益，而是通过显著清除基线存在的有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster和Clostridium属），从而降低色氨酸代谢途径活性并改善全身免疫微环境。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ada46cc65142f66137be5912\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于未经过ICI治疗的原发性耐药患者；NSCLC结果基于高PD-L1表达人群；黑色素瘤结果包含不同BRAF状态。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT联合ICI在NSCLC（抗PD-1）和黑色素瘤（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中的具体ORR数据（分别为80%和75%），证明了其在一线治疗中提高临床活性的能力。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1440b6c81c7ea354a5c0604d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制主要在人类队列中通过相关性分析发现，并通过小鼠模型进行功能验证；不同肿瘤类型中富集的有益菌种类有限重叠，但有害菌清除模式一致。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐明了FMT起效的潜在机制：响应者的获益主要依赖于基线有害细菌物种（如Enterocloster, Clostridium）的大量丢失，而非供体菌株的成功定植。这种丢失与血浆中色氨酸代谢产物（喹啉酸、犬尿氨酸）水平的降低以及效应性CD8+ T细胞的增加相关。动物实验证实，重新引入这些丢失的有害菌会阻断ICI疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d56ff3d1c73603487584373\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅在黑色素瘤双免疫治疗队列中观察到显著的毒性信号；在NSCLC单药治疗或未使用双免疫治疗的既往研究中未观察到相同程度的毒性。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了特定供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制（抗PD-1/CTLA-4）背景下严重免疫相关不良反应（如心肌炎、早期发作的3级以上AEs）之间的关联。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2631f5b2da9f5640b19f7f49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究指出FMT疗效不依赖于供体-宿主相似性或菌株水平定植，而是依赖于基线微生物组的整体重塑和有害菌清除。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a5656eba7a625dd6b12644d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到TACITO试验也观察到类似的结果，即在FMT组中观察到基线物种的消除，而在安慰剂组中没有。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f453542c412b162f0e6a8104\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的机制结论（有害菌清除导致疗效）是基于观察性关联和小鼠功能验证，需谨慎推断其在所有FMT场景下的普适性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5dfc4aabe5eadd2a5f8c90b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"黑色素瘤队列中的严重毒性信号可能与双免疫检查点抑制的背景有关，不能直接外推至单药ICI治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b12e17c00b7f89529c4a3847\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"供体选择对毒性的影响提示个体化差异，但本研究未建立标准化的供体筛选算法，仅作为警示。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78071e0f85770a550546484c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"NSCLC队列的高ORR可能受限于高PD-L1表达人群的预后较好，需注意人群特异性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0223323bb5c9771bfce68f11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::456d19e731aeafe092b5f494\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6edcdf66c26215bc9744d2b6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6daa66dcd75ef6a88df089e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::497b875e9b14be91a0c84f61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e34ebbbb34ba3c89d1c553df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究人群：NSCLC队列（n=20，一线治疗，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，无既往抗PD-1暴露）；黑色素瘤队列（n=20，一线治疗，允许既往辅助抗PD-1但需停药>6个月）。干预措施：单次健康供体粪便微生物移植（FMT，口服胶囊）后紧接着启动ICI治疗。NSCLC组使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）单药；黑色素瘤组使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4（双ICI）治疗的ORR为75%（15/20）。关于毒性信号，在黑色素瘤双ICI组中观察到严重不良事件（AEs）的发生率较高且起病更早：13名患者（65%）经历了3级或更高级别的AEs，其中腹泻或结肠炎是最常见的3级及以上AE（20%的患者），另有15%的患者出现心肌炎。严重毒性的中位起病时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后40天，早于文献报道的60天。相比之下，NSCLC单药抗PD-1组无3级或以上AEs发生。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT联合免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）在非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）和黑色素瘤中的具体客观缓解率（ORR），以及双免疫检查点抑制剂（dual ICI）治疗下的毒性信号特征。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"该研究通过FMT-LUMINate II期临床试验评估了FMT联合ICI在两种不同癌症背景下的临床活性与安全性。结果显示，FMT显著提高了NSCLC患者对单药抗PD-1治疗的反应率（80%），并改善了黑色素瘤患者对双免疫检查点阻断（抗PD-1+抗CTLA-4）的反应率（75%）。然而，在黑色素瘤双ICI背景下，FMT联合治疗伴随着更高的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）风险，特别是心肌炎和早期发作的严重毒性。这种毒性信号与特定供体来源的微生物群（富含Prevotella spp.）有关，且仅在双ICI背景下出现，而在单药抗PD-1背景下未观察到类似毒性。这表明FMT的安全性与特定的ICI治疗方案及供体微生物特征存在交互作用。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": []\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::436fcf7aa325545c7b4b35ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\",\n              \"finding\": \"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R23\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\",\n            \"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1e65c84abaf39bc948ae4e34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\",\n            \"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b581c9a20631821c53f134ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bdf06d41fae85cb4002eea7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e56bf9725ffb96585d3b26d8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The authors explicitly state that this is a phase 2 trial, not a phase 3 trial. They mention that the findings will be assessed as part of the CanBiome2 randomized trial (NCT06623461), which is described as a randomized trial evaluating FMT in combination with ICI in 128 patients, but the current paper does not report the results of this phase 3 trial. The study design was open-label and single-arm for the cohorts reported here, lacking the randomization required for a phase 3 RCT status.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_dcbe39b3d2\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires evidence of a completed large randomised phase III trial. This material provides only a phase 2 trial. While the authors reference an ongoing/forthcoming phase 3 trial (CanBiome2), they do not provide its results or confirm its completion within this text.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of FMT-LUMINate, a multicenter, open-label, phase 2 trial evaluating healthy donor fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) combined with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) or melanoma. The trial enrolled 40 patients (20 NSCLC, 20 melanoma). In the NSCLC cohort receiving anti-PD-1 monotherapy, the objective response rate (ORR) was 80%. In the melanoma cohort receiving dual anti-PD-1 and anti-CTLA-4 therapy, the ORR was 75%. The study found that clinical response was associated with the loss of baseline deleterious bacterial species rather than the engraftment of donor-specific strains. Safety data indicated no grade 3+ adverse events in the NSCLC cohort, but a higher incidence of severe immune-related adverse events (including myocarditis) in the melanoma cohort, particularly among recipients of donors rich in Prevotella spp.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ffe022f4ac7a2eb8241e5388\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a91f0ed643887e9f1b1d\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ef95a97dcd7bd8c151c4\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-501f35983c2f020a5c71\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-81ec1ef0c2a046851171\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d46f32b2af56fa1c47e2\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-02757a568956f4b210b5\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-47775c7896730e2260bc\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b08d87be9985923039c9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4d651eaa044aee02c8ec\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-1294ef6fcf50c0be4a42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-6e217865835c2f670e17\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b1f79ce65e003459f3ed\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-786845b1cd45dd24fdc8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-f0ebbdf389d42cf46d30\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3f08daede868f51719f44f75\",\n          \"snapshot::cc9c61313270bf8ed21449cd\",\n          \"snapshot::858e2e285637cdae2d18e8b5\",\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\",\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11e07541ccca87380640aaae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e0ab03ae8f4e8669b7c7052e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::163a7a8481c0223f6106b97e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是 Ch5/Ch6 核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中安全性数据的详细统计结果、毒性事件的具体临床特征（如心肌炎发生率、起病时间）以及与供体微生物组相关的因果关联分析，作为核心证据支持关于FMT安全性的讨论。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在NSCLC队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1治疗的患者未出现3级或更高不良事件（AEs），仅15%患者因2级AE使用皮质类固醇；而在黑色素瘤队列中，65%患者经历3级或更高AEs，其中腹泻/结肠炎占20%，心肌炎发生率为15%（3例），显著高于文献报道的<1%。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）判定该组合总体安全，但指出黑色素瘤队列中的严重AEs起病更早（中位40天 vs 文献60天）。聚类分析显示，来自富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（特别是供体5）与3级及以上AEs的发生密切相关：所有由供体5提供的粪便导致黑色素瘤患者出现3级+ AEs，且2/3例心肌炎患者接受了供体5的FMT。这些毒性仅在双免疫检查点抑制剂（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）背景下观察到，而在单药抗PD-1治疗中未出现。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的NSCLC（n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。NSCLC组接受单药抗PD-1（pembrolizumab），黑色素瘤组接受双免疫检查点抑制剂（nivolumab + ipilimumab）。供体聚类基于 shotgun metagenomic sequencing 数据，使用 Bray-Curtis 指数进行无监督聚类，并通过 PERMANOVA 评估组间差异。AEs分级依据 CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"展示供体微生物组特征与免疫相关不良反应（irAEs）之间的机制性联系，特别是普雷沃菌属定植与特定T细胞亚群变化的关联，用于解释为何某些供体会增加毒性风险。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"通过无监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个 distinct clusters (P = 0.001)。Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（如 Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤患者中，接受 Cluster B 供体FMT后，出现3级+ AEs的患者中这些菌属显著富集（LDA score > 2, P < 0.05）。进一步分析显示，在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者中，S. copri 的定植与外周血中 CD4+ T细胞亚群比例增加相关（P = 0.026），而这种关联在单药抗PD-1治疗中不存在。这表明普雷沃菌属的定植是双免疫检查点抑制背景下毒性增加的驱动因素。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"分析对象包括FMT-LUMINate黑色素瘤队列及之前发表的MIMIC试验（Phase 1, melanoma, anti-PD-1 monotherapy）数据。统计方法包括 Fisher's exact test 比较组间差异，LEfSe 进行线性判别分析效应大小，以及 Spearman's r 相关性分析微生物定植与免疫细胞频率的关系。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R23\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT联合ICI治疗的安全性与供体微生物组特征及ICI治疗方案之间的复杂相互作用。首先，FMT本身在NSCLC（单药抗PD-1）中表现出良好的耐受性，无3级以上AEs。然而，在黑色素瘤（双药抗PD-1/CTLA-4）中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC认可，但出现了加速发作的严重AEs，特别是心肌炎。这种毒性信号并非随机分布，而是与特定的供体微生物组特征紧密相关。通过供体聚类分析，研究发现富含普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.）的供体（Cluster B）与3级以上AEs的发生显著相关。机制上，这种关联依赖于ICI的治疗背景：普雷沃菌属的定植及其引发的CD4+ T细胞变化仅在双免疫检查点抑制（anti-PD-1 + anti-CTLA-4）条件下导致毒性，而在单药抗PD-1条件下不表现。这提示普雷沃菌属可能是双免疫检查点抑制背景下免疫相关不良反应的潜在驱动因子，强调了根据ICI方案选择合适供体的重要性。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管已将其列为特殊关注AE。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化‘普雷沃菌属丰富度’阈值以排除高风险供体，文中未给出明确操作指南。\\\", \\\"长期随访中，这些早期AEs对最终肿瘤疗效是否有负面影响，文中提到数值上有关联但统计不显著，需更大样本验证。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验的详细安全性数据及供体聚类分析是本章核心证据，需深入解读其统计方法及毒性事件的具体临床特征。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT-LUMINate试验中关于安全性数据的具体统计结果、毒性事件临床特征（特别是心肌炎和腹泻/结肠炎的发作时间），以及供体微生物组聚类分析与免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）关联的详细机制证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在黑色素瘤队列中，19名患者（95%）出现任何级别的与治疗相关的不良事件（AEs），其中12名（60%）出现3级或更高级别的AEs，1名出现4级AEs。最常见的3级或以上AE是腹泻或结肠炎（20%的患者）。有3名患者（15%）发生心肌炎，这高于文献报道的<1%的发生率。严重毒性的中位发作时间为开始抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4治疗后的40天，早于文献报告的60天。独立数据和安全监测委员会（DSMC）认为这些严重AEs比既往文献报道的发作更早。在NSCLC队列中，没有患者出现3级或更高级别的AEs。通过非监督聚类分析，健康供体的肠道微生物组被分为两个截然不同的簇（P = 0.001）。B簇（包含供体5和供体11）以高丰度的Prevotella spp.为特征。差异丰度分析证实，P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae GGB1146 SGB1472在接受双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的黑色素瘤患者中，若发生3级或以上AEs则显著富集。后FMT定植的P. sp. Marseille-P4119、P. stercorea和Prevotellaceae SGB1472与3级或以上AEs显著相关（P < 0.001, P = 0.023, P < 0.001）。供体5提供的粪便在所有接受双ICI治疗的黑色素瘤患者中均导致3级或以上AEs，且两名发生快速发作心肌炎的患者均接受了来自供体5的FMT。然而，当仅使用抗PD-1单药治疗时（如之前的MIMIC试验中的供体5数据或本研究的NSCLC队列），来自Cluster B的供体并未引起毒性。综合所有经历3级或以上AEs的患者（包括当前研究和之前的MIMIC试验），来自Cluster B供体的粪便仅在联合PD-1和CTLA-4阻断的患者中引起毒性（P = 0.051）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为FMT-LUMINate试验中的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC, n=20）和黑色素瘤（n=20）患者。黑色素瘤患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（nivolumab）和抗CTLA-4（ipilimumab）治疗；NSCLC患者接受FMT联合抗PD-1（pembrolizumab）治疗。供体聚类基于41个来自9名供体的样本进行Bray-Curtis不相似度分析。AEs分级依据CTCAE v5.0。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"本研究揭示了FMT结合不同免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）背景下的安全性差异及其潜在的微生物机制。首先，FMT联合抗PD-1在NSCLC中表现出良好的安全性，无3级或以上AEs；而在联合抗PD-1和抗CTLA-4的黑色素瘤中，虽然总体安全性被DSMC判定为可接受，但出现了加速发作的严重免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），特别是心肌炎和中位发作时间提前至40天。其次，供体微生物组的组成决定了这种毒性风险。通过非监督聚类，供体被分为富含Prevotella spp.的Cluster B和其他Cluster A。Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）与严重的irAEs（包括心肌炎）密切相关，但这种关联具有严格的上下文依赖性：它仅在抗CTLA-4存在的情况下显现，而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下不引发毒性。这表明特定的微生物类群（如Prevotella spp.）与ICI骨架之间存在情境依赖性的相互作用，可能驱动了双重阻断下的过度免疫反应。因此，供体选择对于未来FMT试验的安全性至关重要，特别是当联合使用抗CTLA-4时。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"心肌炎的具体病理生理机制尚需进一步探索，尽管观察到其与特定菌属定植及CD4+ T细胞亚群变化的关联。\\\", \\\"供体筛选标准如何具体量化以避免Cluster B供体，目前仅指出需排除此类供体。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1038/s41591-025-04186-5\",\n                \"material_depth\": \"\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"071823eff68d7dbea395490dd4643170131b5f6a\",\n                \"reading_role\": \"\",\n                \"section_path\": [],\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0583\",\n                \"title\": \"Fecal microbiota transplantation plus immunotherapy in non-small cell lung cancer and melanoma: the phase 2 FMT-LUMINate trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"FMT-LUMINate 试验中 FMT 联合 ICI 的 ORR 数据是多少？供体菌群特征（如 Prevotella）与毒性（心肌炎）的关联机制是什么？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供FMT联合ICI在NSCLC和黑色素瘤一线治疗中的客观缓解率（ORR）具体数据，以及安全性特征。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在FMT-LUMINate试验中，接受健康供体FMT联合抗PD-1单药治疗的非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者（n=20），其客观缓解率（ORR）为80%（16/20），超过了预设的64%主要终点阈值。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受FMT联合抗PD-1加抗CTLA-4双免疫检查点抑制剂治疗的患者（n=20），ORR为75%（15/20）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"NSCLC队列：一线治疗，无驱动基因突变，PD-L1 TPS ≥ 50%，使用帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）。黑色素瘤队列：一线或既往辅助治疗后复发>6个月，使用纳武利尤单抗（nivolumab）联合伊匹木单抗（ipilimumab）。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"揭示供体菌群特征（Prevotella富集）与特定毒性（心肌炎、3级及以上AEs）的关联机制，强调治疗背景（双免疫抑制 vs 单药）的关键调节作用。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"供体微生物组聚类显示，Cluster B（包含供体5和11）以高丰度的普雷沃菌属（Prevotella spp.，如Segatella copri, Prevotella sp. Marseille-P4119, P. stercorea）为特征。在黑色素瘤队列中，接受Cluster B供体（特别是供体5）FMT的患者发生了严重的免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），包括3例心肌炎（发生率15%），且发病时间显著提前（中位40天，而文献报道通常为60天）。其中2例心肌炎患者均接受了供体5的FMT，发病迅速（分别为第22天和第25天）。统计分析显示，Cluster B供体的粪便仅在双PD-1和CTLA-4阻断背景下导致毒性（P=0.051），而在抗PD-1单药治疗背景下未观察到此类毒性。此外，S. copri的定植与这些严重AEs患者外周血中CD4+ T细胞亚群增加相关。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"比较对象：接受不同供体FMT的患者；治疗背景对比：黑色素瘤队列（双ICI）vs NSCLC队列及既往MIMIC试验（均为抗PD-1单药）。供体5在MIMIC试验（抗PD-1单药）中提供的7次FMT均未导致3级及以上AEs，而在本试验黑色素瘤队列中导致的FMT均伴随严重AEs。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"该研究阐明了FMT增强ICI疗效的机制并非主要依赖于供体菌株的定植或供主微生物组的相似度，而是取决于患者基线有害菌群的清除。具体来说，响应者（Responders）在接受FMT后表现出比非响应者更显著的基线细菌物种丢失（SGB loss），特别是那些已知与ICI耐药相关的有害菌属（如Enterocloster, Clostridium, Streptococcus等）。这种有害菌的消除导致了色氨酸代谢途径的减弱，降低了血浆中喹啉酸（quinolinic acid）和犬尿氨酸（kynurenine）的水平，从而改善了免疫代谢微环境（增加效应CD8+ T细胞，减少调节性T细胞）。关于毒性机制，研究发现特定的供体菌群特征（富含Prevotella spp.）与双免疫检查点抑制剂（抗PD-1 + 抗CTLA-4）背景下的严重免疫相关不良事件（如心肌炎）存在情境依赖性关联。这种毒性风险在单药抗PD-1治疗中并未出现，提示供体选择需根据具体的ICI治疗方案进行优化。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"Prevotella spp. 诱导心肌炎的具体分子机制（如通过何种抗原或代谢物激活特定T细胞亚群）在本研究中仅表现为相关性，未深入解析其下游信号通路。\\\", \\\"虽然发现了基线有害菌丢失是疗效的关键预测因子，但哪些特定的丢失菌种组合对疗效贡献最大，以及是否可以通过定向清除而非全菌群移植来实现这一效果，仍需进一步研究。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ceff59cf10840ae2fa4f87a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a99646db3b749ddfd25fe40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::deb5f1b5a0ec5f896f857444\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08554aa4c222491df9d38ef8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Single-arm, multicenter phase I clinical trial. Patients received bowel preparation, followed by oral administration of capsules containing stool from one of three healthy male donors. Anti-PD1 therapy (nivolumab or pembrolizumab) started at least 7 days post-FMT. Outcomes were assessed using RECIST 1.1 criteria. Survival analysis used Kaplan-Meier methods. Metagenomic sequencing was performed on stool samples to analyze taxonomic composition (MetaPhlAn) and functional gene families (HUMAnN). Post hoc subgroup analyses compared responders vs. non-responders and patients with vs. without FMT-specific toxicity (FT) based on microbial and functional profiles.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::37fd84d50ba8233eb66b5714\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides long-term survival data (median OS 52.8 months) for a small cohort of advanced melanoma patients treated with oral FMT plus anti-PD1, demonstrating high safety and promising efficacy signals compared to historical controls.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Small sample size (N=20), single-arm design without a control group, and lack of statistical power for definitive conclusions. Results are hypothesis-generating. Patient selection bias (excluded those appropriate for combination therapy).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7e3e6165a31ec1e105e75b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies potential biomarkers for response, linking FMT-specific mild toxicity and long-term survival to specific microbial taxa (e.g., SCFA producers) and functional metabolic pathways (glycan modification, SCFA biosynthesis).\",\n          \"limits\": \"Associations are derived from post hoc analyses. Causality between specific microbes/enzymes and clinical benefit is not established. The 'donor effect' could not be clearly disentangled due to the small cohort and mixed donor usage.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::024518a823f6006dd3e972f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Entire cohort (N=20), median follow-up 52.8 months\",\n          \"finding\": \"Median PFS was 29.6 months; median OS was 52.8 months. ORR was 65% (4 complete responses). Safety profile showed no increase in severe immune-related adverse events (irAEs); only grade 3 toxicities occurred.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3485959e4adbd9d7481e46dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Responders (R, N=13) vs. Non-responders (NR, N=7)\",\n          \"finding\": \"R patients had significantly longer mPFS (52.8 vs. 5.2 months, p=0.0016) and longer mOS (52.8 vs. 17.6 months, p=0.0628). R patients sustained donor-derived microbial similarity over time.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ebb834ea4cc8b7658e4ac8d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients with FMT-specific toxicity (FT, N=8) vs. Without FT (NFT, N=12)\",\n          \"finding\": \"All 8 FT patients were responders. FT patients had significantly improved mPFS (52.8 vs. 15.9 months, p=0.0364) and trend towards improved mOS (53.9 vs. 24.6 months, p=0.0610). FT was associated with enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa and glycan-modifying enzymes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dffaafcf80cafef8980d6a54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Long-term survivors (LTS) vs. Short-term survivors (STS)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LTS were enriched for commensal bacteria (Alistipes, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes involved in amino acid/SCFA biosynthesis. STS were enriched for stress-associated oxidative metabolism pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a938bbf69ccdde1dcf569c84\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::19f5ba98faa7f71a33a18835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To evaluate whether modifying the gut microbiome via oral FMT from healthy donors can improve the safety, response rate, and survival outcomes of anti-PD1 therapy in patients with advanced melanoma who are naive to advanced-stage treatment, potentially overcoming primary resistance to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f99b8e9719b07fd9b3d34bf5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Advanced cutaneous melanoma patients (N=20), treatment-naïve for advanced disease, receiving oral fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) from healthy donors followed by single-agent anti-PD1 therapy. Multicenter phase I trial conducted in Canada.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::835431f5f287a104ceabd51e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This study reports the final survival outcomes of the MIMic phase I trial, evaluating the safety and efficacy of combining oral FMT with healthy donor stool and anti-PD1 immunotherapy as first-line treatment for advanced melanoma. The trial enrolled 20 patients who received a single dose of FMT followed by nivolumab or pembrolizumab. The primary endpoint was safety, while secondary endpoints included objective response rate (ORR), progression-free survival (PFS), and overall survival (OS). The study found that the combination was safe, with an ORR of 65%. Median PFS was 29.6 months and median OS was 52.8 months, figures reported as higher than historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) and real-world data. Post hoc analyses linked clinical responses to specific microbial engraftment patterns and functional metabolic pathways, suggesting that successful microbiome modulation may enhance ICI efficacy.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f8959cd8dd927a10f9dd3654\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Results are from a single-arm, small-sample Phase I trial. Cannot establish causal superiority over standard care due to lack of concurrent control arm. Patient population was restricted to those unsuitable for combination immunotherapy.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Reports clinical efficacy outcomes (ORR 65%, mPFS 29.6 mo, mOS 52.8 mo) for FMT+anti-PD1 in advanced melanoma, showing improvements over historical RCT benchmarks for anti-PD1 alone.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da8e241ae0ffdf09b558a4ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are inferred from correlative post hoc analyses. The role of FMT-specific toxicity as a proxy for engraftment success is observational. Functional profiling relies on metagenomic prediction, which may not reflect actual protein activity or host interaction.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Links clinical response to specific microbial features: Responders and long-term survivors show enrichment of SCFA-producing taxa (Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and enzymes for glycan modification/amino acid biosynthesis. Non-responders/short-term survivors show enrichment of oxidative/stress pathways and Hungatella hathewayi.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d1f3aa72134d1a09a615318\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Comparison of oral capsule-based FMT (this study) vs. invasive colonoscopic FMT (referenced in intro). This study supports the feasibility and safety of oral delivery for systemic immune modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76bf45b8fc5ee9800416db98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"No increase in severe irAEs; FMT-specific toxicities were mild (Grade 1-2 GI).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb82a0f9f419547426bb1f12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Acknowledges small sample size, lack of control arm, and hypothesis-generating nature of results.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::754021e869ff2a2dba53a7aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The study population is limited to advanced cutaneous melanoma patients ineligible for combination immunotherapy; results may not generalize to other solid tumors or earlier-stage disease.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a37fb175d8428498e2cdd297\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Survival comparisons with historical RCTs are noted by authors but are confounded by patient selection biases and temporal changes in care; do not treat as definitive proof of superiority.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de45d8ce55cd7c245f96e6fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Microbial associations are correlational; causality between specific taxa/pathways and ICI response is not proven within this study design.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::faf64be5a80ca4ce1d2dbf3a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Improved survival in advanced melanoma patients treated with fecal microbiota transplantation using healthy donor stool in combination with anti-PD1: final results of the MIMic phase 1 trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::004e7d4bb46dac64f072d7f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e055ed851f0bbe3c6e1076f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为20名晚期黑色素瘤患者；供体为3名健康男性；给药方式为口服胶囊；预处理为PEG肠道准备；无抗生素使用。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MIMic试验使用了来自三位健康男性供体的粪便进行口服FMT。所有患者均接受单一供体的粪便（每位患者对应一位供体），未混合多供体粪便。供体经过“严格的选择标准”筛选（文中引用了之前的出版物Craven et al. 2017及Routy et al. 2023中的详细标准）。FMT产品以胶囊形式给药，每剂包含35-40粒胶囊，相当于80-100克粪便。在给予FMT前一天，患者使用聚乙二醇（PEG）基肠道准备液进行预处理，且治疗期间未使用抗生素。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R12\",\n                \"R13\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为FMT干预标准化中供体筛选和制备流程的具体案例，展示如何通过严格筛选和健康供体来源来保证干预的一致性和安全性，同时指出单供体使用的局限性。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MIMic试验在供体筛选和FMT制备方面采取了高度标准化的策略，旨在确保干预的安全性和微生物定植的可预测性。\\n\\n1. **供体筛选标准**：研究采用了“严格的选择标准”（stringent selection criteria）来筛选健康供体。虽然正文未列出具体排除指标的细节，但明确引用了关于代谢综合征疾病FMT供体筛选成本的研究（Craven et al., 2017, R13）以及该团队之前发表的I期试验方案（Routy et al., 2023, R12），暗示其遵循了当时临床前或早期临床试验中较为严格的卫生学、传染病及健康状况筛查流程。这种严格筛选是作为正面教材的，因为它最大限度地降低了传播病原体或引入致病微生物的风险，确保了“健康供体粪便”这一干预物的纯净度。\\n\\n2. **FMT制备与给药流程**：\\n   - **单一供源 vs 混合供源**：试验设计采用单一供体粪便（single healthy donor stool），每位患者仅接受来自三位指定男性供体中某一人的粪便。这种做法简化了批次管理，减少了不同供体间微生物组异质性带来的混杂因素，有利于评估特定微生物组合对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的反应。然而，这也可能是一个反面教材或局限性，因为缺乏多供体混合可能无法覆盖更广泛的有益菌群多样性，且文中提到“没有明显的供体效应”，说明单个供体的效果在不同患者间可能存在差异，但未深入探讨混合供体是否会更优。\\n   - **制剂形式**：将粪便制成口服胶囊（35-40粒/剂，含80-100g粪便），而非传统的灌肠或鼻胃管给药。这提高了患者的依从性，减少了侵入性操作带来的感染风险，是FMT非侵入化、标准化的重要进展。\\n   - **预处理与辅助措施**：在FMT前一日使用PEG基肠道准备液，旨在清除原有肠道内容物，为新菌群定植腾出生态位。特别值得注意的是，研究中明确禁止使用抗生素，以避免抗生素对肠道菌群的破坏干扰FMT的效果或引起耐药性问题。这种“清洁但不杀菌”的准备策略是标准化流程中的关键控制点。\\n\\n总体而言，该试验通过严格的供体准入、单一的供体来源、标准化的胶囊制剂以及特定的肠道预处理，构建了一套可重复的FMT干预流程。其成功的关键在于确保了输入菌群的健康属性和定植潜力，为后续观察微生物组变化与临床疗效的关系提供了可靠的基础。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"文中引用的供体筛选具体指标（如具体的病原体检测列表、BMI限制、饮食要求等）未在本文正文中详细列出，需参考R12和R13获取完整细节。\",\n            \"单一供体与多供体混合在长期定植稳定性和临床获益上的比较数据不足，仅观察到无显著供体效应，未深入分析为何选择单一供体而非混合供体。\",\n            \"PEG肠道准备的具体配方浓度、体积及服用时间未详细说明。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::25fa34eabb812f0508d3952a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d9a7b270e9001642aeaeb4d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The paper provides mechanistic insights linking clinical response to microbial engraftment, noting that responders and long-term survivors showed enrichment of short-chain fatty acid (SCFA)-produ taxa (e.g., Blautia, Roseburia, Faecalibacterium) and glycan-modifying enzymes. It also suggests that mild FMT-specific gastrointestinal toxicity may serve as a marker for successful microbial integration and immune priming. Additionally, the text contrasts these findings with historical RCT data (e.g., KEYNOTE-006, CheckMate 067) to contextualize the magnitude of observed benefits, though it acknowledges limitations regarding patient selection bias.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU01_search_candidate_8a825f7f53\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap requires confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials. This study is a Phase I single-arm trial, not a Phase III RCT. While it mentions a planned Phase II randomized trial (ME.17), it does not provide data on any completed Phase III trials confirming efficacy.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports results from the MIMic trial, a multicenter, single-arm Phase I safety trial evaluating oral FMT combined with anti-PD1 therapy in 20 patients with advanced melanoma. The study found that the combination was safe and associated with an objective response rate (ORR) of 65%, median progression-free survival (mPFS) of 29.6 months, and median overall survival (mOS) of 52.8 months. These outcomes were compared favorably to historical randomized controlled trials (RCTs) of anti-PD1 monotherapy. The authors explicitly state that the sample size was small, there was no control arm, and the results are hypothesis-generating. The study identifies a subsequent randomized Phase II Canadian study (ME.17, NCT06623461) designed to evaluate the potential benefit of this intervention.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::838e53ce99defdb274a4f6da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0577\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8ad5be629a298899c0672c74\",\n          \"snapshot::d94654cea34f2583334f29d6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3170d76df87bfb377320ebc6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::833ddf71a11d978e6fce42b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bce53def04698b2385f517a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a review article, the approach involves a critical appraisal of published literature rather than primary data generation. The authors systematically discuss: 1) Preclinical models identifying key bacterial species; 2) Clinical correlations between stool microbiome composition and ICI outcomes; 3) The impact of antibiotics on survival; 4) Specific intervention trials for prebiotics (dietary fiber), probiotics (CBM588, SER-401), and FMT across different tumor types and lines of therapy. They compare results against historical benchmarks and note limitations such as small sample sizes and heterogeneity in trial designs.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb889e487c6bdd1e356372eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of current evidence linking gut microbiome composition to ICI efficacy in solid tumors, categorizing strategies into prebiotics, probiotics, and FMT.\",\n          \"limits\": \"The field lacks large, definitive randomized trials; most evidence comes from small phase I/II studies or retrospective analyses. The review acknowledges that widespread adoption is premature and mechanisms are not fully elucidated.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b772a2563878345157adfe5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Highlights the complexity of microbial effects, noting that both low and excessively high levels of certain bacteria (e.g., Akkermansia) may be suboptimal, suggesting a need for balanced composition rather than single-species enrichment.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Does not provide causal mechanistic proof for all observed associations; many findings are correlative.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d8a1dbcd8a5f17abeac1cf9e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific ongoing trials and future directions, such as stratification based on baseline microbiome composition.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Cannot predict the success of future trials or resolve uncertainties regarding universal vs. personalized application of microbiome therapies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6a77b53a16f1542d379f2044\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical and observational clinical studies\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific bacterial taxa (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) correlate with favorable responses to anti-PD-1 antibodies, while antibiotic use before/during ICI initiation is associated with higher primary resistance and shorter overall survival.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0ee1f89ce9752d4834de52d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical trials of Probiotics (CBM588)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Small prospective trials in mRCC showed significantly improved progression-free survival and overall response rates when CBM588 was added to ICI-based regimens, though sample sizes were limited (n=30 per arm).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c04267c3ab6c013d3e805b57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical trials of FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT combined with ICIs showed encouraging results in refractory melanoma (ORR 30%) and frontline settings for melanoma (ORR 65%), NSCLC (ORR 77%), and RCC (12-month PFS improved from 35% to 67%). However, benefits were not consistent in all contexts, such as microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer where outcomes were comparable to historical controls without FMT.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0fbe205ee9cf1e2729d24317\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Biomarker development\",\n          \"finding\": \"The TOPOSCORE biomarker, integrating Akkermansia with other microbial groups, showed significant correlation with overall survival in cohorts of mNSCLC, mRCC, and urothelial carcinoma.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c47c382f8fcd311029400a6b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::391636a4ef531dc3e03166fa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The paper addresses the growing interest in microbiome modulation as a therapeutic strategy to overcome resistance to ICIs in oncology. It seeks to summarize current evidence regarding which microbial species are beneficial or detrimental, how disruption affects outcomes, and whether specific modulation strategies (prebiotics, probiotics, FMT) show clinical benefit.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d466f3497f07b41883777b89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interplay between the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in patients with solid malignancies, specifically advanced melanoma, metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), and metastatic non–small cell lung cancer (mNSCLC). It covers preclinical evidence, clinical observations of microbial associations, and various modulation strategies including prebiotics, probiotics, and fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8bf43a9c720757c7c1b29667\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This article is a narrative review that critically appraises existing studies on how gut microbiome modulation can enhance the efficacy of ICIs in solid tumors. It synthesizes preclinical findings linking specific bacterial taxa to treatment response, discusses the negative impact of antibiotic-induced dysbiosis, and evaluates clinical data from trials involving dietary interventions, probiotic supplementation, and FMT. The authors highlight promising signals but emphasize the lack of large-scale randomized controlled trials needed to establish standard of care.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::067e4c00a3d6d84463a180d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Most clinical data are from small, non-randomized, or early-phase trials. Cannot definitively prove causality for all associations. The review itself notes that large RCTs are lacking.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence showing that specific gut microbes (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved ICI outcomes, while antibiotic disruption correlates with poorer survival. Provides ORR and PFS data from FMT and probiotic trials in melanoma, RCC, and NSCLC.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2cbbb1c1818351f5263e174a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The review is descriptive and does not present new mechanistic experiments. Mechanisms are largely inferred from preclinical models or translational analyses of small cohorts. Does not provide detailed molecular pathway analysis.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discusses potential mechanisms indirectly through observed effects: e.g., dietary fiber enhancing postbiotic production, vancomycin preconditioning disrupting immunity, and intratumoral Gammaproteobacteria hindering gemcitabine response. Mentions the role of short-chain fatty acids.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::193d9a5f14c622a00b8fa4ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"The review establishes the rationale for microbiome modulation, citing preclinical discoveries (Sivan et al., Vétizou et al.) and the general interplay between gut microbiome and immunity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::442c140f14f35073e88fda05\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Contrasting results: FMT worked well in melanoma/RCC/NSCLC but showed no added benefit over historical controls in microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::53f032c1944a751907a8ef5a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of small sample sizes, lack of standardization in FMT donors (responders vs. healthy volunteers), and conflicting data on single-biomarker utility (Akkermansia levels).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e457f01ec0c174b1c1a5c20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative summary, not a systematic meta-analysis. Do not treat its conclusions as definitive consensus.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2f55750dba533f27c47b404c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Clinical trial results cited are primarily from Phase I/II studies with small sample sizes; avoid overstating efficacy as established fact.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b246c5f5e588d398b2174b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic claims are largely based on preclinical models or correlational clinical data; distinguish between observed association and proven mechanism.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::895c49a50d8426f8ea373423\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review explicitly states that large randomized trials are lacking; do not imply that these strategies are standard of care.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b149a9f56e3601f28672e249\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::305d60fcaf083e06084ff435\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::359826ab9a67fb8e61f905ac\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::059d3f40b149cda601516251\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作为一篇叙述性综述，作者基于现有文献（包括观察性研究、临床试验、指南和机制研究），系统性地归纳了影响ICI疗效的非肿瘤内在因素（如炎症、微生物群、生活方式），并据此分类讨论了各类整合肿瘤学干预手段（营养、运动、微生物调节、补充剂、心理干预、草药等）的证据等级、潜在机制及临床建议。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::65d778840757126d567a9fcb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了整合肿瘤学策略支持ICI治疗的全面概览，特别强调了从“预测”转向“响应行动”的转化医学思路（如利用炎症标志物指导干预时机）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所引用的多数证据来自观察性研究或小样本试验，缺乏大规模随机对照试验（RCT）的确证；对于许多干预措施（如特定益生菌、中草药、身心疗法），其因果效应和最佳剂量/方案尚未明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec1a190580c88365600c5078\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了医疗大麻在ICI治疗中的潜在负面信号，以及维生素D补充的具体获益阈值。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对某些新兴领域（如真菌疗法、具体中药方剂）仅提及预临床证据或正在进行的试验，缺乏直接的临床结果支持。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8860efde974ad499faa50edc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"成人实体瘤患者，基线或治疗期间\",\n          \"finding\": \"系统性炎症标志物（如NLR, CRP, LIPI）升高与较差的ICI预后相关；CRP flare（治疗后初期CRP升高后下降）可能与良好的免疫反应相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::86bbfc61afb51265803c7da4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"饮食干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"摄入至少20g/天膳食纤维的地中海式饮食与晚期黑色素瘤患者的无进展生存期（PFS）延长相关；避免超加工食品和高糖饮料有助于维持健康的肠道微生物群。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2b876bfc226ae5503a44cc9d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"运动干预\",\n          \"finding\": \"回顾性研究显示，接受仑伐替尼联合抗PD-1治疗的肝细胞癌患者中，活跃运动组比久坐组具有更长的总生存期（OS）和无进展生存期（PFS）；但针对ICI的特异性RCT数据仍有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cd932a80a64060bbecc8f4d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肠道微生物群调节\",\n          \"finding\": \"粪菌移植（FMT）可使部分ICI耐药患者产生客观缓解；口服活体生物疗法（LBTs，如MRx0518, CBM588）显示出免疫调节和增强ICI疗效的潜力，且可能减轻胃肠道irAEs。益生菌效果存在争议，取决于菌株特异性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5523d14b166740380cf649fd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"维生素D补充\",\n          \"finding\": \"PROVIDENCE前瞻性研究表明，将血清25-羟基维生素D水平补充至≥75 nmol/l可显著延长晚期癌症患者的OS，降低疾病控制失败风险，并减少甲状腺irAEs的发生率。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb25fb43e17b2e5e04ea16bb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"医疗大麻使用\",\n          \"finding\": \"一项前瞻性观察性研究发现，医疗大麻的使用与时间至肿瘤进展缩短及总生存期（OS）显著降低相关；尽管另一项小样本研究未达统计学显著差异，但鉴于潜在风险，建议谨慎使用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6cc18e204e7d4239bb2970d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"慢性压力与身心疗法\",\n          \"finding\": \"治疗前的情绪困扰和慢性心理压力被证实是黑色素瘤和非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者ICI疗效差的独立预后因素；身心疗法（瑜伽、太极等）在此领域尚需进一步临床研究。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::007442678434e9f15c3c399d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4e0135b3ab53a9ab9a02a85e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"随着ICI在实体瘤中的广泛应用，如何识别并利用低成本、低毒性的整合肿瘤学策略来支持ICI治疗，以提高疗效、改善预后并最小化免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da56249308f3600ef240290b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"成人实体瘤患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗期间，整合肿瘤学（Integrative Oncology, IO）策略的应用与潜力。涵盖营养、运动、微生物组调节、补充剂及心理干预等支持性措施。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4c3b4df33ba4e1c3759e973b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在评估整合肿瘤学策略在支持成人实体瘤患者进行免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗中的作用和实际应用。文章指出，除了肿瘤内在因素外，宿主相关的系统性炎症、肠道微生物群、饮食和遗传背景显著影响ICI疗效。综述梳理了当前有前景的支持性干预措施，包括地中海式高纤维饮食、规律运动、活体生物疗法、减少质子泵抑制剂（PPI）和抗生素使用、维生素D补充等，并警告医疗大麻可能带来的生存期缩短风险。文章强调通过多模式术前康复（prehabilitation）和术中支持来优化患者状态，以改善治疗效果并最小化不良反应。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bb8a877a73f48d88979a6319\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些发现主要基于观察性研究和小型试点研究，因果关系的确立程度不一；不同癌症类型（主要是黑色素瘤、NSCLC、HCC）的结果不能直接泛化到所有实体瘤。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群调节ICI疗效的临床证据链：包括FMT诱导缓解的案例、LBTs（如MRx0518, CBM588）增强疗效和减轻irAEs的数据、以及饮食纤维（>20g/d）与PFS延长的关联。同时指出了益生菌效果的菌株特异性和矛盾性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05ca21c8bcfac14fc5240f7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制部分多为动物模型或体外研究推论（如L. reuteri的机制），临床人体内的确切分子通路细节在所给材料中未完全展开；压力机制主要基于动物研究和人类相关性观察，直接因果链条需结合其他文献验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐述了微生物群影响ICI疗效的部分机制路径：包括短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）驱动CD4/CD8 T细胞激活、促进IFN表达；特定菌株代谢物（如I3A）促进肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞浸润；以及系统性炎症（IL-6, IL-8）作为负向调节因子。同时提到了慢性压力通过HPA轴/SNS改变肿瘤微环境（TME）的间接机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdcc90032eecfb78a3c379e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述定义了整合肿瘤学，概述了术前康复（prehabilitation）的概念，以及除微生物群外的其他支持策略（运动、维生素D、大麻禁忌）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::73bacb1e27b3dd0772f60a33\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"医疗大麻导致OS缩短的观察性数据；维生素D补充降低irAEs的数据；VAC（槲寄生提取物）的安全性数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e33d2c01d3eeb43ff349d0b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要聚焦于成人实体瘤，特别是黑色素瘤、NSCLC、肾细胞癌和肝癌，结果可能不适用于血液肿瘤或其他罕见实体瘤。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ea60aed65bb9454bb5fc743c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关于肠道微生物群的许多结论来自观察性研究或小样本试验，需谨慎推断因果关系；例如，饮食纤维的益处可能与整体健康生活方式有关，而非单一成分作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3c4cf0377facebfc49c3301e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"益生菌的效果具有高度的菌株特异性，综述中提到的矛盾结果（Spencer vs Bender）提示不能一概而论地推荐或禁止所有益生菌。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bdae353a87824de36024429d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"医疗大麻的负面结果主要来自观察性研究，可能存在混杂因素（如疼痛严重程度、吸烟史），尽管综述建议谨慎，但不能视为绝对的禁忌证证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d57d12c2e39a9e49dadda7b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0343\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::aee91b6d254c74392754ffb3\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef240eea79c14842a161ea01\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70aec41e07d695a8eac67632\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::68c3a7f85812b14bab2835b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一项嵌入在随机对照III期临床试验（JCOG2007, NIPPON）中的辅助生物标志物研究。研究设计包括：1. 队列选择：从入组的295名患者中筛选出270名提供基线粪便样本的患者进行分析。2. 分组比较：比较两种一线治疗方案（PC vs NIC）。3. 微生物分析：对基线粪便样本进行16S rDNA测序，进行α/β多样性分析和LEfSe差异丰度分析。4. 临床关联分析：将微生物特征（多样性、特定菌属丰度）与主要临床终点（OS超过12或18个月的亚群区分、总体OS、≥Grade 4严重不良事件发生率）进行统计学关联分析，并进行了按治疗方案的亚组分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc5ac621424e5a680d638cf3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了在大型III期临床试验背景下，肠道微生物群与NSCLC化疗-免疫治疗预后及安全性关联的具体实证数据。识别了特定的细菌属（如Fusicatenibacter, Butyricicoccus）作为潜在的预后和安全性标志物，并提示了方案特异性的微生物效应。\",\n          \"limits\": \"仅基于摘要信息，无法评估多变量校正模型的完整性、多重检验校正方法、16S测序的具体流程细节及批次效应处理。结果主要关联观察性，因果机制未阐明。NIC组中Prevotellaceae NK3B31的结果需结合具体统计显著性和置信区间解读。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c86a89535162f292ea1f987\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"整体队列（n=270），根据OS是否超过12或18个月划分的亚群\",\n          \"finding\": \"β多样性分析显示不同生存时间亚群具有不同的微生物结构。LEfSe分析发现，Fusicatenibacter、Butyricicoccus和Blautia在长生存患者中富集。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1057b507eca51d0fcea5f768\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"整体队列，关注严重不良事件（≥ Grade 4 AEs）\",\n          \"finding\": \"较低的微生物α多样性及某些特定菌属的存在与较高的严重AE风险相关。相反，有益菌属（如Fusicatenibacter和Butyricicoccus）的高丰度与较低的严重AE风险相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d2ee193139c04a77bbb7f1c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"按治疗方案分层（NIC臂 vs CP/PC臂）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在NIC组中，Fusicatenibacter和Butyricicoccus的高丰度与更好的OS相关（HR分别为0.56和0.52），优于CP组。而在NIC组中，Prevotellaceae NK3B31的高丰度与更高的死亡风险相关（HR=2.33）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3d1546bb5d6cbcbbdd64352c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d32c7c4fc57964f4eca5feb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫治疗改变了NSCLC的治疗格局，但缺乏可靠的生物标志物来指导治疗选择。肠道微生物群虽被视为潜在生物标志物，但其在NSCLC化疗-免疫联合治疗中的具体作用尚不清楚。本研究试图回答：肠道微生物群的组成和多样性是否能预测晚期NSCLC患者在接受不同化疗-免疫联合方案时的预后（OS）和治疗安全性（严重AEs）？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::11588e401bbf4877af15cff5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对无驱动基因改变的晚期非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者，基于JCOG2007（NIPPON）III期临床试验的辅助生物标志物研究。研究对象为接受培美曲塞+铂类化疗联合帕博利珠单抗（PC组）或纳武利尤单抗+伊匹木单抗联合铂类化疗（NIC组）的患者，分析基线粪便样本中的肠道微生物群。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::64bc295bd46b3e9847e3a952\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探索肠道微生物群作为晚期NSCLC化疗-免疫治疗疗效和安全性生物标志物的潜力。研究利用JCOG2007试验中270名有基线粪便样本患者的16S rDNA测序数据，分析了微生物多样性及特定菌属丰度与总生存期（OS）及严重不良事件（AEs）之间的关联。结果显示，微生物结构随生存时间延长而变化，特定产丁酸菌属富集于长生存患者，且与较低的严重AE风险相关；此外，不同治疗方案下微生物对预后的影响存在差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3ca5c85cf380e43b5cfe3c21\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"结果来自NSCLC特定人群，且为观察性关联。NIC组中Prevotellaceae NK3B31显示负面关联，提示微生物效应具有复杂性和情境依赖性。不能直接外推至所有实体瘤或所有ICI单药治疗。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群与ICI疗效关联的临床队列证据。具体发现：Fusicatenibacter和Butyricicoccus的高丰度与更长的OS相关，特别是在NIC（纳武利尤单抗+伊匹木单抗）方案中效果显著（HR 0.56/0.52）。同时，这些菌属也与较低的严重AE风险相关。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::64d85960adb517ce19d05f9c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"本研究未提供直接的机制验证（如动物模型、体外实验或代谢产物测量）。关联不等于因果。方案特异性结果的生物学解释需谨慎，可能涉及药物代谢、免疫微环境改变等多重因素。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物群落结构与临床结局（生存期和毒性）的关联数据，暗示了微生物可能通过调节宿主免疫反应（进而影响疗效和毒性）发挥作用，但未直接测定分子机制。指出了不同免疫检查点阻断策略（PD-1 vs CTLA-4+PD-1）下微生物效应的差异性（方案特异性）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe193bdc0e2868dc90b9e8c9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究背景指出免疫治疗改变了NSCLC治疗格局，但缺乏可靠生物标志物，肠道微生物群被视为潜在标志物。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c6d8c3fa05acba612e1717fa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"NIC组中Prevotellaceae NK3B31高丰度与高死亡风险（HR=2.33）相关，而Fusicatenibacter等则有益。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b2e0449447121ab035839cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"结论建议将肠道微生物谱分析整合到临床实践中以优化一线治疗策略。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1cedc9d5eb5f2f3606fcdc9a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为观察性附属研究，关联结果不能直接推断因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf4fe4efa643acabaa4c1e7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"结果基于16S rDNA测序，分辨率限于属水平，且未提供功能基因组或代谢组数据，机制解释受限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::97b487409f4caf96753a443e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"NIC组中Prevotellaceae NK3B31的负面结果需警惕，可能与样本量、统计效力或特定亚群特征有关，不宜简单概括为该类菌普遍有害。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1f2b75a988619767a272f17b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"方案特异性结果（NIC vs PC）的差异可能受药物相互作用、患者基线特征或其他混杂因素影响，需谨慎解读。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6dfb0494d7ff39f7b74ab413\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"摘要未提供详细的统计校正方法（如多重检验校正、协变量调整），影响结果的确信度评估。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::66a42283328586c4e93ab1e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study highlights regimen-specific effects, noting that microbial associations with outcomes differed between the PD-1 inhibitor-based regimen (PC) and the dual checkpoint blockade regimen (NIC). It identifies specific bacterial genera (Fusicatenibacter, Butyricicoccus, Blautia) enriched in patients with longer OS (>12 or >18 months). It also notes that lower microbial alpha diversity and presence of certain taxa were linked to a higher risk of serious (≥ Grade 4) AEs. The authors conclude that gut microbiota may serve as a biomarker for chemo-immunotherapy in advanced NSCLC.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_3636101ad7\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"direct\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"fulfilled\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports on the JCOG2007 trial, a completed phase III randomized controlled trial comparing pembrolizumab plus platinum doublet chemotherapy (PC) and nivolumab-ipilimumab plus platinum doublet chemotherapy (NIC) in treatment-naïve advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients. The trial enrolled 295 patients, with an ancillary biomarker analysis performed on baseline fecal samples from 270 patients using 16S rDNA sequencing. The study found that gut microbiota composition was associated with overall survival (OS) and adverse events (AEs). Specifically, higher abundance of Fusicatenibacter and Butyricicoccus was linked to better OS in the NIC arm compared to the PC arm, and these genera were also associated with a lower risk of serious AEs. Conversely, higher abundance of Prevotellaceae NK3B31 was associated with higher mortality risk in the NIC arm.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::420263f1f2804510d71b896a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study highlights regimen-specific effects, noting that microbial associations with outcomes differed between the PD-1 inhibitor-based regimen (PC) and the dual checkpoint blockade regimen (NIC). It identifies specific bacterial genera (Fusicatenibacter, Butyricicoccus, Blautia) enriched in patients with longer OS (>12 or >18 months). It also notes that lower microbial alpha diversity and presence of certain taxa were linked to a higher risk of serious (≥ Grade 4) AEs. The authors conclude that gut microbiota may serve as a biomarker for chemo-immunotherapy in advanced NSCLC.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_3636101ad7\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"direct\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"fulfilled\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports on the JCOG2007 trial, a completed phase III randomized controlled trial comparing pembrolizumab plus platinum doublet chemotherapy (PC) and nivolumab-ipilimumab plus platinum doublet chemotherapy (NIC) in treatment-naïve advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients. The trial enrolled 295 patients, with an ancillary biomarker analysis performed on baseline fecal samples from 270 patients using 16S rDNA sequencing. The study found that gut microbiota composition was associated with overall survival (OS) and adverse events (AEs). Specifically, higher abundance of Fusicatenibacter and Butyricicoccus was linked to better OS in the NIC arm compared to the PC arm, and these genera were also associated with a lower risk of serious AEs. Conversely, higher abundance of Prevotellaceae NK3B31 was associated with higher mortality risk in the NIC arm.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5f53fd31bc8e45bdb2ad45d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0585\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_empty\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_challenge_or_login\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b48b92078f04672f80082d00\",\n          \"snapshot::33eb067b80204dcb68c3dbc6\",\n          \"snapshot::4debf19bd260cc81e2d804ee\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::15061913954a3eb4314bfe63\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2ee5bcc70934484c1c501b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4105e603a60c7ac2142dbb4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a narrative synthesis of literature from microbiology, immunology, and oncology. They organized the content into thematic sections: introduction to the gut-lung axis, alterations in microbiota composition and metabolism in lung cancer patients, microbial biomarkers for early detection, prediction of immunotherapy response, modulation of drug efficacy, microbiota-targeted therapeutic interventions, and mechanistic insights. The review integrates findings from clinical studies, animal models, and multi-omics analyses to construct a cohesive understanding of the gut-lung axis in lung cancer.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0920b699f4612e204bfc385c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive overview of the gut-lung axis in lung cancer, linking specific microbial taxa and metabolites to clinical outcomes in diagnosis and immunotherapy.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not present new primary data or perform a systematic meta-analysis. The causal relationships described are largely inferred from correlative clinical studies and preclinical models, which may vary across populations.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5b8b569e7ef00dbb86acdf1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial signatures (e.g., A. muciniphila, SCFA producers) and metabolic profiles as potential biomarkers for predicting ICI response.\",\n          \"limits\": \"The generalizability of these biomarkers depends on the heterogeneity of patient cohorts and sequencing methodologies used in the cited studies, which are not standardized in this review.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0807e5f5e9cb71aaf08bbdf2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Discusses therapeutic interventions like FMT and probiotics as adjuncts to cancer therapy, highlighting their potential to overcome resistance.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Clinical translation faces challenges including interindividual variability, lack of standardized protocols for FMT/probiotics, and long-term safety concerns, which are noted but not resolved.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::222b7c85cacaaec66836ff67\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"In lung cancer patients compared to healthy controls\",\n          \"finding\": \"Patients exhibit dysbiosis characterized by increased abundance of Ruminococcus, Enterobacteriaceae, Lachnospiraceae, and decreased levels of Faecalibacterium, Bifidobacterium, and Veillonella. Metabolic profiles show reduced SCFA production and increased lactate.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::87afa3d0ef630783c4ccd7f5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"For early detection of lung cancer\",\n          \"finding\": \"A panel of 13 microbial biomarkers was identified with high diagnostic potential, achieving an AUC of 92.4% in discovery and 67.7% in validation cohorts using a Patient Discrimination Index (PDI).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::759a8bfc798893a613e65496\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Predicting response to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Baseline presence of Akkermansia muciniphila, Faecalibacterium spp., and Clostridiales correlates with improved ICI outcomes. Higher levels of acetate, propionate, and butyrate are associated with prolonged progression-free survival. A TOPOSCORE integrating species interaction groups and A. muciniphila abundance predicts individual responses.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9670e0aad2a912986441368f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Impact of antibiotics and probiotics on ICI efficacy\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use prior to ICI therapy is associated with reduced overall survival and impaired efficacy. Probiotic supplementation (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Clostridium butyricum) may enhance ICI efficacy and improve survival outcomes in NSCLC patients.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8f84bfea0480caaf0aa351c6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanisms of action\",\n          \"finding\": \"Gut microbes modulate lung immunity via metabolites (SCFAs), antigen presentation, and immune cell trafficking. Specific bacteria like A. muciniphila can translocate to tumor tissues, restructure the intratumoral ecosystem, and restore exhausted CD8+ T cells, enhancing anti-PD-1 therapy efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9f6defcbd1442747892e1088\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a820b4e3b48d5a4789dc4f56\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To synthesize existing evidence regarding how the gut microbiome influences lung cancer pathogenesis and treatment efficacy, particularly in the context of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), and to identify potential therapeutic strategies and biomarkers derived from this interaction.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff2426568d2acbf08a5a2f34\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut-lung axis in the context of lung cancer, specifically examining non-small cell lung carcinoma (NSCLC) and small cell lung carcinoma. It covers pathogenesis, early detection biomarkers, mechanisms of immune modulation, and therapeutic interventions including immunotherapy response prediction and microbiota-targeted treatments.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d82e26dfd79d7f969e7a4466\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This is a narrative review synthesizing current knowledge on the role of the gut microbiome in lung cancer development, diagnosis, and treatment. It outlines the bidirectional communication between intestinal microbiota and pulmonary health via immune, neural, and metabolic pathways. The paper highlights microbial signatures predictive of disease and therapy response, discusses microbiota-targeted interventions such as probiotics and fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), and elucidates mechanistic insights into microbial-immune crosstalk. It aims to provide a comprehensive framework for leveraging the gut microbiome in personalized lung cancer management.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9d858348408b4d384f36bfad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Focuses primarily on lung cancer; while it mentions other cancers briefly, the detailed evidence is lung-specific. Causal inference is limited to observational associations and preclinical models.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the correlation between specific gut microbiota compositions (e.g., A. muciniphila, SCFA-producing bacteria) and improved clinical outcomes in solid tumors treated with ICIs. It also notes that antibiotic use negatively impacts ICI efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e20b73e0dbfc7da743e07d59\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are often derived from mouse models or inferred from human correlative data. The review acknowledges complexity and multiple interacting pathways rather than a single linear mechanism.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Elaborates on mechanisms including: 1) Metabolite-mediated regulation (SCFAs, acetate, butyrate influencing immune cell function); 2) Immune cell priming and trafficking (dendritic cells, T-cell activation, CD8+ T cell infiltration); 3) Direct translocation of bacteria to tumor sites; 4) Modulation of bile acid metabolism affecting Treg migration.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6ad4bdb640b37eff993589ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Description of the bidirectional network connecting intestinal microbiota with pulmonary health via immune, neural, and metabolic pathways.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b85fd21d4830403e343f172\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of probiotics, prebiotics, FMT, and dietary interventions as adjuncts to immunotherapy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e20f7ca707e5863923e328e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Brief mentions of melanoma, renal, and bladder carcinomas regarding antibiotic impact on ICIs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a29b5a8633f2887be3f5fdf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis, not a systematic review or meta-analysis; therefore, it does not provide pooled effect sizes or rigorous statistical aggregation of all available evidence.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::963355d7afe963db113a6718\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic claims are based on preclinical (mouse) models or correlative clinical studies; causal relationships in humans are not definitively proven within this text.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::744ca1daaa8346a24e399902\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The term 'solid tumours' in the user's plan is broader than the paper's primary focus on lung cancer; users must extrapolate carefully when applying lung-specific findings to other solid tumors.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9f82b783e138f3f0e16d8519\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::55488d84dbb359a3345c319f\",\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c38b942335c5be7de0f70e4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0297\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::7b48398ecbc866361ef2c262\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f268dc5a31e6509082426a96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::915832e3eeeb6c7bf46b4dc7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c9458faeedb93aae1481ce2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究采用多步骤计算与实验结合的策略：1) 利用TCGA bulk RNA-seq数据和ImmuCellAI去卷积算法，鉴定与免疫浸润负相关或正相关的TIIMGs；2) 使用L1000高通量筛选平台，针对TIIMGs筛选739种化合物的转录组扰动效应，并通过drug-to-cell recall验证；3) 在CT26小鼠模型中进行体内给药，收集肿瘤组织进行scRNA-seq，利用NMF算法从肿瘤细胞中提取异质性程序并聚类为12个MPs；4) 开发MP评分算法（结合Cluster 1激活与Cluster 2抑制的加权）量化TME重塑程度；5) 基于MP评分优先选择候选药物（oxypurinol及其前体allopurinol），通过流式细胞术、LC-MS/MS检测肌苷水平、体外共培养及体内协同实验验证机制；6) 回顾性分析人类膀胱癌患者队列中抗痛风药与抗PD-1治疗的生存关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::894b59684f5f72f52dd6cd62\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"建立了首个基于单细胞分辨率的药物诱导TME重塑量化框架（resTMe），定义了12个TME元程序（MPs）和MP评分算法，为预测药物-免疫疗法协同作用提供了新工具。\",\n          \"limits\": \"核心scRNA-seq数据仅来源于小鼠模型（CT26），缺乏人源类器官或PDX模型的直接验证，限制了框架在人类复杂TME中的直接外推性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ef0876af1bde6e00dba83aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"发现了别嘌醇（Allopurinol）作为抗PD-1疗法的潜在增效剂，阐明了其通过嘌呤补救途径增加肌苷分泌、增强肿瘤免疫原性和T细胞功能的分子机制。\",\n          \"limits\": \"机制验证主要在体外细胞系和小鼠模型中进行；人类临床证据仅来自小样本（n=50）、单中心的回顾性观察性研究，存在混杂因素风险，需前瞻性临床试验确认。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b30b08eb075f61505bc09741\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了MDSCs的耗竭是响应性TME的关键标志物，并揭示了低剂量药物可能通过非细胞毒性机制重塑TME以促进免疫浸润。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于其他候选药物（如epirubicin, vemurafenib）的具体分子机制阐述不如AP深入；不同药物对特定免疫亚群的影响差异较大，尚未形成统一的普适性规则。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d89ef3a629b3edc8f1d5680d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"8种癌症类型TCGA数据分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"鉴定出肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），其中COAD拥有最多的dpGenes（792个），KIRC最少，揭示了不同癌症间TME调控网络的异质性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f9f47d7274d6ce123558914d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"L1000平台筛选739种化合物\",\n          \"finding\": \"识别出54种在多癌种中重复出现的候选药物，主要靶向CDKs、HDAC1、PI3K等通路。低剂量处理更倾向于产生非细胞毒性的免疫调节效应，而高剂量常伴随免疫抑制。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13b75fe0affb6edd8981d33b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"CT26小鼠模型scRNA-seq分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"药物处理导致肿瘤细胞比例下降，免疫细胞（特别是巨噬细胞、DCs）浸润增加，但MDSCs显著减少。oxypurinol表现出最强的TME重塑能力，显著降低MDSCs并增加抗原呈递相关细胞。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59223824372c97eeae14a917\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"MP评分算法应用\",\n          \"finding\": \"定义了12个MPs，其中Cluster 2（含MPs 1,3,6,8,10,12）与抗原加工和呈递通路高度相关。oxypurinol获得最高MP评分，提示其具有最强的TME重塑潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f486a10e036032c79861cfc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Allopurinol (AP) 联合抗PD-1治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"AP通过抑制黄嘌呤脱氢酶（XDH）增加肌苷合成并分泌至胞外，肌苷上调肿瘤细胞MHC I类和PD-L1表达，增强CD8+ T细胞介导的细胞毒性。在CT26模型中，AP联合抗PD-1实现4/6小鼠完全治愈。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5b36a5dbcaf7631b8b07425\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"人类膀胱癌回顾性队列（n=50）\",\n          \"finding\": \"在接受抗PD-1治疗的膀胱癌患者中，同时服用抗痛风药物（如AP或febuxostat）的患者组（n=7）的总生存期（OS）显著优于未服用组（n=43）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a9ba68194211f72c5ff2998\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::309f1460bfa5781083656af4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"如何在复杂的肿瘤微环境中系统性地识别能够增强免疫疗法疗效的药物组合？目前缺乏量化药物诱导TME重塑的系统框架，且难以预测哪些非抗癌药物可作为免疫治疗的增效剂。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::732cd6b3522e68e0af8deae5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究聚焦于实体瘤（以小鼠结肠癌CT26模型和人类膀胱癌队列为主）的肿瘤微环境（TME），探讨药物诱导的TME重塑如何影响免疫检查点抑制剂（如抗PD-1/PD-L1）的疗效。研究对象包括8种癌症类型的TCGA数据、739种免疫调节化合物、小鼠体内的单细胞转录组数据以及临床回顾性队列。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82ddeb3927993c2d17aa2d61\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决缺乏系统性框架来量化药物诱导的TME重塑的问题。作者首先通过TCGA数据和ImmuCellAI算法鉴定了肿瘤细胞特异性免疫浸润调节基因（TIIMGs），并利用L1000平台筛选出能显著调控这些基因的化合物。随后，在小鼠CT26肿瘤模型中，通过单细胞RNA测序（scRNA-seq）分析了多种药物处理后的TME变化，识别出12个与TME重塑相关的元程序（Meta-programs, MPs）。基于MP富集情况开发了MP评分算法，用于量化TME对药物的响应程度。该算法成功鉴定出别嘌醇（Allopurinol, AP），一种痛风药物，发现其能通过促进肌苷（inosine）的合成与分泌，上调肿瘤细胞的MHC I类和PD-L1表达，从而增强CD8+ T细胞的杀伤活性。在体内实验中，低剂量AP联合抗PD-1治疗实现了4/6的小鼠完全肿瘤清除。此外，一项包含50名膀胱癌患者的回顾性研究显示，接受抗痛风药物治疗的患者在抗PD-1治疗下的总生存期显著优于未使用者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::29799ff01275a5961dfa4b1f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该研究未涉及肠道菌群，因此不能直接回答菌群如何调制ICI疗效的问题，只能作为平行机制或交互作用的潜在背景。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了非微生物来源的代谢物（肌苷）增强ICI疗效的证据。研究发现别嘌醇通过增加肌苷分泌，增强CD8+ T细胞功能，这与某些肠道菌群代谢产物（如丁酸盐、次级胆汁酸）调节免疫微环境的机制形成互补或对比视角。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cc0bd417229ac67f8358b8ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅限于别嘌醇-肌苷轴，不能推广为所有ICI增效剂的通用机制。人类证据仅为相关性，因果链条在人体中尚待确证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了别嘌醇增强ICI疗效的具体分子机制：抑制XDH -> 增加肌苷 -> 上调MHC I/PD-L1 -> 增强T细胞杀伤。同时指出MDSCs减少是响应性TME的标志。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ce5af135f0f54a3f33ded5af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"基于小鼠模型数据，人类组织中MDSCs的功能异质性更大，需谨慎外推。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了MDSCs耗竭作为ICI响应生物标志物的实证支持。在scRNA-seq分析中，响应性TME显著特征为MDSCs比例降低。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::911473103290b79cdeaaf990\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"别嘌醇（痛风药）被鉴定为抗PD-1增效剂，并在回顾性临床队列中显示生存获益。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d608d3703ed2d823c7784427\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MP评分算法和12个元程序的定义，量化了抗原呈递、盐应激反应等生物学过程在药物处理后的变化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c11e7ad8dda921d2c87e471\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"AP处理导致肌苷大量分泌，增强OT-I T细胞对B16-OVA肿瘤的杀伤力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a50fe6e4b2c8671f940ffb9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的核心对象是小鼠模型和人类膀胱癌回顾性队列，未直接研究肠道菌群。在将其用于回答‘菌群如何调制ICI’问题时，必须明确其作为‘非菌群代谢机制’的对比或补充角色，而非直接证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::78212dc609fe90c3f037d637\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类临床数据仅为小样本回顾性观察（n=50），存在选择偏倚和混杂因素，不能作为因果关系的确凿证据，仅能作为假设生成的线索。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::125505f32ce06e79d94ca2a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"别嘌醇的机制特异性强（肌苷轴），不能将其效果泛化为所有代谢调节药物或所有ICI增效剂的共同机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c058dc0771a54f0d89db5a07\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"MP评分和元程序是基于小鼠CT26模型定义的，在不同癌症类型或人源模型中的适用性需进一步验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::50e3812052714d3b820c4e72\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93b0bc69434a90089e6079fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study developed a meta-program (MP) scoring algorithm based on scRNA-seq data from mouse tumors to quantify TME remodeling, identifying myeloid-derived suppressor cell (MDSC) depletion as a hallmark of responsive TMEs. It established a resource (scIMD) and web tool (resTMe) for screening immunomodulatory drugs. The analysis covered eight cancer types for gene identification but performed in vivo validation primarily in the CT26 colon carcinoma model.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_2\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-h4sdftel\\\\source_units\\\\SU03_search_candidate_7df1939f2d\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"This material does not provide the absolute physiological concentration of inosine within the human tumor microenvironment (TME); the concentration data reported is from mouse cell culture supernatants. Furthermore, it does not report a direct statistical correlation between measured human TME inosine levels and ICI efficacy (e.g., ORR, PFS, OS). The human clinical evidence provided is an association between gout medication usage (as a proxy for inosine elevation) and survival, not a correlation based on quantified inosine metabolite levels in patient tissues or fluids. The study explicitly notes its limitation that drug scRNA-seq data were derived from mouse models.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study investigated the synergistic effect of allopurinol (AP) with anti-PD-1 therapy. In mouse CT26 cell cultures, LC-MS/MS analysis showed AP treatment increased extracellular inosine levels by approximately 500 to 1000-fold in supernatants, while cell lysate levels remained unchanged, indicating active export. Mechanistically, AP inhibits xanthine dehydrogenase (XDH), elevating hypoxanthine which is converted to inosine via the salvage pathway. In vivo, AP combined with anti-PD-1 achieved tumor-free outcomes in 4/6 mice. In a retrospective human cohort of 50 bladder cancer patients receiving anti-PD-1 therapy, the 7 patients concurrently taking gout medications (AP or febuxostat) showed significantly better overall survival compared to the 43 patients who did not. The authors propose that elevated inosine enhances tumor immunogenicity (upregulating MHC class I and PD-L1) and supports T-cell function.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::533541e5da218bf180bf8879\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0593\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-d48cd64bd12b302ad2ba\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-95bd9a77b14edf06222c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a7194a689f46f19f0fc9\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-c44cb221036f78d05573\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"missing\": [\n                \"jitc-14-3-g001.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g002.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g003.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g004.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g005.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-g006.jpg\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s001.docx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s002.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s003.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s004.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s005.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s006.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s007.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s008.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s009.xlsx\",\n                \"jitc-14-3-s010.tif\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"graphic_members_unmatched\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementary_bundle_had_no_safe_matching_images\",\n              \"status\": \"unparsed\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::253f9e6877830f43e32548d1\",\n          \"snapshot::8c09d88d34c8b87066266283\",\n          \"snapshot::4f1fac3cb1126bd412aa5f23\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bb6ad04fca560d182cec1f4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::23b203078daf59896544114b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f68ab6ce48799e6ca1058cd3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的IIa期篮子试验设计。纳入标准包括ICI治疗后疾病进展、ECOG评分0-1及可测量病灶。供体需为ICI长期响应者（>12个月响应）。干预措施包括基线后第1周和第5周通过结肠镜进行两次FMT，随后在第14、30、78周可通过灌肠进行最多三次补充FMT。ICI治疗保持不变或重新引入。主要终点评估安全性和ORR（基于iRECIST）。次要终点包括可行性、临床获益率、无进展生存期（PFS）、总生存期（OS）、微生物定植（16S rRNA测序）、免疫反应（质谱流式细胞术分析PBMCs）及生物标志物（血清细胞因子）。统计分析采用描述性统计、Kaplan-Meier生存分析及Cox比例风险模型探索免疫特征与预后的关联，未进行多重检验校正。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::35e4bb77f5eebd2aa771b705\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，使用ICI响应者供体的FMT是安全和可行的。提供了关于FMT后微生物定植动力学（短暂性）和系统性免疫景观（髓系抑制与T细胞活化）的详细生物标志物数据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量小（n=12），试验因入组缓慢提前终止。单臂设计无法确立因果关系，缺乏对照组。未能实现预期的临床疗效（无ORR），限制了对其机制解释的确定性。结果可能受到快速进展性疾病背景的影响，未能在足够长的时间内观察FMT的潜在延迟效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::59a3a7b73308240f96ffb39c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"12名ICI耐药晚期实体瘤患者，接受来自ICI响应者的FMT联合ICI治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT安全性良好，无严重FMT相关不良事件导致停药，但50%患者出现免疫相关不良事件（irAEs），多数为轻度。客观缓解率（ORR）为0%，中位PFS为1.5个月，中位OS为10.1个月。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::da136020eae35e8a2dfc6af1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"微生物组分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"首次FMT后一周，大多数受体的微生物组向供体方向偏移（定植成功），但这种相似性在后续时间点大多下降，表明定植多为暂时性。仅1名获得临床获益的患者实现了持久的供体-受体微生物相似性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0836a8c74dab91d3a0b4f4ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"免疫微环境分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"基线时高度分化的T细胞环境（CD8+效应记忆T细胞和TEMRA）与改善的PFS和OS相关；而髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型预后较差。CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平随时间增加，高水平的CD14+单核细胞与较短的PFS和OS相关。这些免疫特征与预后的关联在使用ICI治疗起始日期重新计算时依然成立，提示其反映的是宿主对免疫治疗的固有反应能力，而非FMT的直接因果效应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa9a46960936e1395aed9137\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bbf51165ebd9be173e979c8e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"早期研究表明FMT可能逆转ICI耐药，但其适用性在其他肿瘤类型中尚不明确，且关于患者选择、供体选择及给药方案的问题仍未解决。本研究试图回答：在ICI耐药的晚期实体瘤患者中，重复FMT是否安全可行，以及是否能通过微生物定植和免疫重塑来恢复ICI的疗效。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb7c28aa6d5a8423ece0135\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤（黑色素瘤、头颈部鳞癌、肾细胞癌、微卫星不稳定性高胰腺癌）中免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药或进展的患者，评估来自ICI长期响应者的粪菌移植（FMT）联合ICI治疗的安全性和有效性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0ae5567370b869d8e867f54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究是一项单臂IIa期篮子试验（MITRIC），旨在验证通过FMT调节肠道微生物群能否克服已建立的ICI耐药性。研究纳入了12名在转移性阶段对ICI治疗进展的患者，使用ICI长期响应者作为供体，给予患者最多五次FMT（前两次通过结肠镜，后续通过灌肠），并继续原有ICI治疗。主要终点为FMT相关不良事件和客观缓解率（ORR）。结果显示FMT安全性良好，但未能观察到客观肿瘤反应（ORR为0%），仅5名患者达到疾病稳定。尽管缺乏总体疗效证据，研究发现FMT诱导了短暂的微生物定植，且外周血中的免疫细胞特征（如分化T细胞与髓系细胞的平衡）与生存期显著相关，但这些免疫特征似乎更多反映疾病本身状态而非FMT的特异性干预效果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3fb862a9266fa81e78d243db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅适用于ICI耐药/进展人群，不能外推至一线治疗场景。样本量极小，结果可能存在偶然性，但趋势明确。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了FMT在广泛ICI耐药实体瘤队列中的真实世界疗效数据：ORR为0%，中位PFS仅为1.5个月。这表明在非选择性、快速进展的耐药人群中，FMT联合ICI并非有效的挽救疗法。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b6331b5c08533653c791a8b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"免疫关联分析为探索性，未校正多重检验，且缺乏对照组，无法证明FMT改变了这些免疫特征从而改善了预后。仅描述了相关性，未证明因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT干预后系统性免疫景观的变化及其与预后的关联：(1) FMT诱导的微生物定植多为暂时性，仅持久定植者与临床获益相关；(2) 基线高分化T细胞表型预示更好预后，而高髓系细胞（CD14+）和高IL-8水平预示不良预后；(3) 这些免疫特征似乎反映了宿主固有的免疫反应能力，而非FMT直接重塑的结果。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::38d60665b7ae5ef0786b2453\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究讨论了使用ICI响应者作为供体的局限性（微生物组成差异大），以及不同研究间供体数量（单供体vs多供体）对结果的潜在影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fd300138b8a38b7318335545\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"比较了结肠镜给药（前两次）和灌肠给药（后续）的可行性及耐受性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1c0f5c1558648ba8264b5ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的阴性结果主要归因于患者群体的快速进展特性和小样本量，不应将其解读为FMT在所有情况下均无效，而应视为特定情境下的失败尝试。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::602293d8d060926ae50da0a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"免疫生物标志物的发现是探索性的，且可能与ICI治疗本身的效应混淆，需谨慎解读其作为FMT特异性机制的作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d04d310196a133922df7cbd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物定植的暂时性并不必然意味着临床无效，因为唯一获益患者的持久定植提示了两者间的潜在联系，但这仅是个案观察。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::224d056381af07f5414ea73a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"current_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::49d98c7f1b143d31120d9835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"paper_title\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74660f9101b72ae9aef33244\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"plain_text\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::474c7e797e5493a25ea68330\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"prior_question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6a147f41d39b13a9ab869ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\",\n              \"finding\": \"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\",\n            \"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\",\n            \"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6597e99daf38ab354bfeeb09\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"question_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"examples\": [\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Baruch et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R19\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Davar et al. (2021)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R18\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"attribution\": \"Kim et al. (2024)\",\n              \"conditions\": \"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\",\n              \"finding\": \"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\",\n              \"reference_ids\": [\n                \"R20\"\n              ],\n              \"use_in_review\": \"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"explanation\": \"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\n\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\n\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\n\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"remaining_points\": [\n            \"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\",\n            \"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\",\n            \"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe5e2b03a837721c9a331e97\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"deep_read_material\",\n          \"questions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"gap_key\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Supply a concrete, attributed case for the coordinated review.\",\n          \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n          \"question_id\": \"Q01\",\n          \"required_output_ids\": [\n            \"O01\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b8ed4ce6c977fbd7aecee5c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::648ccd951a6ed0f6c928cb17\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The study provides mechanistic insights into why efficacy may be limited in certain contexts. It found that microbiota engraftment from donors was transient in most recipients, with durable engraftment observed only in the single patient who achieved clinical benefit. Mass cytometry analysis revealed that a baseline myeloid-dominant environment (high CD14+ monocytes) and high serum IL-8 were associated with poorer outcomes, while an activated T-cell signature was favorable. These immune features appeared to reflect the host's underlying disease state rather than being directly modified by FMT to improve outcomes. Additionally, the review planning material notes that this study highlights challenges in donor selection (using ICI responders vs healthy donors) and patient heterogeneity (rapidly progressive disease vs stable disease), suggesting that FMT efficacy is highly context-dependent.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"large_scale_rct_results\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260924_microbiome\\\\run01\\\\level1\\\\supplements\\\\large_scale_rct_results\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_fc8af41423\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for confirmation of completed large-scale Phase III randomized controlled trials confirming microbiome intervention efficacy. This study is explicitly identified as a 'single-arm phase IIa' trial. It is neither Phase III nor randomized. Therefore, it does not fulfill the success criterion of providing data from a completed Phase III RCT.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"This study reports the results of the MITRIC trial (NCT05286294), a single-arm, phase IIa basket trial evaluating Fecal Microbiota Transplantation (FMT) from immune checkpoint inhibitor (ICI) responders in patients with advanced cancers progressing on ICIs. The trial enrolled 12 patients across melanoma, head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), renal cell carcinoma (RCC), and microsatellite instability-high pancreatic cancer. The co-primary endpoints were safety and objective response rate (ORR). The study found that FMT was safe and feasible but demonstrated limited clinical activity: no objective responses were observed (ORR 0%), median progression-free survival was 1.5 months, and median overall survival was 10.1 months. Clinical benefit (stable disease >6 months) was achieved in only one patient. The authors conclude that FMT does not support efficacy as a salvage therapy in this non-biomarker-driven, heavily pretreated population.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::748f5657e9b651a2113dca8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::e922ecd2e5e9a27ad505756e\",\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\",\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::acc00d9cd4f644b83ac0cda1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"tool_supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验中 FMT 在 ICI 耐药患者中的 ORR 及 PFS 数据是多少？为何结果为阴性？\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供 FMT 在 ICI 耐药/难治性实体瘤患者中的具体疗效数据（ORR, PFS, OS），并展示阴性结果的具体表现，作为该人群疗效局限性的直接证据。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"MITRIC 试验为一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，纳入 12 名对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药的晚期实体瘤患者（黑色素瘤 n=9, ccRCC n=1, HNSCC n=1, MSI-H 胰腺癌 n=1）。主要终点客观缓解率（ORR）为 0/12（0%），未观察到任何客观缓解（部分或完全缓解）。5 名患者达到最佳稳定疾病（SD），7 名患者进展（PD）。中位无进展生存期（PFS）为 1.5 个月，中位总生存期（OS）为 10.1 个月。仅 1 名黑色素瘤患者获得协议定义的临床获益（SD >6 个月），另 2 名患者出现混合反应（部分病灶消退）。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为 ICI 治疗期间或治疗后进展的晚期实体瘤患者；供体为长期 ICI 响应者；干预措施为结肠镜和灌肠给予的重复 FMT 联合持续或重新引入的 ICI 治疗；评估标准采用 iRECIST。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"作者对 MITRIC 试验结果为阴性的解释主要集中在患者选择、疾病特征及供体匹配等方面：\\\\n1. **患者选择与疾病进展速度**：既往研究（如 Baruch et al., Davar et al.）中的响应往往发生较晚，且有时 preceded by pseudo-progression（假性进展）。而 MITRIC 中的大多数患者表现为弥漫性、快速生长的疾病，可能没有足够的时间让 FMT 发挥有意义的生物学效应。\\\\n2. **供体匹配与异质性**：虽然既往研究中所有响应者均接受单一供体的粪便，而本试验使用了三名供体，可能存在次优的供体-受体匹配或缺乏产生获益所需的特定微生物群落。此外，ICI 响应者之间的微生物组成差异很大，使用健康供体是否更优尚不清楚。\\\\n3. **免疫微环境限制**：基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚 T 细胞表型与较差预后相关，且 FMT 未能逆转这种不利的髓系主导免疫环境（事实上 CD14+ 单核细胞和 IL-8 随时间增加，这与较短的 PFS 和 OS 相关）。这表明 FMT 可能仅在选定的具有特定免疫特征的人群中有效。\\\\n4. **样本量与异质性**：小样本量是重要局限性，且不同研究在供体选择、FMT 制备、给药途径和治疗方案上的异质性也可能影响结果。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"FMT 在 ICI 耐药人群中的最佳生物标志物筛选标准尚未确立。\\\", \\\"供体选择（ICI 响应者 vs 健康供体）及个体化匹配策略对疗效的具体影响仍需进一步研究。\\\", \\\"FMT 是否能通过改变外周血免疫表型（如减少髓系抑制）来增强疗效，目前数据不支持其诱导了显著的全身免疫改变。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"allowed_use\": [],\n            \"conditions\": [],\n            \"limits\": [],\n            \"question\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"sources\": [\n              {\n                \"doi\": \"10.1136/jitc-2026-015122\",\n                \"paper_id\": \"d9577b3a29bd8aec60c9e27c6a56a63faf3f4a27\",\n                \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n                \"title\": \"Safety and efficacy of fecal microbiota transplantation in solid cancers resistant to immune checkpoint inhibitors: results of the MITRIC trial\",\n                \"year\": \"2026\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"still_missing\": \"MITRIC 试验阴性结果需详细提取其关于患者选择、供体匹配及免疫微环境限制的解释，以平衡 Ch5 中的阳性结果。\",\n            \"usable_content\": \"{\\\"question_material\\\": [{\\\"question_id\\\": \\\"Q01\\\", \\\"examples\\\": [{\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"本研究 (MITRIC trial)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"提供阴性结果的详细解释，特别是关于患者选择（快速进展、晚期）、供体匹配（多供体 vs 单供体）及免疫微环境限制（髓系主导、IL-8升高），用于平衡Ch5中的阳性结果。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在12名ICI耐药实体瘤患者中，FMT联合ICI治疗未观察到客观缓解（ORR 0%）。尽管FMT安全且可行，但临床获益有限。机制分析显示，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差预后相关；治疗后CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关，表明FMT未能逆转这种不利的免疫微环境，甚至可能伴随髓系驱动的免疫抑制增加。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为12名接受过多种治疗的晚期实体瘤患者（9例黑色素瘤，1例HNSCC，1例ccRCC，1例MSI-H胰腺癌），均处于ICI治疗后的疾病进展期。供体为3名长期ICI反应者。干预措施包括结肠镜给药的初始FMT和灌肠后续FMT。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": []}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Baruch et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中使用的单一供体策略和特定患者群体，以突显MITRIC试验中多供体和不同患者选择带来的差异。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的概念验证试验中，使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）实现了3/10患者的客观缓解，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。所有反应者均接受来自单一供体的粪便。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R19\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Davar et al. (2021)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示阳性结果中观察到的免疫学变化（如CD56+CD8+ T细胞增加、IL-8降低），与MITRIC试验中的阴性结果形成机制上的对比。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在一项针对抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者的试验中，FMT使3/15患者产生反应，另有3名患者获得持久的疾病稳定。响应者在FMT/抗PD-1治疗后表现出外周血中CD56+CD8+ T细胞水平升高，且这些细胞表达更高的激活标记物；同时，响应者体内循环IL-8降低，肿瘤内产生IL-8的髓系细胞频率减少。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1耐受的转移性黑色素瘤患者。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R18\\\"]}, {\\\"attribution\\\": \\\"Kim et al. (2024)\\\", \\\"use_in_review\\\": \\\"作为对比背景，展示在其他实体瘤（上消化道癌）中FMT的潜在疗效，说明癌症类型和疾病状态对结果的影响。\\\", \\\"finding\\\": \\\"在抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者中，FMT改善了1/13名上消化道癌症患者的抗PD-1抑制剂疗效。\\\", \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"研究对象为抗PD-1抑制剂耐药的不可切除或转移性实体瘤患者，主要为上消化道癌症。\\\", \\\"reference_ids\\\": [\\\"R20\\\"]}], \\\"explanation\\\": \\\"MITRIC试验的阴性结果提示，FMT在克服ICI耐药方面并非普遍有效，其效果受到患者选择、供体匹配和免疫微环境状态的严格限制。\\\\n\\\\n首先，患者选择是关键因素。与之前报告阳性结果的试验（如Baruch等和Davar等）相比，MITRIC试验中的患者大多患有扩散迅速、生长快速的疾病，这可能没有给予FMT足够的时间来发挥有意义的生物学效应。此外，MITRIC试验纳入了原发性和继发性ICI耐药患者，而之前的研究主要关注继发性耐药或特定类型的耐药，这可能导致了结果的异质性。\\\\n\\\\n其次，供体匹配和多样性可能影响疗效。MITRIC试验使用了三名不同的供体，而Baruch等人的研究中所有反应者均来自单一供体。这表明，使用多名供体可能导致供体-受体匹配次优，或者缺乏对特定获益至关重要的微生物群落。供体的微生物组成存在显著差异，且目前尚不清楚使用ICI反应者作为供体是否优于健康供体。\\\\n\\\\n最后，免疫微环境的限制是重要的机制解释。MITRIC试验发现，基线时髓系偏倚环境和幼稚T细胞表型与较差的预后相关。治疗后，CD14+单核细胞和血清IL-8水平升高，这与较短的PFS和OS相关。相比之下，Davar等人的研究发现响应者体内IL-8降低，且髓系细胞产生的IL-8减少。这表明，在MITRIC试验的患者群体中，FMT未能逆转由髓系驱动的免疫抑制微环境，甚至可能伴随着这种抑制的增加，从而限制了临床获益。因此，FMT可能仅在具有特定免疫特征（如高分化T细胞环境、低髓系浸润）的选定人群中有效，而可靠的生物标志物尚未建立。\\\", \\\"remaining_points\\\": [\\\"MITRIC试验样本量小，且为单臂研究，无法进行因果推断或多重检验校正，因此关于免疫微环境和生物标志物的发现应谨慎解读。\\\", \\\"长期定植的效果难以评估，因为大多数患者在疾病进展后无法收集后续的粪便样本。\\\", \\\"需要进一步的研究来确定FMT的最佳给药方案、供体选择标准以及能够预测获益的患者亚群。\\\"]}], \\\"plain_text\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::de6856b325f938438220cbe8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d15b90b1b4387e8af2a1be3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0578\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2796f4a95907dc27585d9be6\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e24c98ddc10d25e6368e25c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7751d6078705a8eed77bd20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7b7e3472b4df79f76e0d24c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法，综合了机制研究（前临床模型与人类观察数据）和临床干预试验证据。具体路线包括：1）梳理微生物组影响ICI的药理学基础（抗原呈递、代谢物耦合、屏障完整性）；2）分类评估三类主要干预手段（FMT、LBPs、定义菌群）的代表性临床试验结果；3）讨论影响可重复性的转化因素（共用药、饮食、定植率）及安全监管问题。未进行系统检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于现有文献进行逻辑整合与批判性评议。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d823b853e4ac54a493eee6ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于微生物组工程化干预ICI治疗的最新临床证据综合，特别区分了FMT、LBPs和定义菌群三种模态的优缺点及适用场景。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为迷你综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对特定菌株或代谢物的因果机制多基于前临床模型或间接人类证据，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cdc0eb48bfb3cc26a577a419\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了将微生物组干预视为“生态药理学”而非简单附加剂的框架，强调了基线生态、共用药和功能性读出（如代谢物、定植率）的重要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于不同肿瘤类型间微生物组效应的异质性解释有限，主要依赖已发表的小规模试验，难以推断普适性规律。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c698a9fd6f94a8050dbc3115\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了安全与监管优先事项，包括供体筛查、追溯性及报告标准，为未来临床试验设计提供了实用指南。\",\n          \"limits\": \"监管建议基于现有案例和专家共识，尚未形成统一的行业标准，具体实施细节尚待后续研究明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::698814d6ffd5131ce300e4d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自反应者的粪菌移植（FMT）提供了最强的人类概念验证，部分患者实现了临床再敏感化，并伴随供体型微生物特征和肿瘤免疫重塑。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8fa931de280fc236eee06476\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用活体生物制剂（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在肾细胞癌中显示出改善临床结果的探索性信号，且能显著改变粪便微生物组特征，但结果具有情境依赖性，需更多大样本验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ccc398d5ad7381abec37394\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用定义菌群（如SER-401）及抗生素预处理\",\n          \"finding\": \"一项针对黑色素瘤的Ib期试验因入组不足未能得出效力结论，但揭示了广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备，提示“清除后添加”策略存在设计陷阱。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46a823fe6dc2d69e904ef7b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI相关的难治性结肠炎\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT在病例系列和转化研究中显示出修复生态平衡、恢复黏膜免疫耐受的活动，支持其作为毒性管理的潜在手段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7235049ddd5daa54ae6a8121\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fc6d62ba3897e0fe7ee791b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs改变了多种恶性肿瘤的管理方式，但仅对部分患者有效且伴随毒性。现有的组织生物标志物无法完全捕捉宿主层面的决定因素。本研究试图解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组如何作为可操作的调节器影响ICI的敏感性和毒性？以及目前基于微生物组的临床干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）的证据基础和转化障碍是什么？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0de486040443081d8ed9cbc1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"聚焦于实体瘤（特别是黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗）时的疗效与毒性管理。研究对象为肠道微生物组及其工程化干预策略，涵盖从基础机制到临床转化试验的综合分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08bc0ccb88530457d6c7da11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇迷你综述，旨在将微生物生态学原理与抗原呈递、T细胞启动及代谢物信号传导等生物学机制联系起来，并系统总结了三种主要干预模式（粪菌移植FMT、活体生物制剂LBPs、定义菌群Consortia）的临床证据。文章指出，肠道微生物组不仅是预测标志物，更是可操作的宿主水平调节剂，能够同时影响抗肿瘤疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。通过回顾早期临床试验，作者强调了微生物组干预在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的概念验证价值，同时也指出了当前干预措施在可重复性、安全性及标准化方面的挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c38bcef62c8079a6036e37c8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"证据主要来自小规模Phase 1/Ib期试验，样本量小，异质性高。不能直接外推至所有一线治疗场景或所有肿瘤类型。特别是SER-401试验未达效力终点，需谨慎解读。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了三类主要微生物组干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）在实体瘤中的具体临床证据对比。例如，FMT在难治性黑色素瘤中显示出的概念验证效力，以及LBPs在肾细胞癌中的探索性信号。同时指出了定义菌群试验中因抗生素预处理导致的负面设计教训。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e83796c6787bdce34f2f296\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节源自前临床模型（小鼠），人类证据多为间接支持（如FMT后的免疫重塑观察）。代谢物水平的因果关系在人类中尚未完全确立，需注意区分观察性关联与因果证据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物组影响ICI疗效的生物学机制框架，包括：1）通过促进树突状细胞激活和交叉呈递来增强CD8+ T细胞反应；2）通过短链脂肪酸等代谢物调节先天免疫编程和炎症基调；3）通过维持肠道屏障完整性来减少系统性炎症和irAEs风险。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d86b2c26e65d14b0a2de91e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了基线生态、共用药（抗生素、PPI、激素）、饮食和定植率对干预结果的影响。强调了‘生态药理学’概念，即干预不是简单的药物添加，而是生态扰动。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8449be79b3a7045e41c5dacb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到了耐药大肠杆菌血症、产志贺毒素大肠杆菌以及SARS-CoV-2传播的案例，强调了供体筛查和制造控制的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5c4718a22ebccf62e6d86dfd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文主要关注实体瘤（黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、NSCLC），其结论不一定适用于血液肿瘤或其他癌症类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::434f935a5128024bbc9228db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的‘强概念验证’仅限于抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤中的FMT，不应过度推广到其他干预模式或肿瘤类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::736f594938f6aedd75c4d1dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分混合了前临床模型和人类观察数据，需明确区分哪些是已证实的人类因果机制，哪些是基于模型的推测。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0fe5dc8f31ddf0d2f44a79a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床试验结果多为早期阶段（Phase 1/Ib），效力结论往往受限（如SER-401试验），解读时需强调其探索性质。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e325d70a97f845ed6b9630a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0be30e1c595392c045092cd7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f738899367563eaec3b1317e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5385a7857d92f184b107095e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"遵循PRISMA指南进行系统综述。使用Covidence管理流程，检索特定关键词组合。纳入标准为成人实体瘤患者，排除非英语、非人类、评论类文章。数据提取包括患者数量、ICI类型、癌症类型、干预措施及其对微生物多样性、OS、PFS和irAE的影响。未进行荟萃分析（因已有相关Meta分析且异质性高），而是采用定性综合方法，对比抗生素组与非抗生素组、FMT干预前后的临床结局和免疫学指标。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a995b8b38ea63be01d384b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了截至2021年的系统性证据汇总，确认抗生素使用与ICI疗效降低的强关联，以及FMT在逆转耐药和管理irAE方面的潜在益处。\",\n          \"limits\": \"1. 未进行定量Meta分析，限制了效应量的精确估计。2. 纳入研究多为观察性或小样本临床试验，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素（如合并用药、饮食、种族信息缺失）。3. OS和PFS定义不统一，影响结果可比性。4. FMT研究样本量极小，且部分患者在使用FMT前接受了强效免疫抑制剂，干扰因果推断。5. 缺乏关于抗生素种类、剂量及具体微生物群落变化的详细数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f61397f7ac6f10ccd811c334\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗生素使用（主要覆盖NSCLC, RCC, Melanoma，靶向PD-1/PD-L1为主），时间窗多为ICI开始前2个月至开始后1个月内\",\n          \"finding\": \"21/22项研究显示抗生素对OS和/或PFS有显著的负面影响。例如，Schett et al. (2019)中NSCLC患者抗生素组OS为1.8 vs 15.4个月；Pinato et al. (2019)中pATB组OS为2 vs 26个月。部分研究（如Lalani et al., Balado et al.）未发现显著差异，但总体趋势为负面。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::62930893a334abdd4a90dacc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT用于ICI耐药或发生严重irAE的实体瘤患者（主要为黑色素瘤，少量前列腺癌/尿路上皮癌）\",\n          \"finding\": \"所有6项FMT研究显示积极效果。Davar et al. (2019)中40%耐药患者克服耐药；Youngster et al. 和 Baruch et al. 分别报告60%和30%的患者克服耐药，伴随CD8+ T细胞浸润增加和IL-8下调。Wang et al. (2018, 2020)显示FMT可缓解ICI诱导的结肠炎（73%临床响应）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::75ab64b8a6712b9b3a7d5e44\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e70d3f39722026e27b2d7bed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 肠道微生物群改变药物（主要是抗生素）是否会对ICI的疗效产生不利影响？2. FMT是否能通过恢复肠道微生物群来改善ICI疗效并降低irAE的发生率？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ec580adacab9bbedb26ba339\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤患者，考察肠道微生物群改变药物（主要为抗生素及其他伴随用药）和粪便微生物群移植（FMT）对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效（总生存期OS、无进展生存期PFS）及毒性（免疫相关不良事件irAEs）的影响。纳入2015年1月至2021年4月发表的英文研究。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e6de935b19653fcb6e426043\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇系统综述，旨在评估肠道菌群调节干预措施与ICI治疗结果之间的关联。作者检索了OVID Medline、Embase等数据库，筛选出28项符合标准的研究：其中22项关注抗生素/其他药物对ICI疗效的影响，6项关注FMT对ICI疗效及irAE减轻的作用。结果显示，绝大多数（21/22）涉及抗生素的研究表明其显著降低OS和/或PFS；所有6项涉及FMT的研究均显示其在恢复ICI疗效或减少irAE方面具有积极效果。综述同时指出了现有研究在定义终点、样本量、混杂因素控制等方面的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91e994144d313746f98c75e2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅基于回顾性队列和小样本前瞻性研究，无法确立严格的因果关系；不同癌症类型和ICI亚型的效果可能存在差异（尽管多数为PD-1/PD-L1抑制剂）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了抗生素使用导致ICI疗效下降的大规模临床观察证据（21/22研究支持），以及FMT改善疗效的具体案例数据。明确了肠道菌群状态是ICI疗效的重要预测/影响因素。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3f83ec56f5f6859978c91322\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述主要来自少数几个高质量的小样本研究（如Davar, Youngster, Baruch），其他研究多仅报告临床结局；部分机制（如IL-8下调）尚未在所有FMT研究中得到一致验证；需区分是直接由菌群引起还是继发于免疫状态改变。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了FMT起效的部分潜在免疫机制：增加CD8+ T细胞浸润、增加抗原呈递细胞（CD68+）、下调促耐药因子IL-8及其产生的髓系细胞。这些发现直接指向了T细胞介导的抗肿瘤免疫增强和炎症微环境改善。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::721f781a7291a3c4ccd59163\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出大多数纳入研究集中在NSCLC, RCC, Melanoma，且主要使用抗PD-1/PD-L1药物。同时提到化疗等其他抗癌治疗也可能破坏肠道屏障和菌群。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e16271ee6436c84aa68cc464\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述详细分析了纳入研究在OS/PFS定义上的不一致性，以及FMT研究中随机化困难、样本量小、合并用药（免疫抑制剂）带来的偏倚风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7c5de44e3cb32833abfeb875\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"建议未来研究应关注抗生素使用时机（提前vs同期）、具体抗生素种类/剂量、患者种族/饮食对菌群的影响，以及扩大FMT研究的样本量。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6daa6bf638fc0a586c155313\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"FMT的积极结果主要来源于小样本、单臂或开放标签研究，且部分患者在使用FMT前已接受过强效免疫抑制治疗，因此不能简单外推为FMT对所有ICI耐药患者的普适性解决方案。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::03d903e6472f77e8ddd42f80\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗生素的负面影响虽在多数研究中观察到，但存在例外（如Lalani, Balado等），这可能源于抗生素类型、给药时机或癌症类型的差异，需谨慎归因。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::75b33df0d637c35db8e354cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述未进行Meta分析，因此提供的效应方向是定性的，缺乏统一的效应量估计。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b51b4a793d85bd67eec15e5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制性发现（如IL-8, CD8+ T cells）主要来自少数几项深入生物学分析的研究，不代表所有临床观察到的疗效变化都有相同的机制基础。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1300bff91406c33fa664d068\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0304\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::235e35281eb4c1f2e906be10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07d9c6e4c1bb2933d52092e4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::84b32c303722590ec2d53121\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6befe43108931f970e929b2e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a review article, this work does not present new primary experimental data but synthesizes existing literature. The authors systematically summarize findings from retrospective clinical studies, prospective cohorts, and preclinical murine models regarding the correlation between gut microbiota composition (diversity, specific taxa like Faecalibacterium, Bifidobacterium, Bacteroides) and ICPI outcomes. They integrate mechanistic insights from immunology (T-cell regulation, dendritic cell maturation) and metabolism (short-chain fatty acids, bile acids). The approach involves categorizing evidence into themes: response prediction, toxicity mediation (colitis, myocarditis), antibiotic effects, and therapeutic manipulation (FMT, probiotics, synthetic biotics), supported by tables listing relevant clinical trials.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c5f0af15908b0603befc98d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of the dual role of the gut microbiome in determining both the efficacy and toxicity of ICPIs in solid tumors. It integrates clinical associations with mechanistic hypotheses (immunological and metabolic) and maps the landscape of ongoing clinical trials for microbiome-based therapies.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not perform a systematic meta-analysis or provide quantitative pooled estimates. The mechanistic explanations are largely derived from preclinical models or correlative human studies, so causal relationships remain to be fully validated in large-scale randomized controlled trials. The review acknowledges heterogeneity in findings across different cancer types and geographic populations.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01f63df59d963a0044ad8942\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Solid tumor patients receiving ICPIs (anti-PD-1/PD-L1, anti-CTLA-4)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Loss of microbial diversity (dysbiosis) and enrichment of certain bacteria (e.g., Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved objective response rates and survival, while depletion of these taxa or enrichment of others (e.g., Bacteroides) correlates with poor response.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d4337ee1dd2b52b96d4bd29a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Patients treated with broad-spectrum antibiotics prior to or during ICPI therapy\",\n          \"finding\": \"Antibiotic use is consistently associated with reduced overall survival and progression-free survival, likely due to disruption of beneficial gut microbiota; narrow-spectrum antibiotics show less clear detrimental effects.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cdc25ae78468f915b4f1e1c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Development of immune-related adverse events (irAEs), particularly colitis and myocarditis\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific bacterial strains influence irAE risk; e.g., Faecalibacterium enrichment is linked to higher incidence of colitis but better tumor response, while Bacteroidetes may protect against colitis. Mechanisms involve cross-reactive T-cells primed by bacterial peptides (e.g., beta-galactosidase from Bacteroides) targeting host tissues (e.g., MYH6 in heart).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b8a5d96c854e7ba7964eeaa9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical and early-phase clinical trials of microbiome modulation\",\n          \"finding\": \"Interventions such as FMT, oral live biotherapeutics (e.g., EDP1503, SER-401), and synthetic biotics are being tested to restore microbiome diversity or introduce beneficial strains, showing preliminary promise in enhancing ICPI efficacy or managing refractory colitis.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05e383c2aae7e03a620e4828\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bb6006227f00f1e06386e3bd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review addresses the challenge that only a minority of cancer patients derive durable benefit from ICPIs, and many experience severe irAEs. It seeks to explain why responses vary among patients by examining the gut microbiome as a potential predictive biomarker and modulator of both therapeutic efficacy and toxicity, aiming to identify avenues for improving patient outcomes through microbiome-targeted strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::00719742511ab12e73100aea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the role of the gut microbiome in modulating response and toxicity to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICPIs) in cancer patients, with specific emphasis on solid tumors (e.g., melanoma, non-small cell lung cancer, renal cell carcinoma, pancreatic adenocarcinoma). It covers clinical observations, preclinical mechanisms, and emerging therapeutic strategies involving microbiome modulation.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6b85ed0929d25a175964026\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This article is a narrative review summarizing current evidence on how the gut microbiome influences the efficacy and safety of ICPI therapy. It discusses the association between microbial diversity/composition and treatment outcomes, outlines putative immunological and metabolic mechanisms linking gut bacteria to anti-tumor immunity and immune-related adverse events (irAEs), and highlights the impact of antibiotics and dietary factors. The review also surveys ongoing clinical trials evaluating microbiome-based interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) and live biotherapeutics to enhance ICPI response or mitigate toxicity.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d93757978c699f59d944785e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are primarily observational or from small prospective studies; causality is not established. Findings may vary by cancer type and geography. Does not provide definitive proof of mechanism.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence linking specific gut microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium vs. Bacteroides) to ICPI response rates and survival outcomes in solid tumors. Details the negative impact of broad-spectrum antibiotic use on treatment efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ef1a42d6b6dd05fa51875187\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or correlative human data. The exact pathways are described as 'putative' and 'not fully elucidated'. Direct causal links in humans require further validation. Specific peptide-crossreactivity details are based on specific transgenic models.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details putative mechanisms including: 1) Modulation of T-regulatory cells and antigen-specific T-cell accumulation in the tumor microenvironment; 2) Production of metabolites (SCFAs, deoxycholate) influencing anti-tumor tolerogenesis; 3) Cross-reactive T-cell activation via bacterial peptides (e.g., beta-galactosidase mimicking MYH6) leading to irAEs like myocarditis; 4) Role of intraepithelial lymphocytes and dendritic cells in colitis pathogenesis.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d93afb5e20374119e59c09bb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Introduction section discussing the paradigm shift in cancer treatment, the lack of universal predictive biomarkers, and the growing interest in the tumor microenvironment and gut microbiome.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c51da46bff8a9c0bbd953a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Table 1 and Table 2 listing phase I/II trials evaluating microbial therapies (EDP1503, SER-401, MRx0518, FMT) in various solid tumors and for managing irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a9c949dec2c60440905ab78b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Section on 'Antibiotic mediated modulation...' and mentions of dysbiosis causes in the toxicity section.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e88468e5ba9034039695a162\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis, not a systematic review with strict inclusion/exclusion criteria or meta-analytic statistics. Claims should be interpreted as summaries of emerging trends rather than definitive consensus.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b93a566b8c782cd7c5da194b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic insights are largely based on preclinical models (mice) or correlative human studies; causal inference in humans is limited.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::79c03182deb792dead1afbfa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Findings on specific bacterial taxa may vary across different cancer types, geographic regions, and study populations. Generalizations should be made cautiously.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a3ec7b906bce3050cdf0fb32\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The term 'solid tumors' is used broadly; specific results may apply only to certain cancers (e.g., melanoma, NSCLC, RCC).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a60373c4ec7d897e091ba05\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Author disclosures indicate potential conflicts of interest related to industry partnerships, which should be noted when evaluating the objectivity of the review's conclusions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::57450d6462c2bcc145f62fda\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0358\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::8717538515f340cb5e7fb185\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a272db2dd9eea5f67a5bae8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de54677b13188b0e9af90db9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ba11e860995b5b93ccba646a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性文献回顾方法。检索PubMed索引的英文出版物（1946-2026年）、主要肿瘤学指南、关键II/III期临床试验、荟萃分析及机制研究。检索词涵盖NSCLC、ICI、TME、耐药及相关分子靶点。对临床证据按试验阶段、人群相关性、终点成熟度及监管意义进行加权；对临床前和假设生成性研究主要用于支持机制概念。通过分类归纳TME组成、分子通路、物理化学抑制因素及系统性因素，构建耐药机制框架，并据此评估不同组合疗法的临床转化潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d0d6e3f09a1c7ce3c1adb314\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了NSCLC中TME介导耐药的整合性框架，强调从孤立因素转向相互连接的生物学过程视角；明确了不同联合疗法（免疫-免疫、免疫-抗血管、免疫-放化疗、免疫-靶向）的临床证据层级和适用情境。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为叙事性综述，其结论依赖于作者对纳入文献的选择和解释；未提供新的原始实验数据；部分机制（如微生物组干预）仅基于初步研究，缺乏大规模临床验证；特定生物标志物（如ctDNA阈值）尚待标准化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c58638947e26fda363bc96b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TME细胞成分异质性\",\n          \"finding\": \"巨噬细胞并非简单的M1/M2二元模型，而是存在激活状态的连续谱系；MDSCs亚型特异性功能不同（单核型通过ARG1/iNOS抑制，多形核型通过ROS抑制）；CAF和ECM重塑通过增加间质硬度促进免疫排斥。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::868f6863791b248bb2f885d2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"内在肿瘤机制\",\n          \"finding\": \"STK11缺失抑制I型干扰素信号，KEAP1缺失激活抗氧化程序，两者共同导致低PD-L1表达和低CD8+ T细胞浸润；EGFR/ALK驱动突变通常伴随低TMB和不活跃的免疫微环境。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8374ecf9788b5088e7803fbf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"联合治疗证据等级\",\n          \"finding\": \"纳武利尤单抗+伊匹木单抗在CheckMate 227中显示疗效（受PD-L1/TMB影响）；阿替利珠单抗+贝伐珠单抗+化疗在IMpower150中证实对转移性非鳞状NSCLC有效，包括肝转移和EGFR突变TKI失败后人群；LAG-3/TIM-3抑制剂在NSCLC中的临床采纳仍需成熟试验确认。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55ac707849e577034afb0fb0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"生物标志物应用\",\n          \"finding\": \"PD-L1检测存在空间异质性和平台间不完全互换性；高TMB预测价值受测序平台和肿瘤纯度影响；空间转录组学可区分免疫表型；液体活检（ctDNA/exosome）需前瞻性验证阈值。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d15f8dadaa9a51de5fbf09e7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a3358fa0ff1afdc9ee48a53\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"解决NSCLC中ICI原发性和获得性耐药限制长期临床获益的问题；阐明TME各组分如何协同导致不同免疫表型，并厘清当前联合治疗策略的证据等级与局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::16c76a5912d11aab9f5c31be\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者中，肿瘤微环境（TME）介导的免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）耐药机制、联合治疗策略及生物标志物框架。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f8fa25779ca4c2210b5be95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇叙事性综述，旨在将TME介导的ICI耐药视为一个相互连接的生物学过程，而非孤立因素的集合。文章系统梳理了免疫抑制细胞群、基质重塑、血管功能障碍、缺氧、代谢重编程以及抗原呈递缺陷和致癌驱动信号如何协同作用，形成免疫沙漠、免疫排斥或耗竭性炎症表型。在此基础上，综述评估了针对这些机制的联合治疗策略，区分了III期支持的临床标准与早期探索性方法，并提出了整合PD-L1、TMB、干扰素γ特征、空间组学、ctDNA等指标的操作化生物标志物框架，以指导NSCLC的精准免疫治疗。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fd45b37845cc9232f8771c98\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了NSCLC中ICI耐药的多维度机制，包括内在肿瘤基因改变、局部TME抑制和系统性因素。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::159d56d3ae0242026c9cb9ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了PD-L1、TMB、空间组学和液体活检等生物标志物的现状、局限性和整合需求。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ca50e4620e570197a4e95208\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"区分了III期支持的联合疗法（如双免疫、免疫+抗血管）与早期探索性疗法（如微生物组调节、IDO抑制）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21e41420c3204126923b02a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限NSCLC人群；关联多为观察性，因果机制未详述；Fusobacterium的作用在其他癌种更明确，此处仅为对比提示。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了NSCLC队列中与ICI疗效相关的特定肠道微生物菌群信息：Akkermansia muciniphila、Bifidobacterium spp. 和 Ruminococcus 被报道有助于促进有利的免疫微环境；而 Fusobacterium 的关联在结直肠癌中更强，在NSCLC中需谨慎外推。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5ce76ef1bd40abb575afd9d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述较为概括，未深入具体的微生物-宿主分子互作细节；主要基于综述转述的其他研究结果；强调需要前瞻性验证。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐述了系统性因素（包括微生物组、营养状态、全身炎症）如何作为TME介导耐药的一部分影响ICI疗效。指出微生物组特征可能通过塑造有利的免疫微环境来增强ICI反应，但同时也强调了这种关联需要NSCLC特异性数据集的支持，且目前微生物组干预（如FMT、益生菌）仍属探索性阶段，缺乏标准化评估和安全监测。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bfe4688b4889c6c75d385bf2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述聚焦于NSCLC，其关于微生物组的发现不能直接外推到所有实体瘤或其他癌症类型，尽管文中提到了结直肠癌的对比。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::75bfe2b13ac9586076893b8d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的微生物组与ICI疗效的关联主要基于观察性研究和初步数据，因果关系尚未完全确立，干预效果也未经验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eaf685d0ccc478e538526402\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述本身是叙事性的，其结论依赖于作者对文献的选择和综合，可能存在选择偏倚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b39a3d326158b7528cc18724\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"对于Fusobacterium等菌种，文中明确指出其在NSCLC中的作用不如在结直肠癌中明确，需谨慎解读。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9b0b35da32a29f6efe86ccd3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0474\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2ebf71c6aa2b1657b267b130\",\n          \"snapshot::153461ac1a5cb9b5a31c3121\",\n          \"snapshot::e83de03b33da0c831779d170\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0199db0a6b296991ed95d91b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1903d13a7df8887be754a784\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::21c502ce4d9feb1abc472eb2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者通过PubMed数据库进行了系统性文献检索（2019年1月至2025年12月），筛选出关于肠道微生物群和代谢物在癌症免疫治疗中作用的基础和转化研究。随后，文章采用叙事性综述的方法，将内容分为三个主要部分：(1) 详细解析核心代谢物（SCFAs、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸、肌苷）的免疫调节机制；(2) 按肿瘤类型（胃肠道与非胃肠道）总结微生物签名与ICI疗效的关联；(3) 评估FMT、益生菌、工程菌等干预策略的转化应用。文中引用了大量图表（Figure 1-3, Table 2）来整合机制网络和治疗策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4eddf4399a38d90f66a52ed4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群-代谢物-免疫轴在多类实体瘤中的系统性机制框架，特别强调了代谢物的情境依赖性（如丁酸的双向作用）和肿瘤特异性微生物签名。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为叙事性综述，其结论基于已发表研究的综合，缺乏原始数据的定量合成（如Meta分析）。许多机制证据来自动物模型或小样本临床研究，大规模随机对照试验（RCTs）数据尚缺，且个体间微生物组异质性导致标准化治疗面临挑战。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::13d020d401659bfd819edc82\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"短链脂肪酸（特别是丁酸）\",\n          \"finding\": \"具有双向且依赖情境的免疫调节作用：一方面通过抑制HDAC活性、增强CD8+ T细胞毒性及TCR信号传导来增强抗肿瘤免疫；另一方面在某些情况下（如抗CTLA-4治疗中）可能抑制树突状细胞成熟，减弱T细胞激活。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::556a2c02b52a8d3397800c2e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"色氨酸代谢物\",\n          \"finding\": \"犬尿氨酸（Kyn）通过AhR通路促进Treg分化，抑制效应T细胞，削弱免疫反应；而吲哚-3-甲醛（I3A）和ICA则通过激活AhR/IL-22轴或抑制IDO1，增强CD8+ T细胞功能并维持肠道屏障完整性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d2f957c8117b0f1944f97f1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"胆汁酸（BAs）\",\n          \"finding\": \"次级胆汁酸如isoDCA促进Treg扩增，抑制DC功能；而UDCA通过降解TGF-β抑制Treg分化，增强抗肿瘤免疫。不同胆汁酸对CD8+ T细胞命运有截然相反的影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf6a692c23cd8b67e8b5e315\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肌苷（Inosine）\",\n          \"finding\": \"作为关键代谢物，肌苷通过抑制UBA6增加肿瘤免疫原性，结合A2AR促进Th1细胞分化，并在葡萄糖受限的微环境中作为替代能源维持效应T细胞的存活和杀伤功能。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::058f047f3f5c1d44f65875b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"不同肿瘤类型\",\n          \"finding\": \"存在肿瘤特异性的微生物签名：例如ESCC中Streptococcus富集与良好响应相关，Fn驱动耐药；HCC中Akk和Ruminococcaceae富集者预后较好；黑色素瘤中Bifidobacterium和Ruminococcaceae与ICI疗效正相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a99672acb9cc746b2c9a196\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::91039a283204ebc61cb46c6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）取得了显著进展，但原发性或获得性耐药限制了其临床疗效。目前对于肠道微生物群-代谢物-免疫轴影响ICI疗效的具体分子机制以及不同肿瘤类型中的特异性调控模式仍不完全清楚。本研究旨在阐明这些机制并综合现有的微生物靶向治疗策略，以改善免疫治疗结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8152b340dba9d984834c3591\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述聚焦于肠道微生物群-代谢物-免疫轴在癌症免疫治疗中的作用，涵盖胃肠道肿瘤（如食管癌、胃癌、胰腺癌、肝癌、结直肠癌）和非胃肠道实体瘤（如黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌）。研究对象包括核心代谢物（短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸、肌苷）、特定微生物菌群及其与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效的相互作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::61b7f2caf7a2598674f9c9f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇叙事性综述，旨在系统梳理肠道微生物群及其代谢产物调节抗肿瘤免疫的分子机制，并综合评估针对该轴的转化治疗策略。文章首先阐述了微生物代谢物如何通过表观遗传修饰、受体结合和代谢重编程等途径重塑免疫微环境；其次，按肿瘤类型归纳了特征性微生物签名及其对ICI响应的影响；最后，讨论了粪菌移植（FMT）、益生菌补充、工程菌及其他干预手段的临床潜力与挑战。尽管采用了系统性的文献检索流程，但其性质为叙事性综述，侧重于机制解释和策略综合，而非严格的荟萃分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ac0f10278878595624a0d171\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些关联多基于观察性队列或动物模型，因果关系需进一步验证；且不同研究间的微生物定义和分析方法可能存在差异。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了不同肿瘤类型中特征性微生物签名与ICI疗效关联的分类信息。具体包括：ESCC中Streptococcus富集与CD8+ T细胞浸润相关，Fn驱动耐药；HCC中Akk和Ruminococcaceae富集预示良好响应；黑色素瘤中Bifidobacterium和Ruminococcaceae与疗效正相关；结直肠癌中Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG和Roseburia intestinalis增强敏感性，而Peptostreptococcus anaerobius促进MDSC积累导致耐药。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cffa01442576e15d938a5da1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制细节多源于体外实验或小鼠模型，人体内的确切浓度和效应阈值尚不明确；部分机制（如丁酸的双向作用）高度依赖肿瘤微环境的特定状态。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了四类核心代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的具体分子机制。包括：(1) SCFAs（如丁酸）通过抑制HDAC、激活GPR109A/TLR5通路增强CD8+ T细胞功能，但具有情境依赖性；(2) 色氨酸代谢物中，Kyn通过AhR促进Treg，而I3A/ICA通过AhR/IDO1通路增强效应T细胞；(3) 胆汁酸中，isoDCA促进Treg，UDCA抑制Treg；(4) 肌苷通过抑制UBA6、激活A2AR/cAMP-CREB通路及作为替代能源支持T细胞代谢。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a132693460907667307d07bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"大多数干预措施仍处于早期临床试验阶段，缺乏大规模RCT证据；个体化匹配和长期安全性仍是未决问题。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"评估了针对微生物组的干预策略（FMT、益生菌、工程菌）在增强ICI疗效方面的转化潜力和当前局限。指出FMT在黑色素瘤和小样本研究中显示出提高ORR的潜力，但面临标准化和安全风险；益生菌（如LGG、Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）可通过产生代谢物或下调PD-L1增强疗效，但也存在负面案例；工程菌和噬菌体疗法代表了精准调控的新方向。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::68177944a4dda1ac58b105ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述引言及机制部分对轴的整体描述，包括代谢物跨肠壁转运、受体结合及表观遗传调控的一般原理。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::832221f445633253af129f0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论部分关于“Translational challenges and future directions”的内容。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17c35972997100ed380495a6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述为叙事性综述，非系统评价或Meta分析，其结论代表作者对现有文献的综合解读，而非统计汇总结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cf39d36dbfa7ab60609a95cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"许多机制证据来自动物模型（如无菌小鼠、人源化小鼠），直接外推到人类临床需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01087a6efb8a2e39da727c5b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"微生物签名的识别依赖于特定的测序技术和分析方法，不同研究间可能存在批次效应或定义差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ce6ec42420753ee3437352d2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"代谢物的作用具有高度的情境依赖性（如丁酸的双向作用），不能简单概括为单一的促进或抑制效应。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bb36f7fcdf84db78fa48a12\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": [\n            \"综述提供了“肠道微生物群 - 代谢物 - 免疫轴”的整体概念框架，解释了代谢物如何作为分子信使从肠腔易位至体循环并调节全身及局部抗肿瘤免疫。\",\n            \"文中还总结了其他核心代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节免疫的具体机制及在不同肿瘤类型（如食管癌、胃癌、肝癌、结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌）中的微生物特征签名，为理解肌苷在整体代谢网络中的位置提供了背景。\",\n            \"讨论了针对微生物组的干预策略（如 FMT、益生菌、工程菌）在增强 ICI 疗效方面的转化潜力和当前面临的标准化、安全性及监管挑战。\"\n          ],\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-gam_e3ai\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_7089b09315\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"该综述未提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数值（如μM 或 ng/mL），也未报告人体临床队列中肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效（如 OS、PFS、ORR）的具体统计学关联数据。文中关于肌苷浓度的描述主要引用了小鼠模型的血浆代谢组分析或体外实验背景，缺乏针对接受 ICI 治疗的人类患者肿瘤组织或间质液的实测浓度数据。\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": [\n            \"该综述详细阐述了肌苷（inosine）作为肠道微生物代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的三大分子机制：(1) 特异性抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素样修饰激活酶 6（UBA6）活性，提高肿瘤免疫原性；(2) 结合 T 淋巴细胞上的腺苷 A2A 受体，激活 cAMP-CREB 信号级联，促进 Th1 细胞分化及肿瘤浸润；(3) 在葡萄糖受限的肿瘤微环境（TME）中作为替代能源底物维持效应 T 细胞的生存和细胞毒性功能。\",\n            \"文中指出肌苷由特定肠道菌群（如假长双歧杆菌 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum、约氏乳杆菌 Lactobacillus johnsonii 等）合成，并在免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗破坏肠道屏障完整性后易位至体循环，从而激活抗肿瘤 T 细胞。\",\n            \"综述提及了临床转化潜力，指出在存在肌苷代谢缺陷的实体瘤中，外源性肌苷补充可能恢复免疫细胞代谢适应性，从而增强 ICI 疗效，这为理解肌苷浓度与疗效的关系提供了理论框架。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::797da90ccaff14b0fe6ff1dc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": [\n              \"综述提供了“肠道微生物群 - 代谢物 - 免疫轴”的整体概念框架，解释了代谢物如何作为分子信使从肠腔易位至体循环并调节全身及局部抗肿瘤免疫。\",\n              \"文中还总结了其他核心代谢物（如短链脂肪酸、色氨酸代谢物、胆汁酸）调节免疫的具体机制及在不同肿瘤类型（如食管癌、胃癌、肝癌、结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌）中的微生物特征签名，为理解肌苷在整体代谢网络中的位置提供了背景。\",\n              \"讨论了针对微生物组的干预策略（如 FMT、益生菌、工程菌）在增强 ICI 疗效方面的转化潜力和当前面临的标准化、安全性及监管挑战。\"\n            ],\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_C2_inosine_tme\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\body_full_staged_acceptance_20261004_40cny\\\\planning\\\\level2\\\\external\\\\Nf2f13ca37a1cba78c9d1-acf4314fb7d520c6\\\\round_3\\\\supplements\\\\case_C2_inosine_tme\\\\attempt-gam_e3ai\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_7089b09315\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"该综述未提供人体肿瘤微环境（TME）内肌苷的绝对生理浓度数值（如μM 或 ng/mL），也未报告人体临床队列中肌苷水平与 ICI 疗效（如 OS、PFS、ORR）的具体统计学关联数据。文中关于肌苷浓度的描述主要引用了小鼠模型的血浆代谢组分析或体外实验背景，缺乏针对接受 ICI 治疗的人类患者肿瘤组织或间质液的实测浓度数据。\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": [\n              \"该综述详细阐述了肌苷（inosine）作为肠道微生物代谢物调节抗肿瘤免疫的三大分子机制：(1) 特异性抑制肿瘤细胞内的泛素样修饰激活酶 6（UBA6）活性，提高肿瘤免疫原性；(2) 结合 T 淋巴细胞上的腺苷 A2A 受体，激活 cAMP-CREB 信号级联，促进 Th1 细胞分化及肿瘤浸润；(3) 在葡萄糖受限的肿瘤微环境（TME）中作为替代能源底物维持效应 T 细胞的生存和细胞毒性功能。\",\n              \"文中指出肌苷由特定肠道菌群（如假长双歧杆菌 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum、约氏乳杆菌 Lactobacillus johnsonii 等）合成，并在免疫检查点阻断（ICB）治疗破坏肠道屏障完整性后易位至体循环，从而激活抗肿瘤 T 细胞。\",\n              \"综述提及了临床转化潜力，指出在存在肌苷代谢缺陷的实体瘤中，外源性肌苷补充可能恢复免疫细胞代谢适应性，从而增强 ICI 疗效，这为理解肌苷浓度与疗效的关系提供了理论框架。\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f7368223bdbf2801e243e0b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0594\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::82bffb4d0f097201933ac437\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::20b7c9407887887b4c1955c1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"structured_partial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d407e9afd4edab967034fec5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f02e6b98612c18ae9aa0912\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用回顾性分析设计，整合两项独立的I期随机临床试验数据。纳入接受nivo/ipi或cabo/nivo +/- CBM588治疗的mRCC患者。收集基线和第12周的粪便样本进行宏基因组测序（MetaPhlan v4）。主要分析方法包括：1) 比较SOC组与SOC/CBM组在基线和第12周的Alpha和Beta多样性；2) 使用Wilcoxon配对检验评估临床相关微生物物种丰度的变化；3) 计算Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率以衡量菌群失调程度。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e59dd59a101dcc1ad5120ae2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了CBM588调节肠道微生物组的直接证据，特别是其能防止Eubacterium siraeum耗竭并纠正Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率失衡，这为之前观察到的临床获益提供了生物学机制假设。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（N=58），且为I期试验数据的二次分析；仅报告了微生物组变化，未直接关联临床结局数据（如ORR、PFS）；未区分两种不同的ICI联合方案对微生物组影响的潜在差异；缺乏长期随访数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b3a3638adfa01b7db6729e9c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SOC组 vs SOC/CBM组，基线 vs 第12周\",\n          \"finding\": \"两组间Alpha和Beta多样性在第12周均无统计学显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fabca92c6655ca00f603409\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SOC组，基线 vs 第12周\",\n          \"finding\": \"Alistipes senegalensis减少（LFC -0.82, P=0.004）；Eubacterium siraeum显著减少（LFC -1.75, P=0.005）；Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率从89.0%增加到96.4%（提示菌群失调加重）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04e5819886921a9c0c850bcc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SOC/CBM组，基线 vs 第12周\",\n          \"finding\": \"Alistipes senegalensis减少（LFC -0.36, P=0.007）；Eubacterium siraeum未发生显著减少；Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率从100.0%显著下降到75.7%（提示菌群失调改善）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb42b8b8bbb293987a68d708\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4d9086cad83959bd751a5143\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"在mRCC患者中，添加CBM588到一线ICI联合治疗方案中，如何影响肠道微生物组的组成和菌群失调状态？其是否通过调节微生物组来介导临床获益？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a35910d01fdeeda24d7f32b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者，接受一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）联合治疗（纳武利尤单抗/伊匹木单抗或卡博替尼/纳武利尤单抗），部分患者联合使用活体生物疗法CBM588。样本来自两项I期临床试验的合并队列，共58名患者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::258b37d2499172ba1cff0c79\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探讨活体生物疗法CBM588对接受一线ICI联合治疗的mRCC患者肠道微生物组组成及菌群失调的影响。研究团队合并了两项I期随机临床试验的数据，对比了标准治疗（SOC）组与SOC联合CBM588组在基线和第12周时的肠道微生物多样性及组成变化。结果显示，CBM588显著改善了菌群失调指标，并防止了与ICI疗效相关的特定菌种耗竭，为CBM588增强临床疗效提供了潜在的微生物机制解释。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b5e043583ccc1fe222739c3e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限mRCC人群；仅涉及CBM588这一种干预手段；未提供临床终点与微生物变化的直接相关性统计，仅作为机制推测的基础。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了CBM588干预下mRCC患者肠道微生物组的具体变化图谱。显示CBM588能逆转ICI治疗常见的菌群失调趋势（降低F/B比率），并维持Eubacterium siraeum水平。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e2e9022343dde30c2c59134\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于观察到的微生物变化的“合理机制推测”，而非经过功能验证的因果证据。需结合其他研究确认E. siraeum在ICI疗效中的具体功能角色。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了CBM588通过防止有益菌（E. siraeum）耗竭和纠正菌群失调来介导临床获益的潜在机制路径。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ba9383b3b5e904f75192b855\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"CBM588作为一种基于丁酸梭菌的活体生物疗法，在mRCC ICI治疗中的应用背景。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b804adfbf51285c1c31a6f4b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用MetaPhlan v4进行分类学分析，以及使用F/B比率作为菌群失调指标的实践。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::97e7c7edd83bd6527d2faa0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为I期试验数据的汇总分析，样本量有限，结果可能受选择偏倚影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7b3c7922923705e274e4c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"发现的微生物变化是观察性关联，不能直接推断为导致临床获益的唯一或主要原因。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6d36c9ac49a58ab6342c847a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"未区分nivo/ipi和cabo/nivo两种方案对微生物组的不同影响，可能存在混杂因素。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4918986773f2c4c113ef4aeb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“机制”是基于微生物组变化的推论，需警惕将相关性误读为因果性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1be8973fcdd65f0d70e4a179\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0006\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"structured source contained metadata or abstract without a research body\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_challenge_or_login\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_challenge_or_login\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"known_losses\": [\n                \"headings/tables/math/image pixels are not preserved by this plain HTML projection\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"body converted to structured material; headings/tables/math/image pixels may be lost\",\n              \"status\": \"derived\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"structured_partial\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::ae6fc092083bad76a3be286e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4c55b9ec1ec7d88603525d32\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b4a031bb38fe09efcf8c017\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::94e57fc3b489cc0cf77510e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用回顾性分析设计，合并两项独立的I期随机临床试验数据。纳入接受nivo/ipi或cabo/nivo +/- CBM588治疗的mRCC患者。使用MetaPhlan v4进行分类学分析，计算Alpha和Beta多样性。利用Wilcoxon配对检验评估从基线到第12周临床相关微生物物种丰度的变化。计算Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率作为菌群失调的衡量指标，并比较SOC组与SOC/CBM组的差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ab294fa19d5ef32aaf225ec4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了CBM588调节肠道微生物组的直接证据，特别是其能防止Eubacterium siraeum耗竭并纠正F/B比率升高，这可能与改善ICI疗效有关。\",\n          \"limits\": \"仅基于两项I期试验的合并小样本（N=58）分析，缺乏长期随访和临床终点（如OS/PFS）的直接关联分析。未交代具体的统计校正方法（如多重比较校正）。所给摘要未交代微生物组变化与具体临床响应率之间的直接相关性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e0ec617ba1358cc1537f956c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SOC组 vs SOC/CBM组，基线 vs 第12周\",\n          \"finding\": \"两组间Alpha和Beta多样性在基线与第12周之间无统计学显著差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0bcd6ee9235948b878cabb1d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Alistipes senegalensis丰度变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"在SOC组和SOC/CBM组中均显著下降（SOC: LFC -0.82, P=0.004; SOC/CBM: LFC -0.36, P=0.007）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0a59e48ba3392ee02df080ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Eubacterium siraeum丰度变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"仅在SOC组中显著下降（LFC -1.75, P=0.005），而在SOC/CBM组中未观察到显著下降。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e560305c8a691f0fbab646ed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"SOC组从89.0%增加至96.4%；SOC/CBM组从100.0%显著下降至75.7%。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8f61ef01720e7a9580955c6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cc71cf5ee6821ea9fb384e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"在mRCC患者中，补充CBM588如何影响肠道微生物组的组成和菌群失调状态？其是否通过调节微生物组来增强ICI治疗的潜在疗效？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a95d397296501b878a36122b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）患者，接受一线免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）联合治疗（纳武利尤单抗/伊匹木单抗或卡博替尼/纳武利尤单抗），并补充活体生物制剂CBM588。研究基于两项I期临床试验的合并队列。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3d53d8d244ac5dadc9c8db42\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探讨活体生物制剂CBM588对接受一线ICI联合治疗的mRCC患者肠道微生物组组成及菌群失调的影响。通过整合两项随机I期临床试验的数据，比较标准治疗（SOC）与SOC联合CBM588两组患者在基线和第12周的肠道微生物多样性、物种丰度变化以及Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率的变化。结果显示，CBM588显著纠正了菌群失调指标，并防止了与ICI反应相关的特定菌种耗竭，为CBM588改善临床结局提供了潜在的微生物机制解释。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::56c7a21a7e043192307dcd02\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限mRCC人群；仅涉及CBM588一种制剂；样本量较小（N=58）；主要关注微生物组变化而非直接的临床疗效关联。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了益生菌（CBM588）调节肠道微生物组以可能增强ICI疗效的具体案例。数据显示CBM588能阻止有益菌（E. siraeum）的耗竭，并改善菌群失调指标（F/B比率）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e112410630a7f26d1436ed76\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制仅为作者提出的“合理推测”（plausible mechanism），需结合其他文献验证E. siraeum在ICI反应中的具体生物学功能。F/B比率作为单一指标的局限性需注意。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了一个潜在的机制路径：通过维持Eubacterium siraeum等关键菌种的丰度和纠正F/B比率失衡，CBM588可能介导了对ICI治疗的更好反应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a16deb1dc752dca76ce15dc5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"CBM588作为一种基于梭菌的活体生物制剂，在mRCC ICI治疗中的应用背景。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::618cb7487f6d9c41a8e420de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"使用Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes比率作为肠道菌群失调（dysbiosis）的衡量指标。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e95988c8996b35e4279714c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究仅分析了微生物组组成的变化，未直接报告临床疗效（如客观缓解率、无进展生存期）与微生物组变化的相关性，因此不能直接推断临床获益是由这些微生物变化介导的，只能说是提供了机制上的合理性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b33eb01193cd43e23b95260c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"样本量较小且来自两项I期试验的合并，可能存在选择偏倚或统计效力不足。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7e2209dfb8403e22d1a38190\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"F/B比率的变化方向在不同研究中可能有不同解读，需结合具体上下文。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::af35102db01eb2fc25e37a92\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所给摘要未交代是否进行了多重比较校正，P值结果需谨慎解读。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::77c5586d6a6da541552def5e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0143\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::890fce072a8f724aaec9108f\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08ad0f10b9a6304213fa3965\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::34d5ad06a0f4dbf0cd215280\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::33421e58bdd46bb513cd9861\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用分阶段的 I/II 期临床试验设计。Part A 为已完成的安全性评估阶段，纳入 12 名经 Safety Review Committee 审核的患者。Part B 为扩展招募阶段，针对 RCC、NSCLC 或膀胱癌患者。入组标准严格定义为 ICIs 耐药：即初始对 PD-1 通路靶向治疗有反应，但在最后一次给药后 12 周内出现由两次间隔至少 4 周的影像学扫描确认的疾病进展，且无快速临床进展。治疗方案为每日两次口服 MRx0518（1×10^10 至 1×10^11 CFU）联合每三周一次静脉注射 pembrolizumab（200 mg）。主要终点为第一周期治疗期间的毒性监测（安全性），次要终点包括客观缓解率（ORR）、缓解持续时间（DOR）、疾病控制率（DCR）和无进展生存期（PFS）。探索性终点涉及生物标志物、微生物组影响、总生存期（OS）以及与 PD-L1 CPS/TPS 的相关性。样本采集包括血液、粪便、尿液及可选的组织活检。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ba7d70347450f2d6caa42c1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了 MRx0518 在 ICIs 耐药实体瘤患者中与 pembrolizumab 联合使用的早期临床开发框架和部分安全性结论（Part A 完成并通过审查）。明确了此类难治性人群的定义标准和试验设计细节。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代任何具体的疗效数据、安全性不良事件详情或机制探索结果。Part B 仍在招募中，因此缺乏完整的临床结局证据。无法从当前材料中得出关于该疗法有效性的结论。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::857a3aff9040d0ca5274fd8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Part A: 12 名 mRCC 和 mNSCLC 患者，联合使用 MRx0518 与 pembrolizumab\",\n          \"finding\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的安全性数据结果、疗效数据（ORR, DCR, PFS 等）或生物标志物分析结果。仅陈述 Safety Review Committee 判定 Proceed to Part B 是适当的。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1f6fc071497e765cf0bf7f37\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fddd054cd361aa8965f6785\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"既往研究表明 MRx0518 具有免疫刺激作用，但在对免疫检查点抑制剂产生耐药性的实体瘤患者中，将其与 pembrolizumab 联合使用的安全性和潜在临床益处尚不明确。本研究试图解决如何逆转或克服 ICIs 耐药的问题。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc4609987a117e2afc41874f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）耐药的实体瘤患者，评估新型口服活体生物制剂 MRx0518（一种源自人肠道微生物群的 Enterococcus 属细菌）与 pembrolizumab 联合治疗的临床安全性及初步疗效。研究队列包括转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）、非小细胞肺癌（mNSCLC）和膀胱癌患者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74fdb746ae398fcc75225601\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文报告了一项 I/II 期临床试验的进展摘要。研究分为两部分：Part A 已完成，评估了 12 名 mRCC 和 mNSCLC 患者的联合治疗安全性；Part B 正在招募中，计划在每个适应症中额外招募最多 30 名患者。MRx0518 被选为开发候选药物是因为其体外和体内研究显示具有强效免疫刺激活性，能抑制肿瘤生长并调节 T 细胞分化。本研究旨在验证在 ICIs 耐药背景下，该联合疗法是否安全并能提供临床获益。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2806d2e7ae81fa8671642ad8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"由于缺乏疗效结果，不能证明 MRx0518 确实改善了耐药患者的预后。仅能说明这是一种正在进行的探索性策略。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了针对 ICIs 耐药实体瘤患者的具体临床干预方案（MRx0518 + pembrolizumab）。定义了“耐药”的临床操作标准（初始响应后进展，影像学确认，时间窗口限制）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3182795180c617396619901f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些机制描述来源于体外和动物模型的前体研究，而非本临床试验的直接发现。本摘要未提供本研究中实际观察到的机制关联数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"介绍了 MRx0518 的拟议作用机制基础（基于前体研究：减少 Treg，增加 Th1/Tc1，增加肿瘤内 CD4+/CD8+ T 细胞和 NK 细胞）。列出了探索性生物标志物收集计划（血液、粪便、组织活检以评估免疫标记和微生物组）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fae60c3135d79d2ec0ad8022\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"对 ICIs 耐药的具体定义：初始 PD-1 靶向治疗有益，但随后出现影像学确认的进展，且在末次给药后 12 周内发生，无快速临床恶化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdb1e41109948840959d1af2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MRx0518 作为一种单菌株口服活体生物制剂，已进入 I/II 期临床试验，并与 pembrolizumab 联用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::123238ea93afd3b66e33d152\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文仅为临床试验摘要，未包含 Part A 的具体安全性数据或 Part B 的任何疗效数据。所有关于“有效性”或“安全性结论”的推断均不可基于此材料。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::716270a739dcf95bd2590cd6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的免疫调节机制（Treg/Th1/Tc1 变化等）是基于前体研究（in vitro/in vivo models）的描述，并非本临床试验的实际结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9bf8d3adffc219b7809a76e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象限定为对 ICIs 耐药的实体瘤患者，结果外推至初治患者或其他癌症类型需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::609824f052eda0bd59878be5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0125\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f63dfcb79a3ed06be7080d88\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ae4ff46b42d0693e6d3e87c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31bcd1d7c5eddf4c0e908bd4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de3e4327fc150f8a04e4f48a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的I期临床试验设计（Part A部分）。入组标准为：既往接受过至少一种ICI治疗（单药或联合），且根据RECIST 1.1标准确认疾病稳定（SD）或进展（PD），但在最后一次ICI剂量后12周内无快速临床进展。治疗方案为口服MRx0518（1×10^10至1×10^11 CFU，每日两次）联合静脉注射帕博利珠单抗（200 mg，每3周一次），最多35个周期。安全性通过监测第一周期的毒性进行评估；疗效通过每9周一次的影像学评估（RECIST 1.1）确定ORR、DCR和PFS。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::12d23d367b3aa2af5ec2341e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了首个基于肠道微生物组的单菌株活体生物疗法MRx0518与ICI联合使用的早期临床数据，证实了该组合在难治性实体瘤中的可耐受性和初步疗效信号。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量极小（仅12名患者），仅为I期Part A部分的数据，缺乏对照组，无法确立因果效力或普遍适用性；随访时间较短，长期生存数据未知。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d8c05c0b76b07e9a430e62d2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"mRCC (n=9) 和 mNSCLC (n=3) 患者，中位既往治疗线数为3线，83%既往接受过纳武利尤单抗治疗，83%既往最佳反应为SD。\",\n          \"finding\": \"安全性方面：联合方案显示积极的 profiles，无治疗相关的严重不良事件（SAEs），无因毒性导致的药物停药，未报告irAEs增加。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::88dd55e8b41e1fb4a2b91e41\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"同一队列，数据截止日为2020年8月21日。\",\n          \"finding\": \"疗效方面：2名RCC患者和1名NSCLC患者达到部分缓解（PR）；另外2名RCC患者获得持久性疾病稳定（SD，分别为6个月和13个月）。协议定义的DCR为42%。中位PFS为2.14个月。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b06a57529aac98a77c03379a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::58164c8a42c60670eb2be979\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"评估源自肠道微生物组的单菌株活体生物疗法MRx0518与免疫检查点抑制剂帕博利珠单抗联合使用，在对ICI难治性实体瘤患者中的安全性和初步疗效；验证其作为“首次概念证明”（proof of concept）的潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3ee06848cac0ca5b43471cc4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究针对对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）难治性的实体瘤患者，具体包括转移性肾细胞癌（mRCC）和转移性非小细胞肺癌（mNSCLC）。研究对象为重度预处理的晚期癌症患者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b8755d691cbde8613902fde8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究是一项在临床开发阶段的活体生物疗法MRx0518与帕博利珠单抗（pembrolizumab）联合治疗实体瘤的I期临床试验摘要。MRx0518是一种源自人类肠道微生物组的单菌株活体生物疗法。研究旨在评估该联合方案的安全性及初步疗效信号。试验招募了既往接受过ICI治疗但疾病稳定或进展的患者，给予MRx0518胶囊与帕博利珠单抗联合治疗。主要终点为安全性，次要终点包括客观缓解率（ORR）、缓解持续时间（DOR）、疾病控制率（DCR）和无进展生存期（PFS）。结果显示联合方案耐受性良好，无治疗相关严重不良事件，并观察到初步的抗肿瘤活性信号。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2eb07e4515a6f6274042df72\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限I期小规模队列，未区分不同肿瘤类型的细微差异，且未提供长期生存数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了具体的临床案例证据：在ICI难治性实体瘤患者中，使用源自肠道微生物组的MRx0518联合帕博利珠单抗，实现了42%的疾病控制率和部分缓解，表明微生物疗法可能恢复或增强ICI的疗效。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a9da280b3a65057ec42b10c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述主要基于临床前小鼠模型和体外观察，临床样本中的具体分子通路验证程度在摘要中未详细展开。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了潜在的机制线索：摘要指出MRx0518通过激活肿瘤TLR5（与细菌鞭毛蛋白有关），诱导NFκB、细胞因子反应以及IFNγ+ CD4+和CD8+ T细胞的浸润，同时减少Tregs。这解释了微生物如何通过先天免疫受体激活适应性免疫反应。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cfe2ac8596053eb7b05cf92c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MRx0518的开发背景、靶点（TLR5）、以及其在难治性患者中的初步表现。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e5335bbb9e25a40d0f12e67b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MRx0518的单菌株特性及其特定的免疫调节作用（增加CD4+/CD8+ T细胞，减少Tregs）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2db21538e2237482eea7e051\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究仅为I期部分数据，样本量极小（n=12），结果具有高度不确定性，不能推广到所有实体瘤或所有ICI类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3a29df783d5f62b48b8745dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制描述主要基于临床前数据，临床层面的机制验证有限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3febee417218564a2917e173\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“首次概念证明”需结合后续更大规模的II期试验结果来评估其实际意义。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6ad237fc5e6520b4e44cd335\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0230\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::791f861f7c03887eb2ba1797\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e36b8ae8a47bfa189578b077\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1abb1f499d4b18e3ba0b2445\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c832fc4e8d623472abd78964\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、开放标签的早期临床试验设计。纳入标准：组织学确诊的实体瘤、计划进行手术切除、初治患者。干预措施：口服 MRx0518（1x10^10 至 1x10^11 CFU），每日两次，持续至术前一天（最长28天）。数据收集：记录不良事件以评估安全性；收集治疗前（诊断性活检）和治疗后（手术标本）的配对样本，利用 NanoString Pan Cancer IO 360™ 基因表达面板进行转录组分析，同时计划进行微生物组和代谢组分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee730c6fb553203920c4f1d3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了 MRx0518 在人类实体瘤患者中短期使用的安全性数据，证实了其良好的耐受性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量小（n=17），且仅分析了前 5 对样本的基因表达数据，缺乏统计效力来确立普遍性的免疫调节模式。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6914591d6c7a033541c2ca5c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"初步证据表明 MRx0518 可能在体内诱导与临床前模型相似的免疫激活信号（基因表达变化）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"基因表达变化的具体机制和功能后果尚未经过充分验证；未提供疗效（如肿瘤缩小）的直接证据，因为主要终点是安全性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a662b667b1877fd96be85eae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"确立了在新辅助设置中使用配对活检样本评估微生物疗法对宿主免疫影响的方法学可行性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"由于 COVID-19 疫情导致手术延迟，部分患者的治疗窗口可能受到影响，且后续 Part B 才包含安慰剂对照和更大规模的疗效评估。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::050ef7985358839115d23429\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Part A, n=17 (breast n=8, prostate n=4, uterine n=3, melanoma n=1, bladder n=1), treatment naive, solid tumours awaiting surgery\",\n          \"finding\": \"MRx0518 单药治疗显示出良好的安全性和耐受性，未报告 3/4 级 CTCAE 毒性，无严重不良反应或治疗中断。所有患者均接受了手术（3例因新冠疫情延迟）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d91e41044a5504a649b0790b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"First 5 paired samples analysed using NanoString Pan Cancer IO 360™ Gene Expression panel\",\n          \"finding\": \"在 48 个基因中观察到显著的基因表达谱变化（p < 0.05），提示免疫细胞浸润增加，这与临床前模型中的观察结果一致。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4430d5dc91f31190a4aac67\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a24fec7a0be7048481d6e85\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"评估 MRx0518 作为单药治疗在实体瘤患者中的安全性和耐受性；探索其是否能在人体内重现临床前观察到的免疫刺激效应，并识别潜在的疗效生物标志物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2ed91443e7efcd18fea2478a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"接受手术切除治疗的初治实体瘤患者（包括乳腺癌、前列腺癌、子宫内膜癌、黑色素瘤和膀胱癌），在术前新辅助阶段口服活体生物制剂 MRx0518。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c2cadd7907d1344788012875\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究是一项针对新型肠道微生物来源口服活体生物制剂 MRx0518 的早期临床试验，旨在评估其在实体瘤患者中的安全性和耐受性，并探索其对免疫微环境的潜在调节作用。MRx0518 源自粪肠球菌，临床前研究显示其能诱导 NK 细胞及 CD8+、CD4+ T 细胞的肿瘤浸润。本研究招募了 17 名初治患者，每日两次服用胶囊，直至术前一天。主要终点为安全性，次要探索性终点包括通过 NanoString 基因表达面板分析配对活检样本中的基因表达变化、微生物组分析及代谢标志物检测。结果显示药物耐受性良好，且初步基因分析显示部分患者存在显著的免疫相关基因表达改变。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76a06f54ec53518c2fd3f0d8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限 Part A 的前 5 对样本分析，未涉及与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）联合用药的实际疗效数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了 MRx0518 在实体瘤患者中诱导免疫相关基因表达变化的初步人体数据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::450256474c35f73fc1d99d21\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制推断基于基因表达谱，而非直接的因果实验（如细胞因子测定或功能实验）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"揭示了 MRx0518 可能通过上调特定免疫基因（48个显著变化基因）来介导免疫刺激，支持其作为免疫佐剂的潜力。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dfe1ba291db24589843418c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MRx0518 的临床前有效性数据（小鼠模型中的肿瘤生长减少和免疫细胞浸润）及其在人体中的安全性概况。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::02c73f928a808336678dd89e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"本研究仅评估 MRx0518 单药的安全性，而提及正在进行的与其他疗法（如 ICI）的组合试验。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dd97f6a487160acdff3ecad1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究未直接测试 MRx0518 与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的联合疗效，因此不能直接回答 F1 中关于“调节 ICI 疗效”的核心问题，只能提供潜在的机制基础。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60476a33589b69030f041294\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"基因表达变化的样本量极小（n=5），结果具有探索性，不应被视为确证的生物学标志物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff1c3e9435300c89bc14e0e3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"COVID-19 导致的延误可能引入了混杂因素，尽管主要结论基于安全性，但需注意治疗依从性或时长的潜在变异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24455e3eb4ee44719fa5d1b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“免疫细胞浸润增加”是基于基因表达数据的推断，需结合其他独立验证数据（如流式细胞术或免疫组化）才能确证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b72dfac1acebcb739cc06f8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0244\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"local source was absent or unreadable\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::20309b87fd0e8cfe50d8893d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b674221023c1dbcd1a299114\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c2620bcc444fc1598dd43ce6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f036c918cd390f5edcdaebe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用还原论视角，从生态水平的菌群相关性分析转向分子水平的机制解析。具体路线包括：1) 梳理建立相关性的大规模测序研究和动物模型实验；2) 验证相关性并识别宿主表型（如CD8+ T细胞浸润）；3) 深入探讨具体的分子机制，分为T细胞刺激、髓系细胞刺激和分子模拟三个子主题；4) 评估基于分子机制的工程化益生菌应用前景。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e6663c1509a79bf070ff83d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统性地从分类学相关性过渡到分子机制，详细列举了多种微生物代谢物和蛋白质如何通过特定受体（GPCRs, A2AR, STING, NOD2, TLR5）和信号通路影响宿主免疫系统。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略和纳入排除标准；主要依赖已发表的小鼠模型和少量临床数据，缺乏大规模前瞻性干预试验的直接证据；对于非细菌类微生物（真菌、古菌）及抑制性微生物的关注不足。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::efc4edd784b59555aab5bd43\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"小鼠模型及患者队列中的相关性研究\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定细菌属（如双歧杆菌、拟杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、普拉梭菌）的存在与ICB疗效正相关，但不同研究间结果存在异质性，且相关性不等于因果性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39351d21f351bf132aaa24af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"粪菌移植（FMT）和单菌定植实验\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自响应者的FMT可重现抗肿瘤效应，增加肿瘤内CD8+ T细胞浸润；特定菌株（如A. muciniphila, Bifidobacterium spp.）的单菌定植足以增强ICB疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a2ad8f127a3e2f7fb383b60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）的作用\",\n          \"finding\": \"SCFAs（如丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有双重性：通常促进Treg和效应T细胞分化，但在某些情况下（如抗CTLA-4治疗）可能产生负面影响。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4abe48e8e01b0acc7b17e16a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肌苷（Inosine）通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"B. pseudolongum等产生的肌苷通过结合T细胞上的A2AR受体，协同TLR9激动剂增强抗CTLA-4疗效，但单独使用不足以完全重现表型。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::44f2d548690b4b10bf73e2c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Akkermansia muciniphila与STING通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"A. muciniphila产生cdAMP，激活STING信号，诱导I型干扰素产生，招募NK细胞和树突状细胞，从而增强抗肿瘤免疫。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e7fda87890cf100670bbed03\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Enterococcus sagA蛋白与NOD2通路\",\n          \"finding\": \"肠球菌表达的SagA蛋白降解肽聚糖产生muropeptides，激活宿主NOD2受体，促进炎症环境和CD8+ T细胞浸润。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4a33dc878424e5c612918cf2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"分子模拟机制\",\n          \"finding\": \"E. hirae中的噬菌体尾长测量蛋白（TMP）含有与宿主PSMB4蛋白相似的表位，引发交叉反应性CD8+ T细胞，增强抗PD-1疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41b69dd74275e596257e7f30\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ecae2ad21b9875306feb272\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知特定微生物群与ICB疗效相关，但确切的分子机制尚不清楚，这限制了将微生物作为精准医疗手段加以利用的能力。本文试图回答：哪些具体的微生物分子特征（蛋白质、酶、代谢物）介导了这种调节作用？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::68dac395c061b642520773c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"人类微生物群（特别是肠道菌群）与癌症免疫治疗中免疫检查点阻断（ICB，如抗PD-1/PD-L1和抗CTLA-4抗体）疗效之间的关系。研究范围涵盖从宏观的菌群组成相关性到微观的分子机制（代谢物、蛋白质、抗原模拟），以及基于这些机制的工程化益生菌策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c8095064895dfad406e569df\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在总结宿主-微生物相互作用在检查点抑制剂免疫治疗背景下的分子理解进展。文章首先回顾了通过小鼠模型和患者队列建立的菌群与ICB疗效之间的相关性，指出仅凭分类学关联难以确定因果关系。随后，重点阐述了具体的微生物分子机制，包括短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）、肌苷（inosine）、环二腺苷酸（cdAMP）、肽聚糖片段（muropeptides）和鞭毛蛋白（flagellin）如何分别通过T细胞刺激、髓系细胞激活或分子模拟来增强抗肿瘤免疫。最后，讨论了利用这些分子特征设计下一代工程化益生菌以改善治疗反应的潜力，并指出了当前研究在真菌/古菌、抑制性微生物及远端器官微生物方面的局限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::599e6bf17709ba8cfbd90929\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些机制大多基于小鼠模型或体外实验，部分已在早期临床试验中探索（如MRx0518），但尚未成为标准治疗指南；不同菌株间存在显著差异，不能简单外推至所有同种细菌。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物群影响ICB疗效的具体生物学途径和关键分子中介。例如，明确了A. muciniphila通过cdAMP-STING轴、肠球菌通过SagA-NOD2轴、以及双歧杆菌通过肌苷-A2AR轴增强抗肿瘤免疫的具体机制。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a57617739887231108e77d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制的复杂性在于多种微生物可能通过相同或不同的路径产生相似效果（冗余性），且单一代谢物往往不足以完全重现体内复杂的生态效应（如肌苷需配合TLR9激动剂）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细描述了介导效应的具体分子机制，包括代谢物（SCFAs, inosine, cdAMP）、蛋白质（SagA, flagellin）和抗原模拟（TMP）。解释了这些分子如何被宿主受体识别并触发下游信号级联反应（如I型干扰素产生、Th1分化、CD8+ T细胞浸润）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4eb4f4671e999f3795550859\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出目前大多数研究集中在细菌，而忽略了真菌、古菌以及具有免疫抑制作用的负相关微生物；同时提到了远端器官（如肿瘤内部）微生物群的潜在作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::07f07877dcebdfd835240f4c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"对比了生态方法（FMT、饮食调整、定义菌群）与还原论方法（小分子、工程化益生菌）的优缺点。指出前者面临标准化和个体差异挑战，后者更具精准性但开发难度大。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3730e786b8b2831b6d7fa00a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的许多机制（如cdAMP, SagA）主要在小鼠模型中验证，其在人体内的确切效力和安全性仍需更多临床数据支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e90d9bb4a7244676654bef0a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者强调“还原论”方法的优势，但这并不意味着生态方法无效，两者应被视为互补而非对立。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3abfe02af60077a50b3004b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"不同菌株甚至同一物种的不同菌株之间可能存在巨大的功能差异（如Bifidobacterium bifidum的不同菌株对PD-1阻断的影响不同），因此在引用具体机制时需严格限定菌株来源。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0d593217581a78566b8d13de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"SCFAs（特别是丁酸盐）对ICB的影响具有情境依赖性（如对CTLA-4可能有负面作用），不能一概而论地认为其总是有益。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::54d4ead502cd94815f6b6dba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0251\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a711d661f19a142c0c3e45ea\",\n          \"snapshot::6c9adb8dafbf57ee773f2f09\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ea94ae88d96da7375e03d569\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bb807576934b684cfc560ae0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7199bd6117295d60e2e20818\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 临床队列：选取MET4-IO试验中接受MET4+ICI联合治疗的患者（n=23有配对样本），分为MET4组、ICI对照组、高/低IgG反应者亚组及定植成功/失败亚组。 2. 抗体检测：使用CFSE标记MET4细菌，与不同稀释度的患者血浆孵育，通过流式细胞术检测IgA和IgG的结合强度（MFI）和频率，计算响应指数（RI）。 3. 菌群分析：对治疗前后粪便进行宏基因组测序，分析整体菌群多样性及MET4特定菌株的相对丰度变化；对经流式分选的IgG结合/未结合细菌组分进行16S rRNA测序，鉴定被抗体结合的特定菌种。 4. 免疫表型分析：利用质谱流式细胞术（CyTOF）对PBMCs进行多参数分析，比较不同IgG反应组别在治疗前后免疫细胞亚群（如B细胞、CD4+ T细胞、单核细胞等）的频率变化。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::88c3d7422c083be143d6c7c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"证实了口服细菌联合体MET4能在人体中诱导特异性的全身性IgG免疫反应，且该反应与特定有益菌的丰度增加及免疫细胞亚群的重塑相关。\",\n          \"limits\": \"1. 早期阶段试验，样本量小（仅23例配对分析），统计效力不足，无法得出关于临床疗效（如生存期、肿瘤缩小）的结论。 2. 存在多种肿瘤类型混杂因素。 3. 抗体检测方法在处理复杂微生物群落时可能存在保留率偏差（Type II error风险），导致某些菌种的抗体反应被低估。 4. 未能直接证明诱导的抗体具有抗肿瘤功能，仅作为系统性免疫激活的标志物。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8a9048b4f7faa99ae05b0687\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"MET4治疗组 vs ICI对照组\",\n          \"finding\": \"MET4治疗显著提高了循环抗MET4 IgG的反应强度和频率，而IgA无显著变化；总血浆IgG浓度在各组间无差异。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ac8729af8b35f74e846875eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"高IgG反应者（RI>3, n=5）vs 其他组\",\n          \"finding\": \"高IgG反应者表现出更高的肠道菌群Shannon多样性增加，且特定MET4菌株（如C. aerofaciens, B. adolescentis）的相对丰度增加更显著。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::085f047b2dfff42aa898e3c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"IgG结合组分分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"尽管C. aerofaciens等菌在粪便中丰度增加并与高IgG相关，但它们并未在IgG结合的细菌组分中富集；相反，Acidaminococcus在IgG结合组分中显著富集，尽管其整体定植效果有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::017b5e3aa522884b5f3d2b79\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"外周血免疫亚群变化\",\n          \"finding\": \"高IgG反应者在MET4治疗后显示出循环B细胞和FoxP3+ CD4+ T细胞的显著增加，以及CD14+和CD16+单核细胞的减少；这些变化在治疗前不存在。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad2edab2bba30c1a1111dafc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d6aa4c7c10f6272b2fbe4e28\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. MET4细菌联合体能否在接受ICI治疗的实体瘤患者中诱导特异性的循环抗体反应？2. 这种抗体反应是否与肠道内MET4菌株的定植（engraftment）或特定菌属丰度的变化相关？3. 特异性抗体反应是否与外周血中免疫细胞亚群（如B细胞、T细胞、单核细胞）的分布变化有关联？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::baffeb683c983156110161c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对晚期实体瘤患者，研究在免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗背景下，口服细菌联合体MET4对系统性免疫反应的影响。研究对象为MET4-IO临床试验队列B中的30名ICI初治患者，分析样本包括治疗前后的血浆、外周血单个核细胞（PBMCs）和粪便。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6c73b08080a9cd312b52c64\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在评估新型微生物疗法MET4是否能诱导特异性的全身性体液免疫反应，并探索其与肠道菌群定植及循环免疫亚群变化的关联。研究利用抗微生物抗体流式细胞术检测血浆中针对MET4的IgG/IgA反应，结合宏基因组测序分析粪便菌群变化，并通过质谱流式细胞术评估PBMCs中免疫细胞亚群的动态变化。结果显示，MET4治疗显著提高了部分患者的抗MET4 IgG水平，高IgG反应者与特定有益菌（如Collinsella aerofaciens）丰度增加及B细胞、调节性T细胞增多相关，但IgG主要结合的对象并非这些定植成功的菌种，提示可能存在异源免疫刺激机制。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::95758ded15cecd4e3d7edfe7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅针对MET4这一特定联合体，且为早期安全性/定植试验，非疗效确证性试验。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了细菌联合体干预后，宿主产生特异性循环抗体的量化数据（RI指数、MFI变化），并展示了高反应者与特定菌群（C. aerofaciens等）丰度增加的关联。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::469f4cbdeb5bc3ad719bb7a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制为相关性观察，非因果验证；体外结合实验不能完全代表体内功能；质谱流式面板有限，未涵盖所有免疫亚群。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"通过IgG结合分选和16S测序，发现抗体主要结合Acidaminococcus而非丰度增加的C. aerofaciens，提出“定植菌作为佐剂激发针对其他菌或自身成分的异源抗体反应”的机制假说。同时记录了高IgG反应者外周B细胞和FoxP3+ T细胞增加、单核细胞减少的免疫重塑现象。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e1080a999c057765ab89992\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了抗微生物抗体流式细胞术的具体操作流程（CFSE标记、血浆稀释、二级抗体染色）及质谱流式在免疫亚群分析中的应用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04daf3518eaf2243919fef62\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了“adjuvant taxa”（佐剂样菌）概念，即某些菌通过模式识别受体激活APC，进而引发广泛的系统性免疫反应，甚至包括针对其他菌的抗体。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::28d75a84749b754609b5e997\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为早期相位（Phase I/II）试验，主要终点是安全性和定植，而非客观缓解率（ORR）或总生存期（OS）。因此，任何关于“MET4提高ICI疗效”的推论均缺乏直接临床结局数据支持，仅能推断其具备免疫激活潜力。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a102ea7c99ecf5904b039720\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"抗体反应的高变异性（仅5人显示高反应）提示个体差异极大，外推至一般人群时需考虑宿主基线免疫状态的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d77f50d5341d6ed41b9423ff\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"IgG结合分选实验中提到的“保留率偏差”意味着未被检测到的菌种可能同样具有免疫原性，解读“谁激发了抗体”时需保持谨慎，避免绝对化结论。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::917c178d07989db3d53e4bdd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0122\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5c752c0f8036d5742e42\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5f82ba52a99d38e52a55\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-5bcddf895da96806b16c\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::73efa1be4be250cf312dbe78\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32afad53dcf43f0b6c9b72e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0bfb82785a3c48347dccebf7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::df7c1c8cdb1b19415f16bd7c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性综述方法，梳理已发表的临床试验数据（包括已完成和正在进行的研究）。作者按干预类型（益生菌、菌群组合、FMT）分类整理证据，对比各试验的设计、患者人群、疗效指标（ORR, mPFS）及不良事件。同时，结合讨论部分，分析导致临床结果不一致的原因（如物种特异性、定植能力、抗生素预处理的影响），并评估当前监管框架和研究方法论（如小鼠模型的局限性）对转化研究的制约。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad144ff01b7112fa74c4f766\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于微生物疗法作为ICI辅助治疗的全景式临床证据汇总，特别是区分了益生菌、菌群组合和FMT在不同实体瘤中的表现差异。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对机制的解释主要基于作者对现有文献的综合推断，具体分子通路尚不明确；所引用的临床试验多为小样本或早期阶段，统计效力有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::18fce5dbd3407432b774c9dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了当前领域面临的非科学障碍，如监管标准不适用于复杂微生物产品、患者招募困难及抗生素预处理策略的潜在风险。\",\n          \"limits\": \"这些观点属于领域内的共识性讨论，并非该综述独有的实证发现；对于如何解决这些系统性问题，仅提出了方向性建议（如AI建模、标准化供体筛选），未提供具体解决方案。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e026da3395f4a6e48096eefc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用单一或少数菌株益生菌（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在某些特定癌种（如转移性肾细胞癌）中显示出较高的ORR提升（58%-74% vs 对照20%），但在其他癌种（如微卫星稳定型结直肠癌）中效果不佳或无效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ffe37d5b7bd2ed2749dc96b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用多菌株微生物菌群组合（如MET4, SER-401, VE800）\",\n          \"finding\": \"结果高度异质。MET4在部分队列中显示潜在获益，但受限于招募失败；SER-401因早期终止且初步数据显示疗效不优于安慰剂而终止；VE800整体ORR极低（1.9%），仅在黑色素瘤亚组中观察到一定益处。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e58ae790bec32ee11a9df4c4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用粪便微生物移植（FMT）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在多种难治性实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、MSI-H癌症等）中显示出一致的积极信号，ORR普遍较高（20%-77%），且安全性总体可控，提示其可能具有广谱抗肿瘤活性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1cdfbbb48f5f9c98936fc044\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"机制研究与模型转化\",\n          \"finding\": \"目前缺乏明确的单一因果细菌物种；机制涉及T细胞浸润、代谢物（如短链脂肪酸）产生及免疫基因集变化。小鼠模型与人类微生物组差异巨大，限制了直接外推。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e9de08819bb3b4ed6078f1fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2827d99d3dcf98657562d9b2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICI疗法改变了部分实体瘤的治疗格局，但其对“冷”肿瘤或无响应患者的效果有限。本研究旨在解决如何安全有效地将微生物疗法作为ICI的辅助手段，以扩大受益人群并克服耐药性问题。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::897420d152a1f4691a65b58e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"固体肿瘤患者中，肠道微生物群作为免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）辅助治疗的临床前与临床研究现状。涵盖益生菌、微生物菌群组合及粪便微生物移植（FMT）三种主要干预手段。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::10082b6cc311135dbfe6dcf1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述，旨在评估通过调节肠道微生物群来增强固体肿瘤免疫治疗疗效的潜力。文章系统回顾了基于单菌株/有限混合物的益生菌（如CBM588、EDP1503）、多菌株微生物菌群组合（如MET4、SER-401、VE800）以及全环境粪便微生物移植（FMT）在联合ICI治疗中的临床试验结果。研究重点分析了不同干预策略在客观缓解率（ORR）、无进展生存期（mPFS）及安全性方面的表现，并探讨了从动物模型到人体转化的挑战、监管障碍、患者招募困难以及现有机制理解的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3a7be2d0ab0883257f020f7a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些数据来自小样本早期临床试验，存在选择偏倚和统计效力不足的问题。不能据此断定某种特定菌株在所有情况下均有效或无效。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了三类微生物干预策略在多种实体瘤中与ICI联用的临床疗效对比数据。具体而言，指出FMT在多种难治性肿瘤中表现出较一致的ORR提升（20-77%），而益生菌和菌群组合的效果则呈现高度的癌种特异性和菌株依赖性（如CBM588在mRCC有效但在MSS CRC无效，VE800整体无效）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e7a08fe8d3267d2e0ff0d6a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"机制描述多为相关性观察或基于动物模型的推测，文中明确承认“大部分未知”。不能将这些关联视为已证实的因果机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"讨论了微生物调节ICI疗效的可能机制线索，包括T细胞浸润增加、抗原呈递细胞（APCs）积累、IL-8产生髓系细胞减少以及短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）等代谢物的作用。同时指出目前缺乏单一因果物种的证据，倾向于网络效应和功能冗余。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6150bc781f7918a9915bfded\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"介绍了ICI的作用原理（PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4抑制，T细胞增殖）及其在“冷”肿瘤中的局限性。定义了“热”与“冷”肿瘤的概念，并引入肠道微生物群作为潜在的共治疗手段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf5d9ab2e65ee7a5c7b0216a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"批评了传统还原论方法（寻找单一因果基因/蛋白）在微生物研究中的失效，提出需要机器学习/AI模型来处理微生物组的复杂性，并指出小鼠模型与人类微生物组的差异是转化研究的瓶颈。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c024714554d6bd9bfa71d6cf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"详细描述了微生物疗法在临床试验中面临的监管难题（难以标准化复现的产品）、患者招募困难以及抗生素预处理带来的潜在危害（如SER-401试验中的负面结果）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb21724cdddb728c61b9904e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要关注细菌疗法，虽提及真菌、古菌和病毒，但未深入展开，阅读时需限定在细菌层面。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b5bf19d3d412ec4c9e5076d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所有临床数据均为早期阶段（Phase I/II）或小样本研究，结果存在较大不确定性，不可将其视为确证性证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3da6b2c628061aac471cc4ce\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者强调FMT效果较好，但这可能源于FMT引入了更多样的菌群而非特定成分，需谨慎归因。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aff3ce7e2f53b8c83f7866ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的“抗生素预处理”在SER-401试验中被证明可能有害，这一反面案例对于设计微生物干预方案具有重要警示意义。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c1253fcac84e6039a9d7c2a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0387\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::2982acd184049ed5bf73367d\",\n          \"snapshot::b108064ede6712f9e766ace8\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b77b4bb509e05a0fbc26248\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7c746f64a2e9e1ee9376c1bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::009b8c762617bca488678bdf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a narrative review, the authors systematically summarize and categorize existing literature rather than conducting a new systematic meta-analysis. The approach involves: (1) reviewing preclinical mouse models to establish causal links between specific bacteria and ICI response; (2) analyzing human observational cohort studies to identify associations between microbiota composition (taxa and diversity) and clinical outcomes (response vs. non-response); (3) synthesizing proposed biological mechanisms (T-cell activation, mimicry, metabolites); and (4) evaluating early-phase clinical trial data for microbiome interventions (FMT, consortia, diet). The review explicitly compares findings across different studies to highlight inconsistencies in biomarker discovery and emphasizes the need for standardized methodologies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::45cafb54dc0b22611aed0da9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of preclinical and clinical evidence linking the gut microbiome to ICI efficacy and toxicity, categorizing mechanisms into three distinct themes.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it does not perform a quantitative meta-analysis; it highlights the lack of consensus in human biomarker studies rather than resolving it.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d12797a4caef170c2b7834bb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Critically evaluates the limitations of current human studies, including small sample sizes, geographic biases, and analytical pipeline differences, advocating for standardized large-scale datasets.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Does not provide definitive answers on which specific microbial signatures are universally predictive across all solid tumor types.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a0404a5b8c8e5b2a74dec45\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes early-phase clinical trial data for various microbiome interventions (FMT, consortia, diet), offering a landscape of current therapeutic developments.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Most clinical trial data reported are from early-phase (I/II) studies with small sample sizes; long-term efficacy and safety profiles are not yet established.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b4bed6075da6fb337a1b29ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific commensals (e.g., Bifidobacterium spp., Akkermansia muciniphila, Bacteroides fragilis) enhance anti-PD-1 or anti-CTLA-4 efficacy via dendritic cell activation, STING pathway signaling, and modulation of T-cell subsets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9c9912d42b9680ae59616b6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Human observational studies (Melanoma, NSCLC, RCC)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders to ICIs often show higher abundance of specific taxa (e.g., Faecalibacterium, Ruminococcaceae, A. muciniphila), but there is no consensus on a universal predictive signature due to cohort-specific variations, geographic differences, and methodological heterogeneity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::db8e6cda2084f9d7f422abcc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Antibiotic use during ICI therapy\",\n          \"finding\": \"Broad-spectrum antibiotic use is consistently associated with reduced progression-free survival and overall survival in ICI-treated patients, likely due to depletion of beneficial microbes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::90e8fc2f9e0b82ab3be5b470\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways\",\n          \"finding\": \"Three primary mechanisms are identified: (1) direct stimulation of antitumor T-cells; (2) molecular mimicry between bacterial and tumor antigens; (3) production of immunomodulatory metabolites like short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs), secondary bile acids, and inosine.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7616bc1463f0ae6cf17cc69a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Immune-related adverse events (irAEs)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbiota profiles are linked to irAEs, particularly colitis. For example, certain Firmicutes are associated with anti-CTLA-4 colitis, and Streptococcus abundance correlates with arthritis and poor prognosis.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1443271fa1da60a509c70ae2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical trials of FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from responders to PD-1 refractory melanoma patients can restore sensitivity to PD-1 inhibitors, with some patients achieving objective responses, though engraftment stability varies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::36650677a8cc9186fdd6e51b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c322d10b5ee066c7278d227\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review addresses the question of how the gut microbiome impacts the efficacy and toxicity of cancer immunotherapies, aiming to consolidate preclinical and clinical evidence to understand the rationale for microbiome-targeted therapies and identify gaps in current knowledge regarding predictive biomarkers and mechanistic pathways.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ebd7242a0ff0d64e461f0432\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the role of the gut microbiome in modulating responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) targeting PD-1/PD-L1 and CTLA-4 in patients with advanced solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, GI cancers). It covers preclinical evidence from mouse models, observational human data linking microbiota composition to clinical outcomes and adverse events, potential biological mechanisms, and early-phase clinical trials of microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cc2c2c28c1caba96afb475d0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This review synthesizes current knowledge on how the gut microbiome influences cancer immunotherapy. It begins by summarizing preclinical studies demonstrating that specific commensal bacteria enhance ICI efficacy through T-cell stimulation and metabolite production. It then reviews human observational studies, highlighting the inconsistent identification of predictive microbial signatures across different cohorts and cancer types, while noting the negative impact of broad-spectrum antibiotics. The paper outlines three main mechanistic themes: direct T-cell stimulation, molecular mimicry, and immunomodulatory metabolites (e.g., SCFAs, bile acids, inosine). It also discusses the microbiome's role in immune-related adverse events (irAEs), particularly colitis. Finally, it evaluates emerging therapeutic strategies, including fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), defined bacterial consortia, probiotics, and dietary interventions, based on results from early-phase clinical trials.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e13747845e98cdad4946f3fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The association is correlational in humans; causality is primarily established in mouse models. Predictive signatures are not consistent across all studies or cancer types.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides evidence that specific gut bacteria (e.g., Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia, Faecalibacterium) are associated with improved response to PD-1/CTLA-4 inhibitors in melanoma, NSCLC, and RCC. It details how broad-spectrum antibiotics negatively impact ICI efficacy.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dd2cd58c619336074abe9073\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from preclinical mouse models; human validation is ongoing. The relative contribution of each mechanism in humans is not fully quantified.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Outlines three mechanistic categories: (1) Direct T-cell stimulation (e.g., via DC activation or TLR signaling); (2) Molecular mimicry (cross-reactive T-cells); (3) Metabolite production (SCFAs, bile acids, inosine) influencing the tumor microenvironment and systemic immunity.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::70d726c889969cd08f8f7c50\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Links are largely observational; causal relationships for non-colitis irAEs are less established.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discusses the role of the microbiome in irAEs, specifically colitis and arthritis, linking specific taxa (e.g., Firmicutes, Streptococcus) to these toxicities.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::60cc01cd7a6971e06ac2562f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Data are from small, early-phase trials; long-term durability and optimal donor selection criteria are not yet resolved.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Reports early clinical trial results for FMT and defined consortia (e.g., CBM588, SER-401) showing potential to restore ICI sensitivity in refractory patients.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4289eb606de8ce121a145709\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of cohort-specific microbial signatures, geographic effects (enterotypes), and methodological heterogeneity (sequencing pipelines, response definitions).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::80c703ff4721ceb9517b1e60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Details on high-fiber diets, ketogenic diets, and fasting-mimicking diets affecting microbiota composition and ICI outcomes.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4bc8badb56ceb9668c0d36b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Table 2 listing various trials (FMT, consortia, probiotics, prebiotics) with their phases, indications, and products.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1ce8fe5bdd1c0d404d911837\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review covers multiple solid tumor types (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, GI cancers); findings may not be generalizable to hematologic malignancies or other cancer types not discussed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::14c17ad9e4bf0d56c7a4595b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Human data are primarily observational associations; causal claims should be attributed to preclinical models unless supported by interventional trial data.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a6aa372fb235e79e846179ea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Biomarker findings are inconsistent across studies; do not present any single taxon as a definitive universal predictor without noting the cohort-specific nature of the evidence.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0a9592c21283fd2c275d56d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Clinical trial results are from early phases; avoid overstating efficacy or safety based on small sample sizes.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::28906915f0b362e419938664\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c96dcd391e3ff6d5952be10a\",\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::922e43319a447a37576a6465\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0261\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::eb5aa52fd3ffd49fe0ad1176\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05c869a01ed92554d02725a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4e2333ff838fdd806b55bdd7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6d2370498917430fe1ce20f1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conduct a narrative review synthesizing literature from structural biology, immunology, oncology, and biomanufacturing. They organize the content by: 1) Structural determinants of bioactivity; 2) Four mechanistic axes of ICI sensitization; 3) Clinical and preclinical evidence; 4) Translational bottlenecks (heterogeneity, PK/PD, trial design); 5) Future strategies (AI, synthetic biology, nanodelivery). They compare polysaccharides with mainstream immunostimulants and contextualize findings within Technology Readiness Levels (TRLs).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a6b20904a951e3029bf63694\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive framework linking polysaccharide structure (ESAR) to immune function and ICI synergy, categorizing mechanisms into four distinct axes.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a review, it synthesizes existing data rather than generating new experimental evidence; clinical validation is limited to early-phase/small-sample studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bc8fd0b296c3aa429b0f019\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific translational bottlenecks (structural heterogeneity, low bioavailability) and proposes advanced technical solutions (AI glycomics, synthetic biology, nanodelivery).\",\n          \"limits\": \"Proposed solutions like Industry 6.0 integration and AI models are largely theoretical or in early development stages; practical implementation details are not yet established.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3c0aa376fdfa2017167426d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Contextualizes polysaccharides against other adjuvants (CpG, STING agonists, FMT) and defines their niche in terms of safety and tolerability.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Direct head-to-head comparative clinical data between polysaccharides and these other agents are sparse; comparisons are often based on separate study contexts.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::28653169b560c809e93eab96\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Fungal beta-glucans\",\n          \"finding\": \"Intact triple-helix conformation is essential for Dectin-1 binding and immune activation; extraction-induced disruption abolishes activity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7dad710dbd3bef9cd89ec24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Plant/Marine polysaccharides\",\n          \"finding\": \"C-2/C-3 acetylation or sulfation degree are key determinants of TLR4/MyD88 signaling intensity and ROS scavenging.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9ed22b067d4d6149e1368f28\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Gut microbiota modulation\",\n          \"finding\": \"Polysaccharides act as prebiotics to enrich beneficial taxa (e.g., Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and increase SCFA production, which synergizes with anti-PD-1 therapy; effects are microbiota-dependent.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e947d43bd1da1a68deb89a35\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical evidence\",\n          \"finding\": \"Early-phase trials show promise (e.g., ORR 21.7% in refractory NSCLC with beta-glucan + envafolimab), but large-scale Phase III RCTs are absent; most strategies remain at TRL 3-5.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bae5619bf50fe0fc4b949c3d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Safety considerations\",\n          \"finding\": \"Excessive intake of fermentable fibers in dysbiotic models may induce cholestatic liver cancer via SCFA accumulation, highlighting a dose-dependent safety boundary.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24fec8d8f2c82155a45e835c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a7aad00488e11d4a7c07f3f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"How can natural polysaccharides be rationally designed and utilized to overcome primary and acquired resistance to ICIs in solid tumors, given their complex structures and variable clinical outcomes?\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::00a97cdd8f787cbe68b388cb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Natural polysaccharides (from fungi, plants, marine organisms) as immune adjuvants to overcome resistance to Immune Checkpoint Inhibitors (ICIs) in solid tumors. Covers structural biology, molecular mechanisms, preclinical/clinical evidence, translational challenges, and future technological directions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0c136f05c57c534c85bdf1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This review systematically analyzes the potential of natural polysaccharides to enhance the efficacy of ICIs by reversing tumor immune resistance. It dissects the structure-activity relationships (SAR) governing immunomodulation, elaborates on four core mechanisms (TAM repolarization, CD8+ T cell rejuvenation, gut microbiota remodeling, and suppression of tumor-intrinsic escape), and evaluates current clinical translation bottlenecks such as structural heterogeneity and low bioavailability. The paper positions polysaccharides within the broader landscape of combination therapies, compares them with other adjuvants, and proposes a roadmap for precision medicine using AI-driven glycomics, synthetic biology, and multi-layer biomarkers.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee7e3572d67dbf2f67526363\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Introduction sections detailing primary/acquired resistance rates, limitations of CAR-T and kinase inhibitors, and the need for novel adjuvants.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17a10ba46be35c4952913371\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Section 5.1 comparing polysaccharides with dual checkpoint blockade, TIM-3 targeting, and oncolytic viruses in terms of efficacy and safety profiles.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fb8e4e0564c5b23f7abc6821\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Sections 6.3-6.6 discussing AI-driven QSAR, graph neural networks, synthetic biology, and large-scale N-glycomics.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::757541f80ab481e594311373\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Most evidence is preclinical (mouse models) or from small early-phase human trials; causal links in humans are inferred from FMT experiments and observational cohorts.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the role of gut microbiota in mediating ICI response, specifically highlighting how polysaccharides remodel microbial composition (enriching Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolite profiles (increasing SCFAs like butyrate and propionate) to enhance anti-tumor immunity.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::000bb7f76afc0e764242ec8f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Mechanisms are often derived from in vitro or syngeneic mouse models; direct translation to human clinical outcomes is not fully validated.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Elaborates on the molecular mechanisms of polysaccharide-mediated immunomodulation, including TAM repolarization (M2 to M1), CD8+ T cell exhaustion reversal, and suppression of tumor-intrinsic escape (PD-L1 downregulation). Links these to specific structural motifs (triple helix, acetylation).\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d2525176a96ae5b3ac60e2bc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Based on specific dysbiotic mouse models; human relevance requires further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discusses the safety boundaries and risks associated with polysaccharide/fiber supplementation, noting that excessive fermentation in dysbiotic guts may lead to adverse outcomes like cholestatic liver cancer.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3eefb31b9abaa8d1b9d67ad1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on natural polysaccharides; do not generalize findings to all prebiotics or dietary fibers without specifying the polysaccharide type.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f2c5255f64a830040e1f35d7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Clinical evidence is primarily from early-phase trials or real-world retrospective studies; avoid overstating efficacy as if confirmed by Phase III RCTs.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e35d942ffc4974b5cd35989\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic claims are largely supported by preclinical models; distinguish between observed associations in mice and validated causal mechanisms in humans.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::20a0ba2e568287fb9bf43378\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Safety warnings (e.g., liver cancer risk) are based on specific dysbiotic conditions; do not assume universal toxicity.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::90e1b843a34aa7ed7dd51615\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0152\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-edcd953058d1d5fa5081\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-847338f921b68453cb16\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::75c05d10f04491719965663b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a5c92501d12e494997ee0cc3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3d2faddc32ac2b1e893da40c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b37713eabcf85e9c66591d0b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇综述（Review）。作者通过梳理现有文献，系统阐述了肠道微生物组与宿主免疫系统之间的相互作用机制，重点分析了特定微生物物种、代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸）以及菌群失调对抗PD-1免疫治疗疗效的影响。文章进一步归纳了基于微生物组的干预策略，包括粪便微生物群移植（FMT）、饮食干预和益生菌使用，并讨论了其在黑色素瘤治疗中的潜力与挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::76dfb64da820177736fc01a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"综合了肠道微生物组影响抗PD-1疗法疗效的多种机制，包括T细胞激活、代谢物调节及免疫检查点表达调控；汇总了FMT、饮食和益生菌等干预策略的临床前及早期临床研究证据；明确了特定菌种（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium）和菌群多样性作为预测生物标志物的潜在价值。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，其结论依赖于所引用的原始研究，未提供新的实验数据或独立验证；对于不同干预策略的有效性和安全性比较缺乏直接的头对头证据；部分机制（如具体菌株与免疫细胞的精确分子通路）仍基于动物模型或小型临床试验，外推至所有实体瘤存在不确定性；摘要未交代具体的文献检索策略、纳入排除标准及质量评估方法。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::24a88f39680af325af37ed0e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在黑色素瘤患者中，接受抗PD-1治疗且肠道菌群中含有特定有益菌（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium）或具有高多样性的个体。\",\n          \"finding\": \"这些患者表现出更好的治疗反应和生存获益，机制涉及增强CD8+ T细胞活化、增加肿瘤浸润及促进Th1/Th17分化。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ee2882a0c098df37543578fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"肠道菌群失调（Dysbiosis），表现为有益菌减少、有害菌增多或多样性降低。\",\n          \"finding\": \"与抗PD-1治疗耐药相关，机制包括调节性T细胞（Tregs）扩增、髓源性抑制细胞（MDSCs）作用增强以及效应T细胞向肿瘤微环境的浸润减少。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fd1bd67acdf7b29fc150364f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用粪便微生物群移植（FMT）将健康供体菌群转移至对免疫治疗耐药的黑色素瘤患者。\",\n          \"finding\": \"Davari等人（2021）的研究显示，FMT可恢复有利的免疫环境，增强T细胞活化，使部分先前耐药的患者重新获得对PD-1阻断的反应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bff9fb7c91d662c3d780bc09\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"摄入富含纤维的饮食以支持短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）产生菌的生长。\",\n          \"finding\": \"SCFAs（如丁酸、丙酸、乙酸）可通过抑制组蛋白去乙酰化酶（HDACs）和促进抗炎信号通路，增强抗肿瘤免疫反应，改善抗PD-1疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a623e8c61ed512d650536c49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ab14efc6b30694f0585ce00\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管抗PD-1免疫疗法显著改善了黑色素瘤患者的生存率，但疗效存在高度异质性。本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物组如何调节这种疗效差异，阐明其背后的免疫学机制，并评估通过调节微生物组（如FMT、饮食、益生菌）来增强免疫治疗效果的潜在策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8628c3209fc51cc52f581364\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为黑色素瘤患者的肠道微生物组及其与抗PD-1免疫治疗的相互作用。情境涵盖从基础免疫机制（T细胞激活、代谢物作用）到临床干预策略（FMT、饮食、益生菌）的多个层面。范围主要聚焦于黑色素瘤，但也提及对其他癌症的潜在启示。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::683021d8eb786f400362468b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本综述旨在解决抗PD-1免疫疗法在黑色素瘤治疗中疗效变异性大的问题。文章首先介绍了肠道微生物组在维持免疫稳态和启动抗肿瘤免疫中的核心作用，详细阐述了微生物通过直接接触（如GALT中的抗原呈递）和间接代谢产物（如SCFAs）调节宿主免疫系统的机制。随后，文章总结了与良好治疗反应相关的微生物特征（如高多样性、特定菌属丰度）以及与耐药相关的菌群失调状态。最后，综述评估了三种主要的微生物组干预策略：FMT在逆转耐药方面的初步成功、高纤维饮食对SCFA产生的促进作用，以及益生菌使用的潜在益处与安全风险。文章指出，理解并操纵微生物组有望实现更个性化的癌症免疫治疗，但仍需更多临床研究来优化方案并确保安全性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a8323f303ecbdef63bd0e6a2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要基于黑色素瘤数据，其他实体瘤的直接证据较少；机制多为相关性或动物模型推断，临床因果链条尚不完全清晰；FMT等证据来自小规模研究。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组通过调节T细胞活化和肿瘤微环境来影响抗PD-1疗效的详细机制图谱，包括特定菌种、代谢物和免疫细胞亚群之间的相互作用。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::569a8cdab6e82079b6483367\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"主要关注黑色素瘤；未提供大规模多中心试验结果；不同干预策略的直接比较缺失。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"总结了目前可用的微生物组干预策略（FMT、饮食、益生菌）在增强ICIs疗效方面的临床前和早期临床证据，并指出了各自的潜在风险和局限性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::94575848cf3b0acc35c832ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"微生物组与免疫系统相互作用的总体描述，包括GALT的作用、T细胞亚群的分化（Th1, Th17, Tregs）以及SCFAs的免疫调节功能。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a954f5e86e5a0341d1cc7048\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0250\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"列举了与良好预后相关的特定菌种和代谢物，以及菌群失调导致的负面后果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::c7c67d13abcc3ba3a71d2af4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::657f67cade4ded2dd0f